#: source/advanced-topics/index.md:1
msgid ""
"This section lists advanced topics related to builds and builds performance"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md:1
msgid "Using the `eval-profiler`"
msgstr "使用 `eval-profiler`"

#: source/advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md:3
msgid ""
"Nix evaluator supports [evaluation](../language/evaluation.md) [profiling]"
"(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Profiling_(computer_programming)) compatible "
"with `flamegraph.pl`. The profiler samples the nix function call stack at "
"regular intervals. It can be enabled with the [`eval-profiler`](../command-"
"ref/conf-file.md#conf-eval-profiler) setting:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md:10
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-instantiate \"<nixpkgs>\" -A hello --eval-profiler flamegraph\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md:14
msgid ""
"Stack sampling frequency and the output file path can be configured with "
"[`eval-profile-file`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-eval-profile-file) "
"and [`eval-profiler-frequency`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-eval-"
"profiler-frequency). By default the collected profile is saved to "
"`nix.profile` file in the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md:19
msgid "The collected profile can be directly consumed by `flamegraph.pl`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md:25
msgid ""
"The line information in the profile contains the location of the [call site]"
"(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Call_site) position and the name of the "
"function being called (when available). For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/eval-profiler.md:33
msgid ""
"Here `import` primop is called at `/nix/store/"
"2q71fdvr4h33g9832hiriwnf20fn630l-source/pkgs/top-level/default.nix:167:5`."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:1
msgid "Remote Builds"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:3
msgid ""
"A local Nix installation can forward Nix builds to other machines, this "
"allows multiple builds to be performed in parallel."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:6
msgid ""
"Remote builds also allow Nix to perform multi-platform builds in a semi-"
"transparent way. For example, if you perform a build for a `aarch64-darwin` "
"on an `i686-linux` machine, Nix can automatically forward the build to a "
"`aarch64-darwin` machine, if one is available."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:11
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:13
msgid ""
"For a local machine to forward a build to a remote machine, the remote "
"machine must:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:15
msgid "Have Nix installed"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:16
msgid "Be running an SSH server, e.g. `sshd`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:17
msgid "Be accessible via SSH from the local machine over the network"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:18
msgid ""
"Have the local machine's public SSH key in `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys.d/"
"<username>`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:19
msgid ""
"Have the username of the SSH user in the `trusted-users` setting in "
"`nix.conf`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:21
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:23
msgid ""
"To test connecting to a remote [Nix instance](../glossary.md#gloss-nix-"
"instance) (in this case `mac`), run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:25
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"nix store info --store ssh://username@mac\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:29
msgid ""
"To specify an SSH identity file as part of the remote store URI add a query "
"parameter, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:32
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"nix store info --store ssh://username@mac?ssh-key=/home/alice/my-key\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:36
msgid ""
"Since builds should be non-interactive, the key should not have a "
"passphrase. Alternatively, you can load identities ahead of time into `ssh-"
"agent` or `gpg-agent`."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:40
msgid ""
"In a multi-user installation (default), builds are executed by the Nix "
"Daemon. The Nix Daemon cannot prompt for a passphrase via the terminal or "
"`ssh-agent`, so the SSH key must not have a passphrase."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:44
msgid ""
"In addition, the Nix Daemon's user (typically root) needs to have SSH access "
"to the remote builder."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:47
msgid ""
"Access can be verified by running `sudo su`, and then validating SSH access, "
"e.g. by running `ssh mac`. SSH identity files for root users are usually "
"stored in `/root/.ssh/` (Linux) or `/var/root/.ssh` (MacOS)."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:51
msgid "If you get the error"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:58
msgid ""
"then you need to ensure that the `PATH` of non-interactive login shells "
"contains Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:61
msgid ""
"The [list of remote build machines](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"builders) can be specified on the command line or in the Nix configuration "
"file. For example, the following command allows you to build a derivation "
"for `aarch64-darwin` on a Linux machine:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:72
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"nix build --impure \\\n"
" --expr '(with import <nixpkgs> { system = \"aarch64-darwin\"; }; runCommand "
"\"foo\" {} \"uname > $out\")' \\\n"
" --builders 'ssh://mac aarch64-darwin'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```console\n"
"nix build --impure \\\n"
" --expr '(with import <nixpkgs> { system = \"aarch64-darwin\"; }; runCommand "
"\"foo\" {} \"uname > $out\")' \\\n"
" --builders 'ssh://mac aarch64-darwin'\n"
"```"

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:78
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"[1/0/1 built, 0.0 MiB DL] building foo on ssh://mac\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:90
msgid ""
"It is possible to specify multiple build machines separated by a semicolon "
"or a newline, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:92
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"  --builders 'ssh://mac aarch64-darwin ; ssh://beastie x86_64-freebsd'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:96
msgid ""
"Remote build machines can also be configured in [`nix.conf`](../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md), e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:98
msgid ""
"    builders = ssh://mac aarch64-darwin ; ssh://beastie x86_64-freebsd\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:100
msgid ""
"After making changes to `nix.conf`, restart the Nix daemon for changes to "
"take effect."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:102
msgid ""
"Finally, remote build machines can be configured in a separate configuration "
"file included in `builders` via the syntax `@/path/to/file`. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/distributed-builds.md:107
msgid ""
"causes the list of machines in `/etc/nix/machines` to be included. (This is "
"the default.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/sharing-packages.md:1
msgid "Sharing Packages Between Machines"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/sharing-packages.md:3
msgid ""
"Sometimes you want to copy a package from one machine to another. Or, you "
"want to install some packages and you know that another machine already has "
"some or all of those packages or their dependencies. In that case there are "
"mechanisms to quickly copy packages between machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:1
msgid "Serving a Nix store via HTTP"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:3
msgid ""
"You can easily share the Nix store of a machine via HTTP. This allows other "
"machines to fetch store paths from that machine to speed up installations. "
"It uses the same _binary cache_ mechanism that Nix usually uses to fetch pre-"
"built binaries from <https://cache.nixos.org>."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:8
msgid ""
"The daemon that handles binary cache requests via HTTP, `nix-serve`, is not "
"part of the Nix distribution, but you can install it from Nixpkgs:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:15
msgid ""
"You can then start the server, listening for HTTP connections on whatever "
"port you like:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:22
msgid ""
"To check whether it works, try fetching the [`nix-cache-info`](../protocols/"
"binary-cache/nix-cache-info.md) file on the client:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:24
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ curl http://avalon:8080/nix-cache-info\n"
"StoreDir: /nix/store\n"
"WantMassQuery: 1\n"
"Priority: 30\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:31
msgid ""
"When writing to a binary cache (e.g., with [`nix copy`](../command-ref/new-"
"cli/nix3-copy.md)), Nix creates [`nix-cache-info`](../protocols/binary-cache/"
"nix-cache-info.md) automatically if it doesn't exist."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:33
msgid ""
"On the client side, you can tell Nix to use your binary cache using `--"
"substituters`, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:36
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-env --install --attr nixpkgs.firefox --substituters http://"
"avalon:8080/\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:40
msgid ""
"The option `substituters` tells Nix to use this binary cache in addition to "
"your default caches, such as <https://cache.nixos.org>. Thus, for any path "
"in the closure of Firefox, Nix will first check if the path is available on "
"the server `avalon` or another binary caches. If not, it will fall back to "
"building from source."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:46
msgid ""
"You can also tell Nix to always use your binary cache by adding a line to "
"the `nix.conf` configuration file like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:49
msgid ""
"    substituters = http://avalon:8080/ https://cache.nixos.org/\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:1
msgid "Serving a Nix store via SSH"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:3
msgid ""
"You can tell Nix to automatically fetch needed binaries from a remote Nix "
"store via SSH. For example, the following installs Firefox, automatically "
"fetching any store paths in Firefox’s closure if they are available on the "
"server `avalon`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:8
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-env --install --attr nixpkgs.firefox --substituters ssh://"
"alice@avalon\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:12
msgid ""
"This works similar to the binary cache substituter that Nix usually uses, "
"only using SSH instead of HTTP: if a store path `P` is needed, Nix will "
"first check if it’s available in the Nix store on `avalon`. If not, it will "
"fall back to using the binary cache substituter, and then to building from "
"source."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:18
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:20
msgid ""
"The SSH substituter currently does not allow you to enter an SSH passphrase "
"interactively. Therefore, you should use `ssh-add` to load the decrypted "
"private key into `ssh-agent`."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:24
msgid ""
"You can also copy the closure of some store path, without installing it into "
"your profile, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:27
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-store --realise /nix/store/m85bxg…-firefox-34.0.5 --substituters\n"
"ssh://alice@avalon\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:32
msgid "This is essentially equivalent to doing"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:39
msgid ""
"You can use SSH’s _forced command_ feature to set up a restricted user "
"account for SSH substituter access, allowing read-only access to the local "
"Nix store, but nothing more. For example, add the following lines to "
"`sshd_config` to restrict the user `nix-ssh`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:53
msgid ""
"On NixOS, you can accomplish the same by adding the following to your "
"`configuration.nix`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:56
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"nix.sshServe.enable = true;\n"
"nix.sshServe.keys = [ \"ssh-dss AAAAB3NzaC1k... bob@example.org\" ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/ssh-substituter.md:61
msgid ""
"where the latter line lists the public keys of users that are allowed to "
"connect."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:1
msgid "Tuning Cores and Jobs"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:3
msgid ""
"Nix has two relevant settings with regards to how your CPU cores will be "
"utilized: `cores` and `max-jobs`. This chapter will talk about what they "
"are, how they interact, and their configuration trade-offs."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:7
msgid ""
"`max-jobs`  \n"
"Dictates how many separate derivations will be built at the same time. If "
"you set this to zero, the local machine will do no builds.  Nix will still "
"substitute from binary caches, and build remotely if remote builders are "
"configured."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:13
msgid ""
"`cores`  \n"
"Suggests how many cores each derivation should use. Similar to `make -j`."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:17
msgid ""
"The `cores` setting determines the value of `NIX_BUILD_CORES`. "
"`NIX_BUILD_CORES` is equal to `cores`, unless `cores` equals `0`, in which "
"case `NIX_BUILD_CORES` will be the total number of cores in the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:22
msgid ""
"The maximum number of consumed cores is a simple multiplication, `max-jobs` "
"\\* `NIX_BUILD_CORES`."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:25
msgid ""
"The balance on how to set these two independent variables depends upon each "
"builder's workload and hardware. Here are a few example scenarios on a "
"machine with 24 cores:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:29
msgid "`max-jobs`"
msgstr "`max-jobs`"

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:29
msgid "`cores`"
msgstr "`cores`"

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:29
msgid "`NIX_BUILD_CORES`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:29
msgid "Maximum Processes"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:29
msgid "Result"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:31
#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:34
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:31
#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:32
#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:34
#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:35
msgid "24"
msgstr "24"

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:31
msgid ""
"One derivation will be built at a time, each one can use 24 cores. Undersold "
"if a job can’t use 24 cores."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:32
msgid "4"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:32
#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:33
msgid "6"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:32
msgid "Four derivations will be built at once, each given access to six cores."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:33
msgid "12"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:33
msgid "72"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:33
msgid ""
"12 derivations will be built at once, each given access to six cores. This "
"configuration is over-sold. If all 12 derivations being built simultaneously "
"try to use all six cores, the machine's performance will be degraded due to "
"extensive context switching between the 12 builds."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:34
msgid ""
"24 derivations can build at the same time, each using a single core. Never "
"oversold, but derivations which require many cores will be very slow to "
"compile."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:35
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:35
msgid "576"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:35
msgid ""
"24 derivations can build at the same time, each using all the available "
"cores of the machine. Very likely to be oversold, and very likely to suffer "
"context switches."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/cores-vs-jobs.md:37
msgid ""
"It is up to the derivations' build script to respect host's requested cores-"
"per-build by following the value of the `NIX_BUILD_CORES` environment "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:1
msgid "Using the `post-build-hook`"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:3
msgid "Implementation Caveats"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:5
msgid ""
"Here we use the post-build hook to upload to a binary cache. This is a "
"simple and working example, but it is not suitable for all use cases."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:8
msgid ""
"The post build hook program runs after each executed build, and blocks the "
"build loop. The build loop exits if the hook program fails."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:11
msgid ""
"Concretely, this implementation will make Nix slow or unusable when the "
"internet is slow or unreliable."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:14
msgid ""
"A more advanced implementation might pass the store paths to a user-supplied "
"daemon or queue for processing the store paths outside of the build loop."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:18
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:20
msgid ""
"This tutorial assumes you have configured an [S3-compatible binary cache](../"
"command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md#s3-binary-cache-store) as a "
"[substituter](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-substituters), and that the "
"`root` user's default AWS profile can upload to the bucket."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:23
msgid "Set up a Signing Key"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:25
msgid ""
"Use `nix-store --generate-binary-cache-key` to create our public and private "
"signing keys. We will sign paths with the private key, and distribute the "
"public key for verifying the authenticity of the paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:35
msgid ""
"Then update [`nix.conf`](../command-ref/conf-file.md) on any machine that "
"will access the cache. Add the cache URL to [`substituters`](../command-ref/"
"conf-file.md#conf-substituters) and the public key to [`trusted-public-keys`]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys):"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:38
msgid ""
"    substituters = https://cache.nixos.org/ s3://example-nix-cache\n"
"    trusted-public-keys = "
"cache.nixos.org-1:6NCHdD59X431o0gWypbMrAURkbJ16ZPMQFGspcDShjY= example-nix-"
"cache-1:1/cKDz3QCCOmwcztD2eV6Coggp6rqc9DGjWv7C0G+rM=\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:41
msgid ""
"Machines that build for the cache must sign derivations using the private "
"key. On those machines, add the path to the key file to the [`secret-key-"
"files`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-secret-key-files) field in their "
"[`nix.conf`](../command-ref/conf-file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:46
msgid "We will restart the Nix daemon in a later step."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:48
msgid "Implementing the build hook"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:50
msgid "Write the following script to `/etc/nix/upload-to-cache.sh`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:53
msgid "#!/bin/sh\n"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:56
msgid "# disable globbing\n"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:57
msgid "' '"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:59
msgid "\"Uploading paths\""
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:60
msgid "\"s3://example-nix-cache\""
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:65
msgid ""
"The `$OUT_PATHS` variable is a space-separated list of Nix store paths. In "
"this case, we expect and want the shell to perform word splitting to make "
"each output path its own argument to `nix store sign`. Nix guarantees the "
"paths will not contain any spaces, however a store path might contain glob "
"characters. The `set -f` disables globbing in the shell. If you want to "
"upload the `.drv` file too, the `$DRV_PATH` variable is also defined for the "
"script and works just like `$OUT_PATHS`."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:74
msgid "Then make sure the hook program is executable by the `root` user:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:80
msgid "Updating Nix Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:82
msgid ""
"Edit `/etc/nix/nix.conf` to run our hook, by adding the following "
"configuration snippet at the end:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:87
msgid "Then, restart the `nix-daemon`."
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:91
msgid "Build any derivation, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/advanced-topics/post-build-hook.md:93
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-build --expr '(import <nixpkgs> {}).writeText \"example\" "
"(builtins.toString builtins.currentTime)'\n"
"this derivation will be built:\n"
"  /nix/store/s4pnfbkalzy5qz57qs6yybna8wylkig6-example.drv\n"
"building '/nix/store/s4pnfbkalzy5qz57qs6yybna8wylkig6-example.drv'...\n"
"running post-build-hook '/home/grahamc/projects/github.com/NixOS/nix/post-"
"hook.sh'...\n"
"post-build-hook: Signing paths /nix/store/ibcyipq5gf91838ldx40mjsp0b8w9n18-"
"example\n"
"post-build-hook: Uploading paths /nix/store/ibcyipq5gf91838ldx40mjsp0b8w9n18-"
"example\n"
"/nix/store/ibcyipq5gf91838ldx40mjsp0b8w9n18-example\n"
