#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:128
msgid "Path-like syntax"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:130
msgid ""
"Flakes corresponding to a local path can also be referred to by a direct "
"path reference, either `/absolute/path/to/the/flake` or`./relative/path/to/"
"the/flake`. Note that the leading `./` is mandatory for relative paths. If "
"it is omitted, the path will be interpreted as [URL-like syntax](#url-like-"
"syntax), which will cause error messages like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:140
msgid "The semantic of such a path is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:142
msgid ""
"If the directory is part of a Git repository, then the input will be treated "
"as a `git+file:` URL, otherwise it will be treated as a `path:` url;"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:143
msgid ""
"If the directory doesn't contain a `flake.nix` file, then Nix will search "
"for such a file upwards in the file system hierarchy until it finds any of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:144
msgid "The Git repository root, or"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:145
msgid "The filesystem root (/), or"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:146
msgid "A folder on a different mount point."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:148
msgid ""
"Contrary to URL-like references, path-like flake references can contain "
"arbitrary unicode characters (except `#` and `?`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:152
msgid "`.`: The flake to which the current directory belongs."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:153
msgid "`/home/alice/src/patchelf`: A flake in some other directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:154
msgid ""
"`./../sub directory/with Ûñî©ôδ€`: A flake in another relative directory "
"that has Unicode characters in its name."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:157
msgid "Flake reference attributes"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:159
msgid "The following generic flake reference attributes are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:161
msgid ""
"`dir`: The subdirectory of the flake in which `flake.nix` is located. This "
"parameter enables having multiple flakes in a repository or tarball. The "
"default is the root directory of the flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:166
msgid ""
"`narHash`: The hash of the [Nix Archive (NAR) serialisation](../../store/"
"file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) (in [SRI](../../"
"glossary.md#gloss-sri) format) of the contents of the flake. This is useful "
"for flake types such as tarballs that lack a unique content identifier such "
"as a Git commit hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:173
msgid ""
"In addition, the following attributes are common to several flake reference "
"types:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:176
msgid "`rev`: A Git or Mercurial commit hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:178
msgid "`ref`: A Git or Mercurial branch or tag name."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:180
msgid ""
"Finally, some attributes are typically not specified by the user, but can "
"occur in _locked_ flake references and are available to Nix code:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:183
msgid "`revCount`: The number of ancestors of the commit `rev`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:185
msgid ""
"`lastModified`: The timestamp (in seconds since the Unix epoch) of the last "
"modification of this version of the flake. For Git/Mercurial flakes, this is "
"the commit time of commit _rev_, while for tarball flakes, it's the most "
"recent timestamp of any file inside the tarball."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:191
msgid "Types"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:193
msgid "Currently the `type` attribute can be one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:195
msgid ""
"`indirect`: _The default_. These are symbolic references to flakes that are "
"looked up in [the flake registries](./nix3-registry.md). These have the form"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:203
msgid ""
"These perform a lookup of `<flake-id>` in the flake registry. For example, "
"`nixpkgs` and `nixpkgs/release-20.09` are indirect flake references. The "
"specified `rev` and/or `ref` are merged with the entry in the registry; see "
"[nix registry](./nix3-registry.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:209
msgid "For example, these are valid indirect flake references:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:211
msgid "`nixpkgs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:212
msgid "`nixpkgs/nixos-unstable`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:213
msgid "`nixpkgs/a3a3dda3bacf61e8a39258a0ed9c924eeca8e293`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:214
msgid "`nixpkgs/nixos-unstable/a3a3dda3bacf61e8a39258a0ed9c924eeca8e293`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:215
msgid "`sub/dir` (if a flake named `sub` is in the registry)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:217
msgid ""
"<a id=\"path-fetcher\"></a>`path`: arbitrary local directories. The required "
"attribute `path` specifies the path of the flake. The URL form is"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:224
msgid ""
"where _path_ is an absolute path to a directory in the file system "
"containing a file named `flake.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:227
msgid ""
"If the flake at _path_ is not inside a git repository, the `path:` prefix is "
"implied and can be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:230
msgid ""
"If _path_ is a relative path (i.e. if it does not start with `/`), it is "
"interpreted as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:233
msgid ""
"If _path_ is a command line argument, it is interpreted relative to the "
"current directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:236
msgid ""
"If _path_ is used in a `flake.nix`, it is interpreted relative to the "
"directory containing that `flake.nix`. However, the resolved path must be in "
"the same tree. For instance, a `flake.nix` in the root of a tree can use "
"`path:./foo` to access the flake in subdirectory `foo`, but `path:../bar` is "
"illegal. On the other hand, a flake in the `/foo` directory of a tree can "
"use `path:../bar` to refer to the flake in `/bar`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:244
msgid ""
"Path inputs can be specified with path values in `flake.nix`. Path values "
"are a syntax for `path` inputs, and they are converted by"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:245
msgid ""
"resolving them into relative paths, relative to the base directory of "
"`flake.nix`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:246
msgid "escaping URL characters (refer to IETF RFC?)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:247
msgid "prepending `path:`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:249
msgid ""
"Note that the allowed syntax for path values in flake `inputs` may be more "
"restrictive than general Nix, so you may need to use `path:` if your path "
"contains certain special characters. See [Path literals](../../language/"
"syntax.md#path-literal)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:251
msgid ""
"Note that if you omit `path:`, relative paths must start with `.` to avoid "
"ambiguity with registry lookups (e.g. `nixpkgs` is a registry lookup; `./"
"nixpkgs` is a relative path)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:255
msgid "For example, these are valid path flake references:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:257
msgid "`path:/home/user/sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:258
msgid "`/home/user/sub/dir` (if `dir/flake.nix` is _not_ in a git repository)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:259
msgid "`path:sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:260
msgid "`./sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:261
msgid "`path:../parent`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:263
msgid ""
"`git`: Git repositories. The location of the repository is specified by the "
"attribute `url`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:266
msgid "They have the URL form"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:268
msgid ""
"```\n"
"git(+http|+https|+ssh|+git|+file):(//<server>)?<path>(\\?<params>)?\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:272
msgid ""
"If _path_ starts with `/` (or `./` when used as an argument on the command "
"line) and is a local path to a git repository, the leading `git:` or `+file` "
"prefixes are implied and can be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:276
msgid "The `ref` attribute defaults to resolving the `HEAD` reference."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:278
msgid ""
"The `rev` attribute must denote a commit that exists in the branch or tag "
"specified by the `ref` attribute, since Nix doesn't do a full clone of the "
"remote repository by default (and the Git protocol doesn't allow fetching a "
"`rev` without a known `ref`). The default is the commit currently pointed to "
"by `ref`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:284
msgid ""
"When `git+file` is used without specifying `ref` or `rev`, files are fetched "
"directly from the local `path` as long as they have been added to the Git "
"repository. If there are uncommitted changes, the reference is treated as "
"dirty and a warning is printed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:289
msgid "For example, the following are valid Git flake references:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:291
msgid "`git:/home/user/sub/dir`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:292
msgid "`/home/user/sub/dir` (if `dir/flake.nix` is in a git repository)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:293
msgid ""
"`./sub/dir` (when used on the command line and `dir/flake.nix` is in a git "
"repository)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:294
msgid "`git+https://example.org/my/repo`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:295
msgid "`git+https://example.org/my/repo?dir=flake1`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:296
msgid ""
"`git+https://example.org/my/repo?shallow=1` A shallow clone of the "
"repository. For large repositories, the shallow clone option can "
"significantly speed up fresh clones compared to non-shallow clones, while "
"still providing faster updates than other fetch methods such as `tarball:` "
"or `github:`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:299
msgid "`git+ssh://git@github.com/NixOS/nix?ref=v1.2.3`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:300
msgid ""
"`git://github.com/edolstra/dwarffs?"
"ref=unstable&rev=e486d8d40e626a20e06d792db8cc5ac5aba9a5b4`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:301
msgid "`git+file:///home/my-user/some-repo/some-repo`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:303
msgid ""
"`mercurial`: Mercurial repositories. The URL form is similar to the `git` "
"type, except that the URL schema must be one of `hg+http`, `hg+https`, "
"`hg+ssh` or `hg+file`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:307
msgid ""
"`tarball`: Tarballs. The location of the tarball is specified by the "
"attribute `url`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:310
msgid ""
"In URL form, the schema must be `tarball+http://`, `tarball+https://` or "
"`tarball+file://`. If the extension corresponds to a known archive format "
"(`.zip`, `.tar`, `.tgz`, `.tar.gz`, `.tar.xz`, `.tar.bz2` or `.tar.zst`), "
"then the `tarball+` can be dropped."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:315
msgid ""
"This can also be used to set the location of gitea/forgejo branches. [See "
"here](../../protocols/tarball-fetcher.md#gitea-and-forgejo-support)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:317
msgid ""
"`file`: Plain files or directory tarballs, either over http(s) or from the "
"local disk."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:320
msgid ""
"In URL form, the schema must be `file+http://`, `file+https://` or "
"`file+file://`. If the extension doesn’t correspond to a known archive "
"format (as defined by the `tarball` fetcher), then the `file+` prefix can be "
"dropped."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:324
msgid ""
"`github`: A more efficient way to fetch repositories from GitHub. The "
"following attributes are required:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:327
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:360
msgid "`owner`: The owner of the repository."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:329
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:362
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:393
msgid "`repo`: The name of the repository."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:331
msgid ""
"These are downloaded as tarball archives, rather than through Git. This is "
"often much faster and uses less disk space since it doesn't require fetching "
"the entire history of the repository. On the other hand, it doesn't allow "
"incremental fetching (but full downloads are often faster than incremental "
"fetches!)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:337
msgid "The URL syntax for `github` flakes is:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:343
msgid ""
"`<rev-or-ref>` specifies the name of a branch or tag (`ref`), or a commit "
"hash (`rev`). Note that unlike Git, GitHub allows fetching by commit hash "
"without specifying a branch or tag."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:347
msgid ""
"You can also specify `host` as a parameter, to point to a custom GitHub "
"Enterprise server."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:350
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:376
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:412
msgid "Some examples:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:352
msgid "`github:edolstra/dwarffs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:353
msgid "`github:edolstra/dwarffs/unstable`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:354
msgid "`github:edolstra/dwarffs/d3f2baba8f425779026c6ec04021b2e927f61e31`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:355
msgid "`github:internal/project?host=company-github.example.org`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:357
msgid ""
"`gitlab`: Similar to `github`, is a more efficient way to fetch GitLab "
"repositories. The following attributes are required:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:364
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:395
msgid "Like `github`, these are downloaded as tarball archives."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:366
msgid "The URL syntax for `gitlab` flakes is:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:368
msgid "`gitlab:<owner>/<repo>(/<rev-or-ref>)?(\\?<params>)?`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:370
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:401
msgid ""
"`<rev-or-ref>` works the same as `github`. Either a branch or tag name "
"(`ref`), or a commit hash (`rev`) can be specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:373
msgid ""
"Since GitLab allows for self-hosting, you can specify `host` as a parameter, "
"to point to any instances other than `gitlab.com`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:378
msgid "`gitlab:veloren/veloren`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:379
msgid "`gitlab:veloren/veloren/master`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:380
msgid "`gitlab:veloren/veloren/80a4d7f13492d916e47d6195be23acae8001985a`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:381
msgid "`gitlab:openldap/openldap?host=git.openldap.org`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:383
msgid ""
"When accessing a project in a (nested) subgroup, make sure to URL-encode any "
"slashes, i.e. replace `/` with `%2F`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:386
msgid "`gitlab:veloren%2Fdev/rfcs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:388
msgid ""
"`sourcehut`: Similar to `github`, is a more efficient way to fetch SourceHut "
"repositories. The following attributes are required:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:391
msgid "`owner`: The owner of the repository (including leading `~`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:397
msgid "The URL syntax for `sourcehut` flakes is:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:399
msgid "`sourcehut:<owner>/<repo>(/<rev-or-ref>)?(\\?<params>)?`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:404
msgid ""
"Since SourceHut allows for self-hosting, you can specify `host` as a "
"parameter, to point to any instances other than `git.sr.ht`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:407
msgid ""
"Currently, `ref` name resolution only works for Git repositories. You can "
"refer to Mercurial repositories by simply changing `host` to `hg.sr.ht` (or "
"any other Mercurial instance). With the caveat that you must explicitly "
"specify a commit hash (`rev`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:414
msgid "`sourcehut:~misterio/nix-colors`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:415
msgid "`sourcehut:~misterio/nix-colors/main`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:416
msgid "`sourcehut:~misterio/nix-colors?host=git.example.org`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:417
msgid ""
"`sourcehut:~misterio/nix-colors/182b4b8709b8ffe4e9774a4c5d6877bf6bb9a21c`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:418
msgid ""
"`sourcehut:~misterio/nix-colors/21c1a380a6915d890d408e9f22203436a35bb2de?"
"host=hg.sr.ht`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:420
msgid "Flake format"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:422
msgid ""
"As an example, here is a simple `flake.nix` that depends on the Nixpkgs "
"flake and provides a single package (i.e. an [installable](./"
"nix.md#installables) derivation):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:426
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{\n"
"  description = \"A flake for building Hello World\";\n"
"\n"
"  inputs.nixpkgs.url = \"github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-20.03\";\n"
"\n"
"  outputs = { self, nixpkgs }: {\n"
"\n"
"    packages.x86_64-linux.default =\n"
"      # Notice the reference to nixpkgs here.\n"
"      with import nixpkgs { system = \"x86_64-linux\"; };\n"
"      stdenv.mkDerivation {\n"
"        name = \"hello\";\n"
"        src = self;\n"
"        buildPhase = \"gcc -o hello ./hello.c\";\n"
"        installPhase = \"mkdir -p $out/bin; install -t $out/bin hello\";\n"
"      };\n"
"\n"
"  };\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:448
msgid "The following attributes are supported in `flake.nix`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:450
msgid "`description`: A short, one-line description of the flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:452
msgid ""
"`inputs`: An attrset specifying the dependencies of the flake (described "
"below)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:455
msgid ""
"`outputs`: A function that, given an attribute set containing the outputs of "
"each of the input flakes keyed by their identifier, yields the Nix values "
"provided by this flake. Thus, in the example above, `inputs.nixpkgs` "
"contains the result of the call to the `outputs` function of the `nixpkgs` "
"flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:461
msgid ""
"In addition to the outputs of each input, each input in `inputs` also "
"contains some metadata about the inputs. These are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:464
msgid ""
"`outPath`: The path in the Nix store of the flake's source tree. This way, "
"the attribute set can be passed to `import` as if it was a path, as in the "
"example above (`import nixpkgs`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:468
msgid "`rev`: The commit hash of the flake's repository, if applicable."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:470
msgid ""
"`revCount`: The number of ancestors of the revision `rev`. This is not "
"available for `github` repositories, since they're fetched as tarballs "
"rather than as Git repositories."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:474
msgid ""
"`lastModifiedDate`: The commit time of the revision `rev`, in the format "
"`%Y%m%d%H%M%S` (e.g. `20181231100934`). Unlike `revCount`, this is available "
"for both Git and GitHub repositories, so it's useful for generating "
"(hopefully) monotonically increasing version strings."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:480
msgid ""
"`lastModified`: The commit time of the revision `rev` as an integer denoting "
"the number of seconds since 1970."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:483
msgid ""
"`narHash`: The SHA-256 (in [SRI](../../glossary.md#gloss-sri) format) of the "
"[Nix Archive (NAR) serialisation](../../store/file-system-object/content-"
"address.md#serial-nix-archive) NAR serialization of the flake's source tree."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:487
msgid ""
"The value returned by the `outputs` function must be an attribute set. The "
"attributes can have arbitrary values; however, various `nix` subcommands "
"require specific attributes to have a specific value (e.g. `packages.x86_64-"
"linux` must be an attribute set of derivations built for the `x86_64-linux` "
"platform)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:493
msgid ""
"`nixConfig`: a set of `nix.conf` options to be set when evaluating any part "
"of a flake. In the interests of security, only a small set of set of options "
"is allowed to be set without confirmation so long as [`accept-flake-config`]"
"(../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-accept-flake-config) is not enabled in "
"the global configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:496
msgid "[`bash-prompt`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-bash-prompt)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:497
msgid ""
"[`bash-prompt-prefix`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-bash-prompt-"
"prefix)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:498
msgid ""
"[`bash-prompt-suffix`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-bash-prompt-"
"suffix)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:499
msgid "[`flake-registry`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-flake-registry)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:500
msgid ""
"[`commit-lock-file-summary`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-commit-lock-"
"file-summary)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:502
msgid "Flake inputs"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:504
msgid ""
"The attribute `inputs` specifies the dependencies of a flake, as an attrset "
"mapping input names to flake references. For example, the following "
"specifies a dependency on the `nixpkgs` and `import-cargo` repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:509
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"# A GitHub repository.\n"
"inputs.import-cargo = {\n"
"  type = \"github\";\n"
"  owner = \"edolstra\";\n"
"  repo = \"import-cargo\";\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"# An indirection through the flake registry.\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs = {\n"
"  type = \"indirect\";\n"
"  id = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:524
msgid "Alternatively, you can use the URL-like syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:526
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.import-cargo.url = \"github:edolstra/import-cargo\";\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs.url = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:531
msgid ""
"Each input is fetched, evaluated and passed to the `outputs` function as a "
"set of attributes with the same name as the corresponding input. The special "
"input named `self` refers to the outputs and source tree of _this_ flake. "
"Thus, a typical `outputs` function looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:543
msgid ""
"It is also possible to omit an input entirely and _only_ list it as expected "
"function argument to `outputs`. Thus,"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:550
msgid "without an `inputs.nixpkgs` attribute is equivalent to"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:552
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs = {\n"
"  type = \"indirect\";\n"
"  id = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:559
msgid ""
"Repositories that don't contain a `flake.nix` can also be used as inputs, by "
"setting the input's `flake` attribute to `false`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:562
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.grcov = {\n"
"  type = \"github\";\n"
"  owner = \"mozilla\";\n"
"  repo = \"grcov\";\n"
"  flake = false;\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"outputs = { self, nixpkgs, grcov }: {\n"
"  packages.x86_64-linux.grcov = stdenv.mkDerivation {\n"
"    src = grcov;\n"
"    ...\n"
"  };\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:578
msgid ""
"Transitive inputs can be overridden from a `flake.nix` file. For example, "
"the following overrides the `nixpkgs` input of the `nixops` input:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:582
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixops.inputs.nixpkgs = {\n"
"  type = \"github\";\n"
"  owner = \"my-org\";\n"
"  repo = \"nixpkgs\";\n"
"};\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:590
msgid ""
"It is also possible to \"inherit\" an input from another input. This is "
"useful to minimize flake dependencies. For example, the following sets the "
"`nixpkgs` input of the top-level flake to be equal to the `nixpkgs` input of "
"the `dwarffs` input of the top-level flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:595
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixpkgs.follows = \"dwarffs/nixpkgs\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:599
msgid ""
"The value of the `follows` attribute is a `/`\\-separated sequence of input "
"names denoting the path of inputs to be followed from the root flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:603
msgid "Self-attributes"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:605
msgid ""
"Flakes can declare attributes about themselves that affect how they are "
"fetched. These attributes are specified using the special `self` input and "
"are retroactively applied to it:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:616
msgid "The following self-attributes are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:618
msgid ""
"`submodules`: A Boolean denoting whether Git submodules should be fetched "
"when this flake is used as an input. When set to `true`, Git submodules will "
"be automatically fetched without requiring callers to specify `submodules=1` "
"in the flake reference URL. Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:620
msgid ""
"`lfs`: A Boolean denoting whether Git LFS (Large File Storage) files should "
"be fetched when this flake is used as an input. When set to `true`, Git LFS "
"files will be automatically fetched. Defaults to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:622
msgid ""
"These self-attributes eliminate the need for consumers of your flake to "
"manually specify fetching options in their flake references."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:624
msgid "Overrides and `follows` can be combined, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:626
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"inputs.nixops.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = \"dwarffs/nixpkgs\";\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:630
msgid ""
"sets the `nixpkgs` input of `nixops` to be the same as the `nixpkgs` input "
"of `dwarffs`. It is worth noting, however, that it is generally not useful "
"to eliminate transitive `nixpkgs` flake inputs in this way. Most flakes "
"provide their functionality through Nixpkgs overlays or NixOS modules, which "
"are composed into the top-level flake's `nixpkgs` input; so their own "
"`nixpkgs` input is usually irrelevant."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:637
msgid "Lock files"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:639
msgid ""
"Inputs specified in `flake.nix` are typically \"unlocked\" in the sense that "
"they don't specify an exact revision. To ensure reproducibility, Nix will "
"automatically generate and use a _lock file_ called `flake.lock` in the "
"flake's directory. The lock file is a UTF-8 JSON file. It contains a graph "
"structure isomorphic to the graph of dependencies of the root flake. Each "
"node in the graph (except the root node) maps the (usually) unlocked input "
"specifications in `flake.nix` to locked input specifications. Each node also "
"contains some metadata, such as the dependencies (outgoing edges) of the "
"node."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:650
msgid ""
"For example, if `flake.nix` has the inputs in the example above, then the "
"resulting lock file might be:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:655
msgid "\"version\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:656
msgid "\"root\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:656
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:658
msgid "\"n1\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:657
msgid "\"nodes\""
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:659
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:666
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:681
#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md:697
