#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:3
msgid "`nix-build` - build a Nix expression"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-build` \\[_paths…_\\] \\[`--arg` _name_ _value_\\] \\[`--argstr` _name_ "
"_value_\\] \\[{`--attr` | `-A`} _attrPath_\\] \\[`--no-out-link`\\] \\[`--"
"dry-run`\\] \\[{`--out-link` | `-o`} _outlink_\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:15
msgid "Disambiguation"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:17
msgid ""
"This man page describes the command `nix-build`, which is distinct from `nix "
"build`. For documentation on the latter, run `nix build --help` or see `man "
"nix3-build`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:23
msgid ""
"The `nix-build` command builds the derivations described by the Nix "
"expressions in _paths_. If the build succeeds, it places a symlink to the "
"result in the current directory. The symlink is called `result`. If there "
"are multiple Nix expressions, or the Nix expressions evaluate to multiple "
"derivations, multiple sequentially numbered symlinks are created (`result`, "
"`result-2`, and so on)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:30
msgid ""
"If no _paths_ are specified, then `nix-build` will use `default.nix` in the "
"current directory, if it exists."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:33
msgid ""
"If an element of _paths_ starts with `http://` or `https://`, it is "
"interpreted as the URL of a tarball that will be downloaded and unpacked to "
"a temporary location. The tarball must include a single top-level directory "
"containing at least a file named `default.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:38
msgid ""
"`nix-build` is essentially a wrapper around [`nix-instantiate`](./nix-"
"instantiate.md) (to translate a high-level Nix expression to a low-level "
"[store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)) and [`nix-store --"
"realise`](../command-ref/nix-store/realise.md) (to build the store "
"derivation)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:48
msgid ""
"The result of the build is automatically registered as a root of the Nix "
"garbage collector. This root disappears automatically when the `result` "
"symlink is deleted or renamed. So don’t rename the symlink."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:54
msgid ""
"All options not listed here are passed to [`nix-store --realise`](./nix-"
"store/realise.md), except for `--arg` and `--attr` / `-A` which are passed "
"to [`nix-instantiate`](./nix-instantiate.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:58
msgid "<span id=\"opt-no-out-link\">[`--no-out-link`](#opt-no-out-link)<span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:60
msgid ""
"Do not create a symlink to the output path. Note that as a result the output "
"does not become a root of the garbage collector, and so might be deleted by "
"`nix-store --gc`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-build.md:66
msgid "Show what store paths would be built or downloaded."
msgstr ""

