"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:3
msgid "`nix-env --delete-generations` - delete profile generations"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:7
msgid "`nix-env` `--delete-generations` _generations_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:11
msgid ""
"This operation deletes the specified generations of the current profile."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:13
msgid "_generations_ can be a one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:15
msgid "<span id=\"generations-list\">[`<number>...`](#generations-list)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:17
msgid ""
"A list of generation numbers, each one a separate command-line argument."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:19
msgid ""
"Delete exactly the profile generations given by their generation number. "
"Deleting the current generation is not allowed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:22
msgid ""
"<span id=\"generations-old\">[The special value `old`](#generations-old)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:24
msgid "Delete all generations except the current one."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:26
msgid "**WARNING**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:28
msgid "Older _and newer_ generations will be deleted by this operation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:30
msgid ""
"One might expect this to just delete older generations than the current one, "
"but that is only true if the current generation is also the latest. Because "
"one can roll back to a previous generation, it is possible to have "
"generations newer than the current one. They will also be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:34
msgid "<span id=\"generations-time\">[`<number>d`](#generations-time)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:36
msgid "The last _number_ days"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:38
msgid "_Example_: `30d`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:40
msgid ""
"Delete all generations created more than _number_ days ago, except the most "
"recent one of them. This allows rolling back to generations that were "
"available within the specified period."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:43
msgid "<span id=\"generations-count\">[`+<number>`](#generations-count)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:45
msgid "The last _number_ generations up to the present"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:47
msgid "_Example_: `+5`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:49
msgid "Keep the last _number_ generations, along with any newer than current."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:51
msgid ""
"Periodically deleting old generations is important to make garbage "
"collection effective. The is because profiles are also garbage collection "
"roots — any [store object](../../store/store-object.md) reachable from a "
"profile is \"alive\" and ineligible for deletion."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:59
msgid ""
"The following options are allowed for all `nix-env` operations, but may not "
"always have an effect."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:61
msgid "`--file` / `-f` _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:63
msgid ""
"Specifies the Nix expression (designated below as the _active Nix "
"expression_) used by the `--install`, `--upgrade`, and `--query --available` "
"operations to obtain derivations. The default is `~/.nix-defexpr`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:68
msgid ""
"If the argument starts with `http://` or `https://`, it is interpreted as "
"the URL of a tarball that will be downloaded and unpacked to a temporary "
"location. The tarball must include a single top-level directory containing "
"at least a file named `default.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:73
msgid "`--profile` / `-p` _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:75
msgid ""
"Specifies the profile to be used by those operations that operate on a "
"profile (designated below as the _active profile_). A profile is a sequence "
"of user environments called _generations_, one of which is the _current "
"generation_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:80
msgid "`--dry-run`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:82
msgid ""
"For the `--install`, `--upgrade`, `--uninstall`, `--switch-generation`, `--"
"delete-generations` and `--rollback` operations, this flag will cause `nix-"
"env` to print what _would_ be done if this flag had not been specified, "
"without actually doing it."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:87
msgid ""
"`--dry-run` also prints out which paths will be [substituted](../../"
"glossary.md) (i.e., downloaded) and which paths will be built from source "
"(because no substitute is available)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:91
msgid "`--system-filter` _system_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:93
msgid ""
"By default, operations such as `--query --available` show derivations "
"matching any platform. This option allows you to use derivations for the "
"specified platform _system_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:113
msgid ""
"For machine-readable output, including versions of the libraries Nix links "
"against, see the [`nix version`](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md) "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:247
msgid ""
"This option is accepted by `nix-env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-shell` and "
"`nix-build`. When evaluating Nix expressions, the expression evaluator will "
"automatically try to call functions that it encounters. It can automatically "
"call functions for which every argument has a [default value](../../language/"
"syntax.md#functions) (e.g., `{ argName ?  defaultValue }: ...`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:263
msgid ""
"So if you call this Nix expression (e.g., when you do `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname`), the function will be called automatically using the value "
"[`builtins.currentSystem`](../../language/builtins.md) for the `system` "
"argument. You can override this using `--arg`, e.g., `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname --arg system \\\"i686-freebsd\\\"`. (Note that since the "
"argument is a Nix string literal, you have to escape the quotes.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:282
msgid ""
"Select an attribute from the top-level Nix expression being evaluated. (`nix-"
"env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.) The _attribute "
"path_ _attrPath_ is a sequence of attribute names separated by dots. For "
"instance, given a top-level Nix expression _e_, the attribute path "
"`xorg.xorgserver` would cause the expression `e.xorg.xorgserver` to be used. "
"See [`nix-env --install`](../../command-ref/nix-env/install.md) for some "
"concrete examples."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:295
msgid ""
"The [URL to the Nix store](../../store/types/index.md#store-url-format) to "
"use for evaluation, i.e. where to store derivations (`.drv` files) and "
"inputs referenced by them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:307
msgid ""
"Add an entry to the list of search paths used to resolve [lookup paths]"
"(../../language/constructs/lookup-path.md). This option may be given "
"multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:332
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr "環境變數"

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:334
msgid "`NIX_PROFILE`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:336
msgid ""
"Location of the Nix profile. Defaults to the target of the symlink `~/.nix-"
"profile`, if it exists, or `/nix/var/nix/profiles/default` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:347
msgid ""
"The following environment variables affect how Nix loads its configuration. "
"See the [configuration file](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#configuration-"
"file) documentation for full details."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:393
msgid ""
"See the [Store Types](../../store/types/index.md) chapter; each store has a "
"`store` setting linking back to this as its default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:401
#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:409
msgid ""
"The [Local Store](../../store/types/local-store.md), [Local Daemon Store]"
"(../../store/types/local-daemon-store.md), and [Experimental SSH Store with "
"filesystem mounted](../../store/types/experimental-ssh-store-with-filesystem-"
"mounted.md) have per-store settings that override this."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:416
msgid ""
"See the [Local Daemon Store](../../store/types/local-daemon-store.md) "
"documentation for details on how the socket path is resolved."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:426
msgid ""
"Overrides the [`store`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-store) setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:456
msgid ""
"A colon-separated list of search path entries used to resolve [lookup paths]"
"(../../language/constructs/lookup-path.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:458
msgid ""
"This environment variable overrides the value of the [`nix-path` "
"configuration setting](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-nix-path)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:460
msgid ""
"It can be extended using the [`-I` option](../../command-ref/opt-"
"common.md#opt-I)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:493
msgid ""
"For backwards compatibility, legacy Nix commands (e.g. `nix-env`, `nix-"
"channel`) use dotfiles in `$HOME` instead of these directories unless [`use-"
"xdg-base-directories`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-"
"directories) is enabled. [New Nix commands](../../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix.md) (experimental) use the proper directories by default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:496
msgid ""
"When [`use-xdg-base-directories`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-"
"xdg-base-directories) is enabled, the configuration directory is resolved as:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:542
msgid "Delete explicit generation numbers"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:548
msgid ""
"Delete the generations numbered 3, 4, and 8, so long as the current active "
"generation is not any of those."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:550
msgid "Keep most-recent by count (number of generations)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:556
msgid ""
"Suppose `30` is the current generation, and we currently have generations "
"numbered `20` through `32`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:558
msgid ""
"Then this command will delete generations `20` through `25` (`<= 30 - 5`), "
"and keep generations `26` through `31` (`> 30 - 5`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:561
msgid "Keep most-recent by time (number of days)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:567
msgid ""
"This command will delete all generations older than 30 days, except for the "
"generation that was active 30 days ago (if it currently exists)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md:569
msgid "Delete all older"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:3
msgid "`nix-env --install` - add packages to user environment"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-env` {`--install` | `-i`} _args…_ \\[{`--prebuilt-only` | `-b`}\\] \\"
"[{`--attr` | `-A`}\\] \\[`--from-expression`\\] \\[`-E`\\] \\[`--from-"
"profile` _path_\\] \\[`--preserve-installed` | `-P`\\] \\[`--remove-all` | `-"
"r`\\] \\[`--priority` _priority_\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:18
msgid ""
"The `--install` operation creates a new user environment. It is based on the "
"current generation of the active [profile](../../command-ref/files/"
"profiles.md), to which a set of [store paths](../../store/store-path.md) "
"described by _args_ is added."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:23
msgid "The arguments _args_ map to store paths in a number of possible ways:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:25
msgid ""
"By default, _args_ is a set of names denoting derivations in the [default "
"Nix expression](../../command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md). These "
"are [realised](../../glossary.md#gloss-realise), and the resulting output "
"paths are installed. Currently installed derivations with a name equal to "
"the name of a derivation being added are removed unless the option `--"
"preserve-installed` is specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:33
msgid ""
"If there are multiple derivations matching a name in _args_ that have the "
"same name (e.g., `gcc-3.3.6` and `gcc-4.1.1`), then the derivation with the "
"highest _priority_ is used. A derivation can define a priority by declaring "
"the `meta.priority` attribute. This attribute should be a number, with a "
"higher value denoting a lower priority. The default priority is `5`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:40
msgid ""
"If there are multiple matching derivations with the same priority, then the "
"derivation with the highest version will be installed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:43
msgid ""
"You can force the installation of multiple derivations with the same name by "
"being specific about the versions. For instance, `nix-env --install "
"gcc-3.3.6 gcc-4.1.1` will install both version of GCC (and will probably "
"cause a user environment conflict!)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:48
msgid ""
"If [`--attr`](#opt-attr) / `-A` is specified, the arguments are _attribute "
"paths_ that select attributes from the [default Nix expression](../../"
"command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md). This is faster than using "
"derivation names and unambiguous. Show the attribute paths of available "
"packages with [`nix-env --query`](./query.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:56
msgid ""
"If `--from-profile` _path_ is given, _args_ is a set of names denoting "
"installed [store paths](../../store/store-path.md) in the profile _path_. "
"This is an easy way to copy user environment elements from one profile to "
"another."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:61
msgid ""
"If `--from-expression` is given, _args_ are [Nix language functions](../../"
"language/syntax.md#functions) that are called with the [default Nix "
"expression](../../command-ref/files/default-nix-expression.md) as their "
"single argument. The derivations returned by those function calls are "
"installed. This allows derivations to be specified in an unambiguous way, "
"which is necessary if there are multiple derivations with the same name."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:65
msgid ""
"If `--priority` _priority_ is given, the priority of the derivations being "
"installed is set to _priority_. This can be used to override the priority of "
"the derivations being installed. This is useful if _args_ are [store paths]"
"(../../store/store-path.md), which don't have any priority information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:69
msgid ""
"If _args_ are [store paths](../../store/store-path.md) that point to [store "
"derivations](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation), then those store "
"derivations are [realised](../../glossary.md#gloss-realise), and the "
"resulting output paths are installed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:71
msgid ""
"If _args_ are [store paths](../../store/store-path.md) that do not point to "
"store derivations, then these are [realised](../../glossary.md#gloss-"
"realise) and installed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:73
msgid ""
"By default all [outputs](../../language/derivations.md#attr-outputs) are "
"installed for each [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"derivation). This can be overridden by adding a `meta.outputsToInstall` "
"attribute on the derivation listing a subset of the output names."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:78
msgid ""
"The file `example.nix` defines a derivation with two outputs `foo` and "
"`bar`, each containing a file."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:80
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"# example.nix\n"
"let\n"
"  pkgs = import <nixpkgs> {};\n"
"  command = ''\n"
"    ${pkgs.coreutils}/bin/mkdir -p $foo $bar\n"
"    echo foo > $foo/foo-file\n"
"    echo bar > $bar/bar-file\n"
"  '';\n"
"in\n"
"derivation {\n"
"  name = \"example\";\n"
"  builder = \"${pkgs.bash}/bin/bash\";\n"
"  args = [ \"-c\" command ];\n"
"  outputs = [ \"foo\" \"bar\" ];\n"
"  system = builtins.currentSystem;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:99
msgid ""
"Installing from this Nix expression will make files from both outputs appear "
"in the current profile."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:110
msgid ""
"Adding `meta.outputsToInstall` to that derivation will make `nix-env` only "
"install files from the specified outputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:112
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"# example-outputs.nix\n"
"import ./example.nix // { meta.outputsToInstall = [ \"bar\" ]; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:129
msgid "`--prebuilt-only` / `-b`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:131
msgid ""
"Use only derivations for which a substitute is registered, i.e., there is a "
"pre-built binary available that can be downloaded in lieu of building the "
"derivation. Thus, no packages will be built from source."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:136
msgid "`--preserve-installed` / `-P`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:138
msgid ""
"Do not remove derivations with a name matching one of the derivations being "
"installed. Usually, trying to have two versions of the same package "
"installed in the same generation of a profile will lead to an error in "
"building the generation, due to file name clashes between the two versions. "
"However, this is not the case for all packages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:145
msgid "`--remove-all` / `-r`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-env/install.md:147
msgid ""
"Remove all previously installed packages first. This is equivalent to "
"running `nix-env --uninstall '.*'` first, except that everything happens in "
"a single transaction."
msgstr ""

