"`nix-store --generate-binary-cache-key` - generate key pair to use for a "
"binary cache"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/generate-binary-cache-key.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-store` `--generate-binary-cache-key` _key-name_ _secret-key-file_ "
"_public-key-file_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/generate-binary-cache-key.md:11
msgid ""
"This command generates an [Ed25519 key pair](http://ed25519.cr.yp.to/) that "
"can be used to create a signed binary cache. It takes three mandatory "
"parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/generate-binary-cache-key.md:15
msgid ""
"A key name, such as `cache.example.org-1`, that is used to look up keys on "
"the client when it verifies signatures. It can be anything, but it’s "
"suggested to use the host name of your cache (e.g. `cache.example.org`) with "
"a suffix denoting the number of the key (to be incremented every time you "
"need to revoke a key)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/generate-binary-cache-key.md:21
msgid "The file name where the secret key is to be stored."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/generate-binary-cache-key.md:23
