#: source/command-ref/nix-store/import.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix-store --import` - import [Nix Archive](../../store/file-system-object/"
"content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) into the store"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/import.md:9
msgid "`nix-store` `--import`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/import.md:13
msgid ""
"The operation `--import` reads a serialisation of a set of [store objects]"
"(../../glossary.md#gloss-store-object) produced by [`nix-store --export`](./"
"export.md) from standard input, and adds those store objects to the "
"specified [Nix store](../../store/index.md). Paths that already exist in the "
"target Nix store are ignored. If a path [refers](../../glossary.md#gloss-"
"reference) to another path that doesn’t exist in the target Nix store, the "
"import fails."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/import.md:497
msgid "Given a closure of GNU Hello as a file:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/import.md:499
msgid ""
"```shell-session\n"
"$ storePath=\"$(nix-build '<nixpkgs>' -I nixpkgs=channel:nixpkgs-unstable -A "
"hello --no-out-link)\"\n"
"$ nix-store --export $(nix-store --query --requisites $storePath) > "
"hello.closure\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/import.md:504
msgid ""
"Import the closure into a [remote SSH store](../../store/types/ssh-store.md) "
"using the [`--store`](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-store) option:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/import.md:506
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-store --import --store ssh://alice@itchy.example.org < hello.closure\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/load-db.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --load-db` - import Nix database"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/load-db.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--load-db`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/load-db.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--load-db` reads a dump of the Nix database created by `--"
"dump-db` from standard input and loads it into the Nix database."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/optimise.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --optimise` - reduce disk space usage"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/optimise.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--optimise`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/optimise.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--optimise` reduces Nix store disk space usage by finding "
"identical files in the store and hard-linking them to each other. It "
"typically reduces the size of the store by something like 25-35%. Only "
"regular files and symlinks are hard-linked in this manner. Files are "
"considered identical when they have the same [Nix Archive (NAR)](../../store/"
"file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) serialisation: "
"that is, regular files must have the same contents and permission "
"(executable or non-executable), and symlinks must have the same contents."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/optimise.md:20
msgid ""
"After completion, or when the command is interrupted, a report on the "
"achieved savings is printed on standard error."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/optimise.md:23
msgid "Use `-vv` or `-vvv` to get some progress indication."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/print-env.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --print-env` - print the build environment of a derivation"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/print-env.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--print-env` _drvpath_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/print-env.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--print-env` prints out the environment of a derivation in a "
"format that can be evaluated by a shell. The command line arguments of the "
"builder are placed in the variable `_args`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --query` - display information about store paths"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-store` {`--query` | `-q`} {`--outputs` | `--requisites` | `-R` | `--"
"references` | `--referrers` | `--referrers-closure` | `--deriver` | `-d` | "
"`--valid-derivers` | `--graph` | `--tree` | `--binding` _name_ | `-b` _name_ "
"| `--hash` | `--size` | `--roots`} \\[`--use-output`\\] \\[`-u`\\] \\[`--"
"force-realise`\\] \\[`-f`\\] _paths…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:17
msgid ""
"The operation `--query` displays various bits of information about the store "
"paths . The queries are described below. At most one query can be specified. "
"The default query is `--outputs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:21
msgid ""
"The paths _paths_ may also be symlinks from outside of the Nix store, to the "
"Nix store. In that case, the query is applied to the target of the symlink."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:25
msgid "Common query options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:27
msgid "`--use-output` / `-u`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:29
msgid ""
"For each argument to the query that is a [store derivation](../../"
"glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation), apply the query to the output path of "
"the derivation instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:32
msgid "`--force-realise` / `-f`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:34
msgid ""
"Realise each argument to the query first (see [`nix-store --realise`](./"
"realise.md))."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:40
msgid "`--outputs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:42
msgid ""
"Prints out the [output paths](../../glossary.md#gloss-output-path) of the "
"store derivations _paths_. These are the paths that will be produced when "
"the derivation is built."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:48
msgid "`--references`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:50
msgid ""
"Prints the set of [references](../../glossary.md#gloss-reference) of the "
"store paths _paths_, that is, their immediate dependencies. (For _all_ "
"dependencies, use `--requisites`.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:56
msgid "`--requisites` / `-R`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:58
msgid ""
"Prints out the set of [_requisites_](../../glossary.md#gloss-requisite) "
"(better known as the [closure](../../glossary.md#gloss-closure)) of the "
"store path _paths_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:63
msgid "This query has one option:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:65
msgid ""
"`--include-outputs` Also include the existing output paths of [store "
"derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s, and their closures."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:69
msgid ""
"This query can be used to implement various kinds of deployment. A _source "
"deployment_ is obtained by distributing the closure of a store derivation. A "
"_binary deployment_ is obtained by distributing the closure of an output "
"path. A _cache deployment_ (combined source/binary deployment, including "
"binaries of build-time-only dependencies) is obtained by distributing the "
"closure of a store derivation and specifying the option `--include-outputs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:77
msgid "`--referrers`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:79
msgid ""
"Prints the set of [_referrers_](../../glossary.md#gloss-referrer) of the "
"store paths _paths_, that is, the store paths currently existing in the Nix "
"store that refer to one of _paths_. Note that contrary to the references, "
"the set of referrers is not constant; it can change as store paths are added "
"or removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:87
msgid "`--referrers-closure`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:89
msgid ""
"Prints the closure of the set of store paths _paths_ under the [referrers "
"relation](../../glossary.md#gloss-referrer); that is, all store paths that "
"directly or indirectly refer to one of _paths_. These are all the path "
"currently in the Nix store that are dependent on _paths_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:96
msgid "`--deriver` / `-d`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:98
msgid ""
"Prints the [deriver](../../glossary.md#gloss-deriver) that was used to build "
"the store paths _paths_. If the path has no deriver (e.g., if it is a source "
"file), or if the deriver is not known (e.g., in the case of a binary-only "
"deployment), the string `unknown-deriver` is printed. The returned deriver "
"is not guaranteed to exist in the local store, for example when _paths_ were "
"substituted from a binary cache. Use `--valid-derivers` instead to obtain "
"valid paths only."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:108
msgid "`--valid-derivers`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:110
msgid ""
"Prints a set of derivation files (`.drv`) which are supposed produce said "
"paths when realized. Might print nothing, for example for source paths or "
"paths substituted from a binary cache."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:114
msgid "`--graph`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:116
msgid ""
"Prints the references graph of the store paths _paths_ in the format of the "
"`dot` tool of AT&T's [Graphviz package](http://www.graphviz.org/). This can "
"be used to visualise dependency graphs. To obtain a build-time dependency "
"graph, apply this to a store derivation. To obtain a runtime dependency "
"graph, apply it to an output path."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:123
msgid "`--tree`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:125
msgid ""
"Prints the references graph of the store paths _paths_ as a nested ASCII "
"tree. References are ordered by descending closure size; this tends to "
"flatten the tree, making it more readable. The query only recurses into a "
"store path when it is first encountered; this prevents a blowup of the tree "
"representation of the graph."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:131
msgid "`--graphml`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:133
msgid ""
"Prints the references graph of the store paths _paths_ in the [GraphML]"
"(http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/) file format. This can be used to "
"visualise dependency graphs. To obtain a build-time dependency graph, apply "
"this to a [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation). To "
"obtain a runtime dependency graph, apply it to an output path."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:139
msgid "`--binding` _name_ / `-b` _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:141
msgid ""
"Prints the value of the attribute _name_ (i.e., environment variable) of the "
"[store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s _paths_. It is "
"an error for a derivation to not have the specified attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:145
msgid "`--hash`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:147
msgid ""
"Prints the SHA-256 hash of the contents of the store paths _paths_ (that is, "
"the hash of the output of `nix-store --dump` on the given paths). Since the "
"hash is stored in the Nix database, this is a fast operation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:152
msgid "`--size`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:154
msgid ""
"Prints the size in bytes of the contents of the store paths _paths_ — to be "
"precise, the size of the output of `nix-store --dump` on the given paths. "
"Note that the actual disk space required by the store paths may be higher, "
"especially on filesystems with large cluster sizes."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:160
msgid "`--roots`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:162
msgid ""
"Prints the garbage collector roots that point, directly or indirectly, at "
"the store paths _paths_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:639
msgid ""
"Print the closure (runtime dependencies) of the `svn` program in the current "
"user environment:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:649
msgid "Print the build-time dependencies of `svn`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:659
msgid ""
"The difference with the previous example is that we ask the closure of the "
"derivation (`-qd`), not the closure of the output path that contains `svn`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:663
msgid "Show the build-time dependencies as a tree:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:675
msgid "Show all paths that depend on the same OpenSSL library as `svn`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:685
msgid ""
"Show all paths that directly or indirectly depend on the Glibc (C library) "
"used by `svn`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:695
msgid ""
"Note that `ldd` is a command that prints out the dynamic libraries used by "
"an ELF executable."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:698
msgid ""
"Make a picture of the runtime dependency graph of the current user "
"environment:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/query.md:706
msgid ""
"Show every garbage collector root that points to a store path that depends "
"on `svn`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/read-log.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --read-log` - print build log"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/read-log.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` {`--read-log` | `-l`} _paths…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/read-log.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--read-log` prints the build log of the specified store paths "
"on standard output. The build log is whatever the builder of a derivation "
"wrote to standard output and standard error. If a store path is not a "
"derivation, the deriver of the store path is used."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/read-log.md:16
msgid ""
"Build logs are kept in `/nix/var/log/nix/drvs`. However, there is no "
"guarantee that a build log is available for any particular store path. For "
"instance, if the path was downloaded as a pre-built binary through a "
"substitute, then the log is unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --realise` - build or fetch store objects"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` {`--realise` | `-r`} _paths…_ \\[`--dry-run`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:12
msgid "Each of _paths_ is processed as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:14
msgid ""
"If the path leads to a [store derivation](../../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"derivation):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:15
msgid ""
"If it is not [valid](../../glossary.md#gloss-validity), substitute the store "
"derivation file itself."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:16
msgid "Realise its [output paths](../../glossary.md#gloss-output-path):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:17
msgid ""
"Try to fetch from [substituters](../../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"substituters) the [store objects](../../store/store-object.md) associated "
"with the output paths in the store derivation's [closure](../../"
"glossary.md#gloss-closure)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:18
msgid ""
"With [content-addressing derivations](../../development/experimental-"
"features.md#xp-feature-ca-derivations) (experimental): Determine the output "
"paths to realise by querying content-addressed realisation entries in the "
"[Nix database](../../glossary.md#gloss-nix-database)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:20
msgid ""
"For any store paths that cannot be substituted, produce the required store "
"objects:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:21
msgid "Realise all outputs of the derivation's dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:22
msgid ""
"Run the derivation's [`builder`](../../language/derivations.md#attr-builder) "
"executable"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:24
msgid ""
"Otherwise, and if the path is not already valid: Try to fetch the associated "
"[store objects](../../store/store-object.md) in the path's [closure](../../"
"glossary.md#gloss-closure) from [substituters](../../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-substituters)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:26
msgid ""
"If no substitutes are available and no store derivation is given, "
"realisation fails."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:38
msgid ""
"The resulting paths are printed on standard output. For non-derivation "
"arguments, the argument itself is printed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:56
msgid ""
"The build output was rejected because it does not match the [`outputHash` "
"attribute of the derivation](../../language/advanced-attributes.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:81
msgid ""
"Print on standard error a description of what packages would be built or "
"downloaded, without actually performing the operation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:84
msgid "`--ignore-unknown`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:86
msgid ""
"If a non-derivation path does not have a substitute, then silently ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:89
msgid "`--check`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:91
msgid ""
"This option allows you to check whether a derivation is deterministic. It "
"rebuilds the specified derivation and checks whether the result is bitwise-"
"identical with the existing outputs, printing an error if that’s not the "
"case. The outputs of the specified derivation must already exist. When used "
"with `-K`, if an output path is not identical to the corresponding output "
"from the previous build, the new output path is left in `/nix/store/"
"name.check.`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:574
msgid ""
"This operation is typically used to build [store derivation](../../"
"glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s produced by [`nix-instantiate`](../../"
"command-ref/nix-instantiate.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:582
msgid ""
"This is essentially what [`nix-build`](../../command-ref/nix-build.md) does."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:584
msgid "To test whether a previously-built derivation is deterministic:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/realise.md:590
msgid ""
"Use [`nix-store --read-log`](./read-log.md) to show the stderr and stdout of "
"a build:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --register-validity` - register store objects as valid"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-store` `--register-validity` \\[`--reregister`\\] \\[`--hash-given`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--register-validity` reads serialised [metadata](../../store/"
"store-object.md#metadata) for [store objects](../../store/store-object.md) "
"from standard input and registers those store objects as [valid](../../"
"glossary.md#gloss-validity) in the [local Nix store](../../store/types/local-"
"store.md). As with the [traditional (post-build) processing of outputs]"
"(../../store/building.md#traditional-post-build-processing) during building, "
"this command is used when the [file system objects](../../store/file-system-"
"object.md) of the would-be store objects already exist in the local store, "
"but the database does not yet know their metadata. Running this command "
"catches the database up with the file system, making them bona fide store "
"objects."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:15
msgid ""
"The input consists of a sequence of records, one per store object. Each "
"record has the following format:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:29
msgid ""
"Here, _path_ is the [store path](../../store/store-path.md) of the store "
"object to register. _nar-hash_ is the base-16 SHA-256 hash of the path’s "
"[NAR](../../store/file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) "
"serialisation, and _nar-size_ is the size of the NAR in bytes. These two "
"lines are only present when `--hash-given` is specified; otherwise they must "
"be omitted, and Nix computes the NAR hash and size from the store object "
"instead. _deriver_ is the [store path](../../store/store-path.md) of the "
"[deriver](../../glossary.md#gloss-deriver), the derivation that produced "
"this path, or an empty line if unknown. _number-of-references_ specifies how "
"many [reference](../../glossary.md#gloss-reference) paths follow, which are "
"listed on the subsequent lines."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:35
msgid ""
"The input is typically generated by other Nix operations such as "
"[`exportReferencesGraph`](../../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-"
"exportReferencesGraph). Only this textual format is understood; the JSON "
"form that `exportReferencesGraph` produces with [structured attributes]"
"(../../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-structuredAttrs) is not "
"accepted. Since the files produced for builders contain no hashes, they must "
"be used without `--hash-given`. It is the responsibility of the caller to "
"provide a complete [closure](../../glossary.md#gloss-closure)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:40
msgid ""
"This is a low-level operation intended for internal use. Its main use is "
"registering the closure of a system inside an image or chroot being "
"populated with a Nix store, e.g. when building NixOS installation images."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:45
msgid "`--reregister`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:47
msgid ""
"Register the store objects even if they are already marked as valid in the "
"store. Without this flag, already-valid store objects are skipped."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:50
msgid "`--hash-given`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/register-validity.md:52
msgid ""
"Expect the NAR hash and size in the input, as described above, instead of "
"computing them from the store objects."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:3
msgid "`nix --repair-path` - re-download path from substituter"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--repair-path` _paths…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/repair-path.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--repair-path` attempts to “repair” the specified paths by "
"redownloading them using the available substituters. If no substitutes are "
"available, then repair is not possible."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/restore.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --restore` - extract a Nix archive"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/restore.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--restore` _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/restore.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--restore` unpacks a [Nix Archive (NAR)](../../store/file-"
"system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) to _path_, which must "
"not already exist. The archive is read from standard input."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --serve` - serve local Nix store over SSH"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--serve` \\[`--write`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--serve` provides access to the Nix store over stdin and "
"stdout, and is intended to be used as a means of providing Nix store access "
"to a restricted ssh user."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:15
msgid "The following flags are available:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:17
msgid "`--write`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:19
msgid ""
"Allow the connected client to request the realization of derivations. In "
"effect, this can be used to make the host act as a remote builder."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:497
msgid ""
"To turn a host into a build server, the `authorized_keys` file can be used "
"to provide build access to a given SSH public key:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/serve.md:500
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ cat <<EOF >>/root/.ssh/authorized_keys\n"
"command=\"nice -n20 nix-store --serve --write\" ssh-rsa "
"AAAAB3NzaC1yc2EAAAA...\n"
"EOF\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify-path.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --verify-path` - check path contents against Nix database"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify-path.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--verify-path` _paths…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify-path.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--verify-path` compares the contents of the given store paths "
"to their cryptographic hashes stored in Nix’s database. For every changed "
"path, it prints a warning message. The exit status is 0 if no path has "
"changed, and 1 otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify-path.md:490
msgid "To verify the integrity of the `svn` command and all its dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify.md:3
msgid "`nix-store --verify` - check Nix database for consistency"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify.md:7
msgid "`nix-store` `--verify` \\[`--check-contents`\\] \\[`--repair`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify.md:11
msgid ""
"The operation `--verify` verifies the internal consistency of the Nix "
"database, and the consistency between the Nix database and the Nix store. "
"Any inconsistencies encountered are automatically repaired. Inconsistencies "
"are generally the result of the Nix store or database being modified by non-"
"Nix tools, or of bugs in Nix itself."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify.md:19
msgid "`--check-contents`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify.md:21
msgid ""
"Checks that the contents of every valid store path has not been altered by "
"computing a SHA-256 hash of the contents and comparing it with the hash "
"stored in the Nix database at build time. Paths that have been modified are "
"printed out. For large stores, `--check-contents` is obviously quite slow."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify.md:27
msgid "`--repair`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-store/verify.md:29
msgid ""
"If any valid path is missing from the store, or (if `--check-contents` is "
"given) the contents of a valid path has been modified, then try to repair "
"the path by redownloading it. See `nix-store --repair-path` for details."
msgstr ""

