#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` - delete unreachable [store objects](../store/store-"
"object.md)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` \\[`--delete-old`\\] \\[`-d`\\] \\[`--delete-older-"
"than` _period_\\] \\[`--max-freed` _bytes_\\] \\[`--dry-run`\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:11
msgid ""
"The command `nix-collect-garbage` is mostly an alias of [`nix-store --gc`]"
"(../command-ref/nix-store/gc.md). That is, it deletes all unreachable [store "
"objects](../store/store-object.md) in the Nix store to clean up your system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:14
msgid ""
"However, it provides two additional options, [`--delete-old`](#opt-delete-"
"old) and [`--delete-older-than`](#opt-delete-older-than), which also delete "
"old [profiles](../command-ref/files/profiles.md), allowing potentially more "
"[store objects](../store/store-object.md) to be deleted because profiles are "
"also garbage collection roots. These options are the equivalent of running "
"[`nix-env --delete-generations`](../command-ref/nix-env/delete-"
"generations.md) with various augments on multiple profiles, prior to running "
"`nix-collect-garbage` (or just `nix-store --gc`) without any flags."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:24
msgid "Deleting previous configurations makes rollbacks to them impossible."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:26
msgid ""
"These flags should be used with care, because they potentially delete "
"generations of profiles used by other users on the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:28
msgid "Locations searched for profiles"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:30
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` cannot know about all profiles; that information "
"doesn't exist. Instead, it looks in a few locations, and acts on all "
"profiles it finds there:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:33
msgid ""
"The default profile locations as specified in the [profiles](../command-ref/"
"files/profiles.md) section of the manual."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:35
msgid "**NOTE**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:37
msgid "Not stable; subject to change"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:39
msgid ""
"Do not rely on this functionality; it just exists for migration purposes and "
"may change in the future. These deprecated paths remain a private "
"implementation detail of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:42
msgid "`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles` and `$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:44
msgid ""
"With the exception of `$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root` and "
"`$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/default`, these directories are no longer used by "
"other commands. `nix-collect-garbage` looks there anyways in order to clean "
"up profiles from older versions of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:49
msgid ""
"These options are for deleting old [profiles](../command-ref/files/"
"profiles.md) prior to deleting unreachable [store objects](../store/store-"
"object.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:51
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-delete-old\">[`--delete-old`](#opt-delete-old)</span> / `-d`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:53
msgid "Delete all old generations of profiles."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:55
msgid ""
"This is the equivalent of invoking [`nix-env --delete-generations old`](../"
"command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md#generations-old) on each found "
"profile."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:57
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-delete-older-than\">[`--delete-older-than`](#opt-delete-older-"
"than)</span> _period_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:59
msgid ""
"Delete all generations of profiles older than the specified amount (except "
"for the generations that were active at that point in time). _period_ is a "
"value such as `30d`, which would mean 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:62
msgid ""
"This is the equivalent of invoking [`nix-env --delete-generations <period>`]"
"(../command-ref/nix-env/delete-generations.md#generations-time) on each "
"found profile. See the documentation of that command for additional "
"information about the _period_ argument."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:65
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-freed\">[`--max-freed`](#opt-max-freed)</span> _bytes_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-collect-garbage.md:510
msgid ""
"To delete from the Nix store everything that is not used by the current "
"generations of each profile, do"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix-copy-closure` - copy store objects to or from a remote machine via SSH"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-copy-closure` \\[`--to` | `--from` \\] \\[`--gzip`\\] \\[`--include-"
"outputs`\\] \\[`--use-substitutes` | `-s`\\] \\[`-v`\\] \\"
"[_user_@\\]_machine_\\[:_port_\\] _paths_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:17
msgid ""
"Given _paths_ from one machine, `nix-copy-closure` computes the [closure](../"
"glossary.md#gloss-closure) of those paths (i.e. all their dependencies in "
"the Nix store), and copies [store objects](../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"object) in that closure to another machine via SSH. It doesn’t copy store "
"objects that are already present on the other machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:22
msgid ""
"While the Nix store to use on the local machine can be specified on the "
"command line with the [`--store`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-store) "
"option, the Nix store to be accessed on the remote machine can only be "
"[configured statically](../command-ref/conf-file.md#configuration-file) on "
"that remote machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:24
msgid ""
"Since `nix-copy-closure` calls `ssh`, you may need to authenticate with the "
"remote machine. In fact, you may be asked for authentication _twice_ because "
"`nix-copy-closure` currently connects twice to the remote machine: first to "
"get the set of paths missing on the target machine, and second to send the "
"dump of those paths. When using public key authentication, you can avoid "
"typing the passphrase with `ssh-agent`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:30
msgid "`--to`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:32
msgid ""
"Copy the closure of _paths_ from a Nix store accessible from the local "
"machine to the Nix store on the remote _machine_. This is the default "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:35
msgid "`--from`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:37
msgid ""
"Copy the closure of _paths_ from the Nix store on the remote _machine_ to "
"the local machine's specified Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:39
msgid "`--gzip`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:41
msgid "Enable compression of the SSH connection."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:43
msgid "`--include-outputs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:45
msgid ""
"Also copy the outputs of [store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"derivation)s included in the closure."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:49
msgid "`--use-substitutes` / `-s`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:51
msgid ""
"Attempt to download missing store objects on the target from [substituters]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-substituters). Any store objects that "
"cannot be substituted on the target are still copied normally from the "
"source. This is useful, for instance, if the connection between the source "
"and target machine is slow, but the connection between the target machine "
"and `cache.nixos.org` (the default binary cache server) is fast."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:292
msgid "`NIX_SSHOPTS`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:294
msgid "Additional options to be passed to `ssh` on the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:499
msgid "Copy GNU Hello with all its dependencies to a remote machine:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:501
msgid ""
"```shell-session\n"
"$ storePath=\"$(nix-build '<nixpkgs>' -I nixpkgs=channel:nixpkgs-unstable -A "
"hello --no-out-link)\"\n"
"$ nix-copy-closure --to alice@itchy.example.org \"$storePath\"\n"
"copying 5 paths...\n"
"copying path '/nix/store/h6q8sqsqfbd3252f9gixqn3z282wds7m-xgcc-13.2.0-"
"libgcc' to 'ssh://alice@itchy.example.org'...\n"
"copying path '/nix/store/imnwvn96lw355giswsk36hx105j4wnpj-libunistring-1.1' "
"to 'ssh://alice@itchy.example.org'...\n"
"copying path '/nix/store/85301indj7scg34spnfczkz72jgv8wa9-libidn2-2.3.7' to "
"'ssh://alice@itchy.example.org'...\n"
"copying path '/nix/store/ypwfsaljwhzw9iffiysxmxnhjj8v7np0-glibc-2.39-31' to "
"'ssh://alice@itchy.example.org'...\n"
"copying path '/nix/store/0dklv59zppdsqdvgf0qdvjgzcs5wbwxa-hello-2.12.1' to "
"'ssh://alice@itchy.example.org'...\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:514
msgid ""
"Copy GNU Hello from a remote machine using a known store path, and run it:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:516
msgid ""
"```shell-session\n"
"$ storePath=\"$(nix-instantiate --eval --raw '<nixpkgs>' -I "
"nixpkgs=channel:nixpkgs-unstable -A hello.outPath)\"\n"
"$ nix-copy-closure --from alice@itchy.example.org \"$storePath\"\n"
"$ \"$storePath\"/bin/hello\n"
"Hello, world!\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-daemon.md:3
msgid "`nix-daemon` - Nix multi-user support daemon"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-daemon.md:7
msgid "`nix-daemon`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-daemon.md:11
msgid ""
"The Nix daemon is necessary in multi-user Nix installations. It runs build "
"tasks and other operations on the Nix store on behalf of unprivileged users."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:3
msgid "`nix-hash` - compute the cryptographic hash of a path"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-hash` \\[`--flat`\\] \\[`--base32`\\] \\[`--truncate`\\] \\[`--type` "
"_hashAlgo_\\] _path…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:9
msgid ""
"`nix-hash` \\[`--to-base16`\\|`--to-base32`\\|`--to-base64`\\|`--to-sri`\\] "
"\\[`--type` _hashAlgo_\\] _hash…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:13
msgid ""
"The command `nix-hash` computes the cryptographic hash of the contents of "
"each _path_ and prints it on standard output. By default, it computes an MD5 "
"hash, but other hash algorithms are available as well. The hash is printed "
"in hexadecimal. To generate the same hash as `nix-prefetch-url` you have to "
"specify multiple arguments, see below for an example."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:20
msgid ""
"The hash is computed over a _serialisation_ of each path: a dump of the file "
"system tree rooted at the path. This allows directories and symlinks to be "
"hashed as well as regular files. The dump is in the _[Nix Archive (NAR)](../"
"store/file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) format_ "
"produced by [`nix-store --dump`](../command-ref/nix-store/dump.md).  Thus, "
"`nix-hash path` yields the same cryptographic hash as `nix-store --dump path "
"| md5sum`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:32
msgid "`--flat`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:34
msgid ""
"Print the cryptographic hash of the contents of each regular file _path_. "
"That is, instead of computing the hash of the [Nix Archive (NAR)](../store/"
"file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-nix-archive) of _path_, just "
"[directly hash](../store/file-system-object/content-address.md#serial-flat) "
"_path_ as is. This requires _path_ to resolve to a regular file rather than "
"directory. The result is identical to that produced by the GNU commands "
"`md5sum` and `sha1sum`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:42
msgid "`--base16`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:44
msgid "Print the hash in a hexadecimal representation (default)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:46
msgid "`--base32`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:48
msgid ""
"Print the hash in [Nix32](../protocols/nix32.md) representation rather than "
"hexadecimal. This representation is more compact and can be used in Nix "
"expressions (such as in calls to `fetchurl`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:52
msgid "`--base64`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:54
msgid ""
"Similar to `--base32`, but print the hash in a [Base64](https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base64) representation, which is more compact than the "
"Nix32 one."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:57
msgid "`--sri`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:59
msgid ""
"Print the hash in [SRI](../glossary.md#gloss-sri) format with Base64 "
"encoding. The type of hash algorithm will be prepended to the hash string, "
"followed by a hyphen (-) and the Base64 hash body."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:63
msgid "`--truncate`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:65
msgid "Truncate hashes longer than 160 bits (such as SHA-256) to 160 bits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:67
msgid "`--type` _hashAlgo_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:69
msgid ""
"Use the specified cryptographic hash algorithm, which can be one of "
"`blake3`, `md5`, `sha1`, `sha256`, and `sha512`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:72
msgid "`--to-base16`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:74
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the [Nix32](../protocols/nix32.md) hash "
"representation _hash_ to hexadecimal."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:77
msgid "`--to-base32`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:79
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the hexadecimal hash representation _hash_ "
"to [Nix32](../protocols/nix32.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:82
msgid "`--to-base64`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:84
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the hexadecimal hash representation _hash_ "
"to Base64."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:87
msgid "`--to-sri`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:89
msgid ""
"Don’t hash anything, but convert the hexadecimal hash representation _hash_ "
"to SRI."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:94
msgid "Computing the same hash as `nix-prefetch-url`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:96
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-prefetch-url file://<(echo test)\n"
"1lkgqb6fclns49861dwk9rzb6xnfkxbpws74mxnx01z9qyv1pjpj\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha256 --flat --base32 <(echo test)\n"
"1lkgqb6fclns49861dwk9rzb6xnfkxbpws74mxnx01z9qyv1pjpj\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:103
msgid "Computing hashes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-hash.md:105
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ mkdir test\n"
"$ echo \"hello\" > test/world\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash test/ (MD5 hash; default)\n"
"8179d3caeff1869b5ba1744e5a245c04\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-store --dump test/ | md5sum (for comparison)\n"
"8179d3caeff1869b5ba1744e5a245c04  -\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 test/\n"
"e4fd8ba5f7bbeaea5ace89fe10255536cd60dab6\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --base16 test/\n"
"e4fd8ba5f7bbeaea5ace89fe10255536cd60dab6\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --base32 test/\n"
"nvd61k9nalji1zl9rrdfmsmvyyjqpzg4\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --base64 test/\n"
"5P2Lpfe76upazon+ECVVNs1g2rY=\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha1 --sri test/\n"
"sha1-5P2Lpfe76upazon+ECVVNs1g2rY=\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha256 --flat test/\n"
"error: reading file `test/': Is a directory\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-hash --type sha256 --flat test/world\n"
"5891b5b522d5df086d0ff0b110fbd9d21bb4fc7163af34d08286a2e846f6be03\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

