#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:3
msgid "`nix-instantiate` - instantiate store derivations from Nix expressions"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate` \\[`--parse` | `--eval` \\[`--strict`\\] \\[`--raw` | `--"
"json` | `--xml`\\] \\] \\[`--read-write-mode`\\] \\[`--arg` _name_ "
"_value_\\] \\[{`--attr`\\| `-A`} _attrPath_\\] \\[`--add-root` _path_\\] \\"
"[`--expr` | `-E`\\] _files…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:16
msgid "`nix-instantiate` `--find-file` _files…_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:20
msgid ""
"The command `nix-instantiate` produces [store derivation](../"
"glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s from (high-level) Nix expressions. It "
"evaluates the Nix expressions in each of _files_ (which defaults to _./"
"default.nix_). Each top-level expression should evaluate to a derivation, a "
"list of derivations, or a set of derivations. The paths of the resulting "
"store derivations are printed on standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:28
msgid ""
"If _files_ is the character `-`, then a Nix expression will be read from "
"standard input."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:33
msgid "`--add-root` _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:35
msgid "See the [corresponding option](./nix-store.md) in `nix-store`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:37
msgid "`--parse`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:39
msgid ""
"Just parse the input files, and print their abstract syntax trees on "
"standard output as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:42
msgid "`--eval`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:44
msgid ""
"Just parse and evaluate the input files, and print the resulting values on "
"standard output. Store derivations are not serialized and written to the "
"store, but instead just hashed and discarded."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:50
msgid ""
"This option produces output which can be parsed as a Nix expression which "
"will produce a different result than the input expression when evaluated. "
"For example, these two Nix expressions print the same result despite having "
"different meaning:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:62
msgid ""
"For human-readable output, `nix eval` (experimental) is more informative:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:71
msgid ""
"For machine-readable output, the `--xml` option produces unambiguous output:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:74
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-instantiate --eval --xml --expr '{ foo = <CODE>; }'\n"
"<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>\n"
"<expr>\n"
"  <attrs>\n"
"    <attr column=\"3\" line=\"1\" name=\"foo\">\n"
"      <unevaluated />\n"
"    </attr>\n"
"  </attrs>\n"
"</expr>\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:86
msgid "`--find-file`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:88
msgid ""
"Look up the given files in Nix’s search path (as specified by the `NIX_PATH` "
"environment variable). If found, print the corresponding absolute paths on "
"standard output. For instance, if `NIX_PATH` is `nixpkgs=/home/alice/"
"nixpkgs`, then `nix-instantiate --find-file nixpkgs/default.nix` will print "
"`/home/alice/nixpkgs/default.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:94
msgid "`--strict`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:96
msgid ""
"When used with `--eval`, recursively evaluate list elements and attributes. "
"Normally, such sub-expressions are left unevaluated (since the Nix language "
"is lazy)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:102
msgid ""
"This option can cause non-termination, because lazy data structures can be "
"infinitely large."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:105
msgid "`--raw`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:107
msgid ""
"When used with `--eval`, the evaluation result must be a string, which is "
"printed verbatim, without quoting, escaping or trailing newline."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:112
msgid ""
"When used with `--eval`, print the resulting value as an JSON representation "
"of the abstract syntax tree rather than as a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:117
msgid ""
"When used with `--eval`, print the resulting value as an XML representation "
"of the abstract syntax tree rather than as a Nix expression. The schema is "
"the same as that used by the [`toXML` built-in](../language/builtins.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:122
msgid "`--read-write-mode`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:124
msgid ""
"When used with `--eval`, perform evaluation in read/write mode so nix "
"language features that require it will still work (at the cost of needing to "
"do instantiation of every evaluated derivation). If this option is not "
"enabled, there may be uninstantiated store paths in the final output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:566
msgid ""
"Instantiate [store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)s from "
"a Nix expression, and build them using `nix-store`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:581
msgid "You can also give a Nix expression on the command line:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:588
msgid "This is equivalent to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:594
msgid "Parsing and evaluating Nix expressions:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:606
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-instantiate --eval --xml --expr '1 + 2'\n"
"<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>\n"
"<expr>\n"
"  <int value=\"3\" />\n"
"</expr>\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:614
msgid "The difference between non-strict and strict evaluation:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-instantiate.md:616
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-instantiate --eval --xml --expr '{ x = {}; }'\n"
"<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>\n"
"<expr>\n"
"  <attrs>\n"
"    <attr column=\"3\" line=\"1\" name=\"x\">\n"
"      <unevaluated />\n"
"    </attr>\n"
"  </attrs>\n"
"</expr>\n"
"\n"
"$ nix-instantiate --eval --xml --strict --expr '{ x = {}; }'\n"
"<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>\n"
"<expr>\n"
"  <attrs>\n"
"    <attr column=\"3\" line=\"1\" name=\"x\">\n"
"      <attrs>\n"
"      </attrs>\n"
"    </attr>\n"
"  </attrs>\n"
"</expr>\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix-prefetch-url` - copy a file from a URL into the store and print its hash"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-prefetch-url` _url_ \\[_hash_\\] \\[`--type` _hashAlgo_\\] \\[`--print-"
"path`\\] \\[`--unpack`\\] \\[`--name` _name_\\]"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:15
msgid ""
"The command `nix-prefetch-url` downloads the file referenced by the URL "
"_url_, prints its cryptographic hash, and copies it into the Nix store. The "
"file name in the store is `hash-baseName`, where _baseName_ is everything "
"following the final slash in _url_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:20
msgid ""
"This command is just a convenience for Nix expression writers. Often a Nix "
"expression fetches some source distribution from the network using the "
"`fetchurl` expression contained in Nixpkgs. However, `fetchurl` requires a "
"cryptographic hash. If you don't know the hash, you would have to download "
"the file first, and then `fetchurl` would download it again when you build "
"your Nix expression. Since `fetchurl` uses the same name for the downloaded "
"file as `nix-prefetch-url`, the redundant download can be avoided."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:29
msgid ""
"If _hash_ is specified, then a download is not performed if the Nix store "
"already contains a file with the same hash and base name. Otherwise, the "
"file is downloaded, and an error is signaled if the actual hash of the file "
"does not match the specified hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:34
msgid ""
"This command prints the hash on standard output. The hash is printed using "
"[Nix32](../protocols/nix32.md) unless `--type md5` is specified, in which "
"case it's printed using base-16. Additionally, if the option `--print-path` "
"is used, the path of the downloaded file in the Nix store is also printed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:44
msgid ""
"Use the specified cryptographic hash algorithm, which can be one of "
"`blake3`, `md5`, `sha1`, `sha256`, and `sha512`. The default is `sha256`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:48
msgid "`--print-path`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:50
msgid "Print the store path of the downloaded file on standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:52
msgid "`--unpack`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:54
msgid ""
"Unpack the archive (which must be a tarball or zip file) and add the result "
"to the Nix store. The resulting hash can be used with functions such as "
"Nixpkgs’s `fetchzip` or `fetchFromGitHub`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:58
msgid "`--executable`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:60
msgid "Set the executable bit on the downloaded file."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:62
msgid "`--name` _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:64
msgid ""
"Override the name of the file in the Nix store. By default, this is `hash-"
"basename`, where _basename_ is the last component of _url_. Overriding the "
"name is necessary when _basename_ contains characters that are not allowed "
"in Nix store paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:71
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-prefetch-url ftp://ftp.gnu.org/pub/gnu/hello/hello-2.10.tar.gz\n"
"0ssi1wpaf7plaswqqjwigppsg5fyh99vdlb9kzl7c9lng89ndq1i\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:76
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-prefetch-url --print-path mirror://gnu/hello/hello-2.10.tar.gz\n"
"0ssi1wpaf7plaswqqjwigppsg5fyh99vdlb9kzl7c9lng89ndq1i\n"
"/nix/store/8alrpdaasjd1x6g1fczchmzbpqm936a3-hello-2.10.tar.gz\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-prefetch-url.md:82
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-prefetch-url --unpack --print-path https://github.com/NixOS/patchelf/"
"archive/0.8.tar.gz\n"
"079agjlv0hrv7fxnx9ngipx14gyncbkllxrp9cccnh3a50fxcmy7\n"
"/nix/store/19zrmhm3m40xxaw81c8cqm6aljgrnwj2-0.8.tar.gz\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

