msgid "into the users’ login scripts."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/multi-user.md:63
msgid "Restricting access"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/multi-user.md:65
msgid ""
"To limit which users can perform Nix operations, you can use the permissions "
"on the directory `/nix/var/nix/daemon-socket`. For instance, if you want to "
"restrict the use of Nix to the members of a group called `nix-users`, do"
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/multi-user.md:75
msgid ""
"This way, users who are not in the `nix-users` group cannot connect to the "
"Unix domain socket `/nix/var/nix/daemon-socket/socket`, so they cannot "
"perform Nix operations."
msgstr ""

#: source/installation/single-user.md:1
msgid "Single-User Mode"
msgstr "單使用者模式"

#: source/installation/single-user.md:3
msgid ""
"In single-user mode, all Nix operations that access the database in `prefix/"
"var/nix/db` or modify the Nix store in `prefix/store` must be performed "
"under the user ID that owns those directories. This is typically root. (If "
"you install from RPM packages, that’s in fact the default ownership.) "
"However, on single-user machines, it is often convenient to `chown` those "
"directories to your normal user account so that you don’t have to `su` to "
"root all the time."
msgstr ""

