#: source/language/builtins.md:40
msgid ""
"On the flip side, this means they have accumulated a few quirks that Nix is "
"unable to change, but a library like Nixpkgs `lib` _can_ improve, replace or "
"deprecate those behaviors, because its sources are pinned where "
"reproducibility matters."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:44
msgid ""
"So while it is not wrong to use `builtins` directly, for instance in small "
"Nixpkgs-independent projects, you will have a better experience using a "
"library like `lib` as your primary source of functions, as it hides "
"problematic functions, fixes up others, and helps you improve your code by "
"means of future deprecations, which are still sufficiently rare."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:59
msgid "Abort Nix expression evaluation and print the error message _s_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:68
msgid "Return the sum of the numbers _e1_ and _e2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:77
msgid ""
"Create a copy of the given string where a single [constant](../language/"
"string-context.md#string-context-constant) string context element is turned "
"into a [derivation deep](../language/string-context.md#string-context-"
"element-derivation-deep) string context element."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:83
msgid ""
"The store path that is the constant string context element should point to a "
"valid derivation, and end in `.drv`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:85
msgid ""
"The original string context element must not be empty or have multiple "
"elements, and it must not have any other type of element other than a "
"constant or derivation deep element. The latter is supported so this "
"function is idempotent."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:88
msgid ""
"This is the opposite of [`builtins.unsafeDiscardOutputDependency`](#builtins-"
"unsafeDiscardOutputDependency)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:97
msgid ""
"Evaluate _context_, which can be coerced to a string, and append it to any "
"error or stack traces displayed while evaluating _value_. Then return "
"_value_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:101
msgid ""
"This function is useful for providing helpful context in complex Nix "
"expressions when the evaluation of _value_ fails. The additional context is "
"applied when evaluating _value_ itself fails, not when attributes or "
"elements of _value_ are evaluated."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:106
msgid ""
"For example, the module system from nixpkgs uses this to show the relevant "
"information about the options that were evaluating when an error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:110
msgid ""
"```nix-repl\n"
"nix-repl> addErrorContext \"while evaluating foo\" (throw \"bar\")\n"
"error:\n"
"       … while evaluating foo\n"
"\n"
"       … while calling the 'throw' builtin\n"
"         at «string»:1:56:\n"
"            1| with builtins; addErrorContext \"while evaluating foo\" "
"(throw \"bar\")\n"
"             |                                                        ^\n"
"\n"
"       error: bar\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:130
msgid ""
"Return `true` if the function _pred_ returns `true` for all elements of "
"_list_, and `false` otherwise. Short-circuits and does not evaluate elements "
"that appear later in the list if `pred` evaluates to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:141
msgid ""
"Return `true` if the function _pred_ returns `true` for at least one element "
"of _list_, and `false` otherwise. Short-circuits and does not evaluate "
"elements that appear later in the list if `pred` evaluates to `true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:152
msgid ""
"Return the names of the attributes in the set _set_ in an alphabetically "
"sorted list. For instance, `builtins.attrNames { y = 1; x = \"foo\"; }` "
"evaluates to `[ \"x\" \"y\" ]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:156 source/language/builtins.md:168
msgid ""
"Has `O(n log n)` time complexity, where `n` is number of attributes in the "
"_set_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:165
msgid ""
"Return the values of the attributes in the set _set_ in the order "
"corresponding to the sorted attribute names."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:177
msgid ""
"Return the _base name_ of either a [path value](../language/types.md#type-"
"path) _x_ or a string _x_, depending on which type is passed, and according "
"to the following rules."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:179
msgid ""
"For a path value, the _base name_ is considered to be the part of the path "
"after the last directory separator, including any file extensions. This is "
"the simple case, as path values don't have trailing slashes."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:182
msgid ""
"When the argument is a string, a more involved logic applies. If the string "
"ends with a `/`, only this one final slash is removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:184
msgid ""
"After this, the _base name_ is returned as previously described, assuming `/"
"` as the directory separator. (Note that evaluation must be platform "
"independent.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:186
msgid ""
"This is somewhat similar to the [GNU `basename`](https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/coreutils/manual/html_node/basename-invocation.html) command, but "
"GNU `basename` strips any number of trailing slashes."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:195
msgid "Return the bitwise AND of the integers _e1_ and _e2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:204
msgid "Return the bitwise OR of the integers _e1_ and _e2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:213
msgid "Return the bitwise XOR of the integers _e1_ and _e2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:222
msgid ""
"In debug mode (enabled using `--debugger`), pause Nix expression evaluation "
"and enter the REPL. Otherwise, return the argument `v`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:232
msgid "Contains all the built-in functions and values."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:234
msgid ""
"Since built-in functions were added over time, [testing for attributes](./"
"operators.md#has-attribute) in `builtins` can be used for graceful fallback "
"on older Nix installations:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:248
msgid ""
"Collect each attribute named _attr_ from a list of attribute sets.  Attrsets "
"that don't contain the named attribute are ignored. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:252
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.catAttrs \"a\" [{a = 1;} {b = 0;} {a = 2;}]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:256
msgid "evaluates to `[1 2]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:258
msgid "Has `O(n)` time complexity, where `n` is the size of the _list_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:267
msgid ""
"Rounds and converts _number_ to the next higher NixInt value if possible, "
"i.e. `ceil *number* >= *number*` and `ceil *number* - *number* < 1`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:270
msgid ""
"An evaluation error is thrown, if there exists no such NixInt value `ceil "
"*number*`. Due to bugs in previous Nix versions an evaluation error might be "
"thrown, if the datatype of _number_ is a NixInt and if `*number* < "
"-9007199254740992` or `*number* > 9007199254740992`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:274
msgid ""
"If the datatype of _number_ is neither a NixInt (signed 64-bit integer) nor "
"a NixFloat (IEEE-754 double-precision floating-point number), an evaluation "
"error is thrown."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:284
msgid ""
"Compare two strings representing versions and return `-1` if version _s1_ is "
"older than version _s2_, `0` if they are the same, and `1` if _s1_ is newer "
"than _s2_. The version comparison algorithm is the same as the one used by "
"[`nix-env -u`](../command-ref/nix-env/upgrade.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:297
msgid "Concatenate a list of lists into a single list."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:306
msgid ""
"This function is equivalent to `builtins.concatLists (map f list)` but is "
"more efficient."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:316
msgid ""
"Concatenate a list of strings with a separator between each element, e.g. "
"`concatStringsSep \"/\" [\"usr\" \"local\" \"bin\"] == \"usr/local/bin\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:327
msgid ""
"Return the specified representation of a hash string, based on the "
"attributes presented in _args_:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:331
msgid "The hash to be converted. The hash format is detected automatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:334
msgid "`hashAlgo`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:336
msgid "The algorithm used to create the hash. Must be one of"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:337
msgid "`\"md5\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:338
msgid "`\"sha1\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:339
msgid "`\"sha256\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:340
msgid "`\"sha512\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:342
msgid ""
"The attribute may be omitted when `hash` is an [SRI hash](https://www.w3.org/"
"TR/SRI/#the-integrity-attribute) or when the hash is prefixed with the hash "
"algorithm name followed by a colon. That `<hashAlgo>:<hashBody>` syntax is "
"supported for backwards compatibility with existing tooling."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:345
msgid "`toHashFormat`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:347
msgid "The format of the resulting hash. Must be one of"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:348
msgid "`\"base16\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:349
msgid "`\"nix32\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:350
msgid "`\"base32\"` (deprecated alias for `\"nix32\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:351
msgid "`\"base64\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:352
msgid "`\"sri\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:354
msgid ""
"The result hash is the _toHashFormat_ representation of the hash _hash_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:358
msgid "Convert a SHA256 hash in Base16 to SRI:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:360
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.convertHash {\n"
"  hash = "
"\"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\";\n"
"  toHashFormat = \"sri\";\n"
"  hashAlgo = \"sha256\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:368 source/language/builtins.md:394
msgid ""
"    \"sha256-47DEQpj8HBSa+/TImW+5JCeuQeRkm5NMpJWZG3hSuFU=\"\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:372
msgid "Convert a SHA256 hash in SRI to Base16:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:374
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.convertHash {\n"
"  hash = \"sha256-47DEQpj8HBSa+/TImW+5JCeuQeRkm5NMpJWZG3hSuFU=\";\n"
"  toHashFormat = \"base16\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:381
msgid ""
"    \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\"\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:385
msgid "Convert a hash in the form `<hashAlgo>:<hashBody>` in Base16 to SRI:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:387
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.convertHash {\n"
"  hash = "
"\"sha256:e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\";\n"
"  toHashFormat = \"sri\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:403
msgid ""
"The value of the [`eval-system`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-eval-"
"system) or else [`system`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-system) "
"configuration option."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:409
msgid ""
"It can be used to set the `system` attribute for [`builtins.derivation`](../"
"language/derivations.md) such that the resulting derivation can be built on "
"the same system that evaluates the Nix expression:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:418
msgid ""
"It can be overridden in order to create derivations for different system "
"than the current one:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:420
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-instantiate --system \"mips64-linux\" --eval --expr "
"'builtins.currentSystem'\n"
"\"mips64-linux\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:427 source/language/builtins.md:456
#: source/language/builtins.md:2737
msgid ""
"Not available in [pure evaluation mode](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"pure-eval)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:436
msgid ""
"Return the [Unix time](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unix_time) at first "
"evaluation. Repeated references to that name re-use the initially obtained "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:452
msgid ""
"The [store path](../store/store-path.md) of a derivation depending on "
"`currentTime` differs for each evaluation, unless both evaluate "
"`builtins.currentTime` in the same second."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:465
msgid ""
"This is like `seq e1 e2`, except that _e1_ is evaluated _deeply_: if it’s a "
"list or set, its elements or attributes are also evaluated recursively."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:476
msgid ""
"Return the directory part of the string _s_, that is, everything before the "
"final slash in the string. This is similar to the GNU `dirname` command."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:487
msgid "Return the quotient of the numbers _e1_ and _e2_."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:496
msgid ""
"Return `true` if a value equal to _x_ occurs in the list _xs_, and `false` "
"otherwise. Short-circuits and does not evaluate elements that occur in the "
"list after the first match."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:507
msgid ""
"Return element _n_ from the list _xs_. Elements are counted starting from 0. "
"A fatal error occurs if the index is out of bounds."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:517 source/language/builtins.md:2276
#: source/language/builtins.md:3067
msgid "Primitive value."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:519 source/language/builtins.md:3069
msgid ""
"It can be returned by [comparison operators](../language/"
"operators.md#comparison) and used in [conditional expressions](../language/"
"syntax.md#conditionals)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:524
msgid "The name `false` is not special, and can be shadowed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:540
msgid ""
"This function is only available if the [`fetch-closure` experimental feature]"
"(../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-fetch-closure) is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:542 source/language/builtins.md:886
#: source/language/builtins.md:1505 source/language/builtins.md:1782
#: source/language/builtins.md:2296 source/language/builtins.md:2349
msgid ""
"For example, include the following in [`nix.conf`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:548
msgid ""
"Fetch a store path [closure](../glossary.md#gloss-closure) from a binary "
"cache, and return the store path as a string with context."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:550
msgid ""
"This function can be invoked in three ways that we will discuss in order of "
"preference."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:552
msgid "**Fetch a content-addressed store path**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:556
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchClosure {\n"
"  fromStore = \"https://cache.nixos.org\";\n"
"  fromPath = /nix/store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:563
msgid ""
"This is the simplest invocation, and it does not require the user of the "
"expression to configure [`trusted-public-keys`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys) to ensure their authenticity."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:565
msgid ""
"If your store path is [input addressed](../glossary.md#gloss-input-addressed-"
"store-object) instead of content addressed, consider the other two "
"invocations."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:567
msgid ""
"**Fetch any store path and rewrite it to a fully content-addressed store "
"path**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:571
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchClosure {\n"
"  fromStore = \"https://cache.nixos.org\";\n"
"  fromPath = /nix/store/nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1;\n"
"  toPath = /nix/store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:579
msgid ""
"This example fetches `/nix/store/r2jd...` from the specified binary cache, "
"and rewrites it into the content-addressed store path `/nix/store/ldbh...`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:583
msgid ""
"Like the previous example, no extra configuration or privileges are required."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:585
msgid ""
"To find out the correct value for `toPath` given a `fromPath`, use [`nix "
"store make-content-addressed`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-store-make-"
"content-addressed.md):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:588
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix store make-content-addressed --from https://cache.nixos.org /nix/store/"
"nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1\n"
"rewrote '/nix/store/nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1' to '/nix/"
"store/ldbhlwhh39wha58rm61bkiiwm6j7211j-git-2.33.1'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:593
msgid ""
"Alternatively, set `toPath = \"\"` and find the correct `toPath` in the "
"error message."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:595
msgid "**Fetch an input-addressed store path as is**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:599
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.fetchClosure {\n"
"  fromStore = \"https://cache.nixos.org\";\n"
"  fromPath = /nix/store/nph9br6y2dmciy6q3dj3fwk2brdlr4gh-git-2.33.1;\n"
"  inputAddressed = true;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:607
msgid ""
"It is possible to fetch an [input-addressed store path](../glossary.md#gloss-"
"input-addressed-store-object) and return it as is. However, this is the "
"least preferred way of invoking `fetchClosure`, because it requires that the "
"input-addressed paths are trusted by the Nix configuration."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:610
msgid "**`builtins.storePath`**"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:612
msgid ""
"`fetchClosure` is similar to [`builtins.storePath`](#builtins-storePath) in "
"that it allows you to use a previously built store path in a Nix expression. "
"However, `fetchClosure` is more reproducible because it specifies a binary "
"cache from which the path can be fetched. Also, using content-addressed "
"store paths does not require users to configure [`trusted-public-keys`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-trusted-public-keys) to ensure their "
"authenticity."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:623
msgid ""
"Fetch a path from git. _args_ can be a URL, in which case the HEAD of the "
"repo at that URL is fetched. Otherwise, it can be an attribute with the "
"following attributes (all except `url` optional):"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:627 source/language/builtins.md:1284
msgid "`url`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:629
msgid ""
"The [Git URL](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-clone#_git_urls) of the repo. SCP-"
"like syntax is supported, but relative paths are rewritten to absolute ones. "
"For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:632
msgid "`git@github.com:repo/path` becomes `ssh://git@github.com/repo/path`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:636
msgid "`name` (default: `source`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:638
msgid "The name of the directory the repo should be exported to in the store."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:640
msgid "`rev` (default: _the tip of `ref`_)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:642
msgid ""
"The [Git revision](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-rev-"
"parse#_specifying_revisions) to fetch. This is typically a commit hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:647
msgid "`ref` (default: `HEAD`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:649
msgid ""
"The [Git reference](https://git-scm.com/book/en/v2/Git-Internals-Git-"
"References) under which to look for the requested revision. This is often a "
"branch or tag name."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:654 source/language/builtins.md:687
msgid "This option has no effect once `shallow` cloning is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:656
msgid ""
"By default, the `ref` value is prefixed with `refs/heads/`. As of 2.3.0, Nix "
"doesn't prefix `refs/heads/` if `ref` starts with `refs/`."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:659
msgid "`submodules` (default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:661
msgid ""
"A Boolean parameter that specifies whether submodules should be checked out."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:663
msgid "`exportIgnore` (default: `true`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:665
msgid ""
"A Boolean parameter that specifies whether `export-ignore` from "
"`.gitattributes` should be applied. This approximates part of the `git "
"archive` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:668
msgid ""
"Enabling this option is not recommended because it is unknown whether the "
"Git developers commit to the reproducibility of `export-ignore` in newer Git "
"versions."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:670
msgid "`shallow` (default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:672 source/language/builtins.md:1072
msgid ""
"Make a shallow clone when fetching the Git tree. When this is enabled, the "
"options `ref` and `allRefs` have no effect anymore."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:675
msgid "`lfs` (default: `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:677
msgid ""
"A boolean that when `true` specifies that [Git LFS](https://git-lfs.com/) "
"files should be fetched."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:681
msgid "`allRefs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:683
msgid ""
"Whether to fetch all references (eg. branches and tags) of the repository. "
"With this argument being true, it's possible to load a `rev` from _any_ "
"`ref`. (by default only `rev`s from the specified `ref` are supported)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:689
msgid ""
"`verifyCommit` (default: `true` if `publicKey` or `publicKeys` are provided, "
"otherwise `false`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:691
msgid ""
"Whether to check `rev` for a signature matching `publicKey` or `publicKeys`. "
"If `verifyCommit` is enabled, then `fetchGit` cannot use a local repository "
"with uncommitted changes. Requires the [`verified-fetches` experimental "
"feature](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-verified-"
"fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:695
msgid "`publicKey`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:697
msgid ""
"The public key against which `rev` is verified if `verifyCommit` is enabled. "
"Requires the [`verified-fetches` experimental feature](../development/"
"experimental-features.md#xp-feature-verified-fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:700
msgid "`keytype` (default: `\"ssh-ed25519\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:702
msgid "The key type of `publicKey`. Possible values:"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:704
msgid "`\"ssh-dsa\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:705
msgid "`\"ssh-ecdsa\"`"
msgstr ""

#: source/language/builtins.md:706
