#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:1
msgid "Release 0.7 (2005-01-12)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:3
msgid ""
"Binary patching. When upgrading components using pre-built binaries (through "
"nix-pull / nix-channel), Nix can automatically download and apply binary "
"patches to already installed components instead of full downloads. Patching "
"is “smart”: if there is a _sequence_ of patches to an installed component, "
"Nix will use it. Patches are currently generated automatically between "
"Nixpkgs (pre-)releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:10
msgid "Simplifications to the substitute mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:12
msgid "Nix-pull now stores downloaded manifests in `/nix/var/nix/manifests`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.7.md:15
msgid ""
"Metadata on files in the Nix store is canonicalised after builds: the last-"
"modified timestamp is set to 0 (00:00:00 1/1/1970), the mode is set to 0444 "
"or 0555 (readable and possibly executable by all; setuid/setgid bits are "
"dropped), and the group is set to the default. This ensures that the result "
"of a build and an installation through a substitute is the same; and that "
"timestamp dependencies are revealed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:1
msgid "Release 0.8 (2005-04-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:3
msgid ""
"NOTE: the hashing scheme in Nix 0.8 changed (as detailed below). As a "
"result, `nix-pull` manifests and channels built for Nix 0.7 and below will "
"not work anymore. However, the Nix expression language has not changed, so "
"you can still build from source. Also, existing user environments continue "
"to work. Nix 0.8 will automatically upgrade the database schema of previous "
"installations when it is first run."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:10
msgid "If you get the error message"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:15
msgid "you should delete previously downloaded manifests:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:19
msgid "If `nix-channel` gives the error message"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:21
msgid ""
"    manifest `http://catamaran.labs.cs.uu.nl/dist/nix/channels/[channel]/"
"MANIFEST'\n"
"    is too old (i.e., for Nix <= 0.7)\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:24
msgid ""
"then you should unsubscribe from the offending channel (`nix-channel --"
"remove URL`; leave out `/MANIFEST`), and subscribe to the same URL, with "
"`channels` replaced by `channels-v3` (e.g., <http://catamaran.labs.cs.uu.nl/"
"dist/nix/channels-v3/nixpkgs-unstable>)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:30
msgid "Nix 0.8 has the following improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:32
msgid ""
"The cryptographic hashes used in store paths are now 160 bits long, but "
"encoded in base-32 so that they are still only 32 characters long (e.g., `/"
"nix/store/csw87wag8bqlqk7ipllbwypb14xainap-atk-1.9.0`). (This is actually a "
"160 bit truncation of a SHA-256 hash.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:38
msgid ""
"Big cleanups and simplifications of the basic store semantics. The notion of "
"“closure store expressions” is gone (and so is the notion of “successors”); "
"the file system references of a store path are now just stored in the "
"database."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:43
msgid "For instance, given any store path, you can query its closure:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:48
msgid ""
"Also, Nix now remembers for each store path the derivation that built it "
"(the “deriver”):"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:54
msgid "So to see the build-time dependencies, you can do"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:58
msgid "or, in a nicer format:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:62
msgid ""
"File system references are also stored in reverse. For instance, you can "
"query all paths that directly or indirectly use a certain Glibc:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:68
msgid ""
"The concept of fixed-output derivations has been formalised. Previously, "
"functions such as `fetchurl` in Nixpkgs used a hack (namely, explicitly "
"specifying a store path hash) to prevent changes to, say, the URL of the "
"file from propagating upwards through the dependency graph, causing rebuilds "
"of everything. This can now be done cleanly by specifying the `outputHash` "
"and `outputHashAlgo` attributes. Nix itself checks that the content of the "
"output has the specified hash. (This is important for maintaining certain "
"invariants necessary for future work on secure shared stores.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:78
msgid ""
"One-click installation :-) It is now possible to install any top-level "
"component in Nixpkgs directly, through the web — see, e.g., <http://"
"catamaran.labs.cs.uu.nl/dist/nixpkgs-0.8/>. All you have to do is associate "
"`/nix/bin/nix-install-package` with the MIME type `application/nix-package` "
"(or the extension `.nixpkg`), and clicking on a package link will cause it "
"to be installed, with all appropriate dependencies. If you just want to "
"install some specific application, this is easier than subscribing to a "
"channel."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:87
msgid ""
"`nix-store -r         PATHS` now builds all the derivations PATHS in "
"parallel. Previously it did them sequentially (though exploiting possible "
"parallelism between subderivations). This is nice for build farms."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:92
msgid "`nix-channel` has new operations `--list` and `--remove`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:94
msgid "New ways of installing components into user environments:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:96
msgid "Copy from another user environment:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:100
msgid ""
"Install a store derivation directly (bypassing the Nix expression language "
"entirely):"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:105
msgid ""
"(This is used to implement `nix-install-package`, which is therefore immune "
"to evolution in the Nix expression language.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:108
msgid "Install an already built store path directly:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:112
msgid ""
"Install the result of a Nix expression specified as a command-line argument:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:117
msgid ""
"The difference with the normal installation mode is that `-E` does not use "
"the `name` attributes of derivations. Therefore, this can be used to "
"disambiguate multiple derivations with the same name."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:122
msgid ""
"A hash of the contents of a store path is now stored in the database after a "
"successful build. This allows you to check whether store paths have been "
"tampered with: `nix-store         --verify --check-contents`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:127
msgid ""
"Implemented a concurrent garbage collector. It is now always safe to run the "
"garbage collector, even if other Nix operations are happening simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:131
msgid ""
"However, there can still be GC races if you use `nix-instantiate` and `nix-"
"store                 --realise` directly to build things. To prevent races, "
"use the `--add-root` flag of those commands."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:136
msgid ""
"The garbage collector now finally deletes paths in the right order (i.e., "
"topologically sorted under the “references” relation), thus making it safe "
"to interrupt the collector without risking a store that violates the closure "
"invariant."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:141
msgid ""
"Likewise, the substitute mechanism now downloads files in the right order, "
"thus preserving the closure invariant at all times."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:144
msgid ""
"The result of `nix-build` is now registered as a root of the garbage "
"collector. If the `./result` link is deleted, the GC root disappears "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:148
msgid ""
"The behaviour of the garbage collector can be changed globally by setting "
"options in `/nix/etc/nix/nix.conf`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:151
msgid ""
"`gc-keep-derivations` specifies whether deriver links should be followed "
"when searching for live paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:154
msgid ""
"`gc-keep-outputs` specifies whether outputs of derivations should be "
"followed when searching for live paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:157
msgid ""
"`env-keep-derivations` specifies whether user environments should store the "
"paths of derivations when they are added (thus keeping the derivations "
"alive)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:161
msgid "New `nix-env` query flags `--drv-path` and `--out-path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.md:163
msgid ""
"`fetchurl` allows SHA-1 and SHA-256 in addition to MD5. Just specify the "
"attribute `sha1` or `sha256` instead of `md5`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.1.md:1
msgid "Release 0.8.1 (2005-04-13)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.1.md:3
msgid "This is a bug fix release."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.1.md:5
msgid "Patch downloading was broken."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.8.1.md:7
msgid ""
"The garbage collector would not delete paths that had references from "
"invalid (but substitutable) paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:1
msgid "Release 0.9 (2005-09-16)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:3
msgid ""
"NOTE: this version of Nix uses Berkeley DB 4.3 instead of 4.2. The database "
"is upgraded automatically, but you should be careful not to use old versions "
"of Nix that still use Berkeley DB 4.2. In particular, if you use a Nix "
"installed through Nix, you should run"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:12
msgid ""
"Unpacking of patch sequences is much faster now since we no longer do "
"redundant unpacking and repacking of intermediate paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:15
msgid "Nix now uses Berkeley DB 4.3."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:17
msgid ""
"The `derivation` primitive is lazier. Attributes of dependent derivations "
"can mutually refer to each other (as long as there are no data dependencies "
"on the `outPath` and `drvPath` attributes computed by `derivation`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:22
msgid ""
"For example, the expression `derivation         attrs` now evaluates to "
"(essentially)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:25
msgid ""
"    attrs // {\n"
"      type = \"derivation\";\n"
"      outPath = derivation! attrs;\n"
"      drvPath = derivation! attrs;\n"
"    }\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:31
msgid ""
"where `derivation!` is a primop that does the actual derivation "
"instantiation (i.e., it does what `derivation` used to do). The advantage is "
"that it allows commands such as `nix-env -qa` and `nix-env -i` to be much "
"faster since they no longer need to instantiate all derivations, just the "
"`name` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:37
msgid ""
"Also, it allows derivations to cyclically reference each other, for example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:40
msgid ""
"    webServer = derivation {\n"
"      ...\n"
"      hostName = \"svn.cs.uu.nl\";\n"
"      services = [svnService];\n"
"    };\n"
"     \n"
"    svnService = derivation {\n"
"      ...\n"
"      hostName = webServer.hostName;\n"
"    };\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:51
msgid "Previously, this would yield a black hole (infinite recursion)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:53
msgid ""
"`nix-build` now defaults to using `./default.nix` if no Nix expression is "
"specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:56
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate`, when applied to a Nix expression that evaluates to a "
"function, will call the function automatically if all its arguments have "
"defaults."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:60
msgid ""
"Nix now uses libtool to build dynamic libraries. This reduces the size of "
"executables."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:63
msgid ""
"A new list concatenation operator `++`. For example, `[1 2 3] ++ [4 "
"5         6]` evaluates to `[1 2 3 4 5         6]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:68
msgid ""
"Some currently undocumented primops to support low-level build management "
"using Nix (i.e., using Nix as a Make replacement). See the commit messages "
"for `r3578` and `r3580`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.md:72
msgid "Various bug fixes and performance improvements."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.1.md:1
msgid "Release 0.9.1 (2005-09-20)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.1.md:3
msgid ""
"This bug fix release addresses a problem with the ATerm library when the `--"
"with-aterm` flag in `configure` was _not_ used."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.2.md:1
msgid "Release 0.9.2 (2005-09-21)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.2.md:3
msgid "This bug fix release fixes two problems on Mac OS X:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.2.md:5
msgid ""
"If Nix was linked against statically linked versions of the ATerm or "
"Berkeley DB library, there would be dynamic link errors at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-0.9.2.md:8
msgid ""
"`nix-pull` and `nix-push` intermittently failed due to race conditions "
"involving pipes and child processes with error messages such as `open2: "
"open(GLOB(0x180b2e4), >&=9) failed: Bad         file descriptor at /nix/bin/"
"nix-pull line 77` (issue `NIX-14`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:1
msgid "Release 1.0 (2012-05-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:3
msgid ""
"There have been numerous improvements and bug fixes since the previous "
"release. Here are the most significant:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:6
msgid ""
"Nix can now optionally use the Boehm garbage collector. This significantly "
"reduces the Nix evaluator’s memory footprint, especially when evaluating "
"large NixOS system configurations. It can be enabled using the `--enable-gc` "
"configure option."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:11
msgid ""
"Nix now uses SQLite for its database. This is faster and more flexible than "
"the old _ad hoc_ format. SQLite is also used to cache the manifests in `/nix/"
"var/nix/manifests`, resulting in a significant speedup."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:16
msgid ""
"Nix now has an search path for expressions. The search path is set using the "
"environment variable `NIX_PATH` and the `-I` command line option. In Nix "
"expressions, paths between angle brackets are used to specify files that "
"must be looked up in the search path. For instance, the expression `<nixpkgs/"
"default.nix>` looks for a file `nixpkgs/default.nix` relative to every "
"element in the search path."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:23
msgid ""
"The new command `nix-build --run-env` builds all dependencies of a "
"derivation, then starts a shell in an environment containing all variables "
"from the derivation. This is useful for reproducing the environment of a "
"derivation for development."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:28
msgid ""
"The new command `nix-store --verify-path` verifies that the contents of a "
"store path have not changed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:31
msgid ""
"The new command `nix-store --print-env` prints out the environment of a "
"derivation in a format that can be evaluated by a shell."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:34
msgid ""
"Attribute names can now be arbitrary strings. For instance, you can write "
"`{ \"foo-1.2\" = …; \"bla bla\" = …; }.\"bla                 bla\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:38
msgid ""
"Attribute selection can now provide a default value using the `or` operator. "
"For instance, the expression `x.y.z or e` evaluates to the attribute `x.y.z` "
"if it exists, and `e` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:42
msgid ""
"The right-hand side of the `?` operator can now be an attribute path, e.g., "
"`attrs ?                 a.b.c`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:46
msgid ""
"On Linux, Nix will now make files in the Nix store immutable on filesystems "
"that support it. This prevents accidental modification of files in the store "
"by the root user."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:50
msgid ""
"Nix has preliminary support for derivations with multiple outputs. This is "
"useful because it allows parts of a package to be deployed and garbage-"
"collected separately. For instance, development parts of a package such as "
"header files or static libraries would typically not be part of the closure "
"of an application, resulting in reduced disk usage and installation time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:57
msgid ""
"The Nix store garbage collector is faster and holds the global lock for a "
"shorter amount of time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:60
msgid ""
"The option `--timeout` (corresponding to the configuration setting `build-"
"timeout`) allows you to set an absolute timeout on builds — if a build runs "
"for more than the given number of seconds, it is terminated. This is useful "
"for recovering automatically from builds that are stuck in an infinite loop "
"but keep producing output, and for which `--max-silent-time` is ineffective."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.0.md:67
msgid "Nix development has moved to GitHub (<https://github.com/NixOS/nix>)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:1
msgid "Release 1.1 (2012-07-18)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:5
msgid ""
"On Linux, when doing a chroot build, Nix now uses various namespace features "
"provided by the Linux kernel to improve build isolation. Namely:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:9
msgid ""
"The private network namespace ensures that builders cannot talk to the "
"outside world (or vice versa): each build only sees a private loopback "
"interface. This also means that two concurrent builds can listen on the same "
"port (e.g. as part of a test) without conflicting with each other."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:15
msgid ""
"The PID namespace causes each build to start as PID 1. Processes outside of "
"the chroot are not visible to those on the inside. On the other hand, "
"processes inside the chroot _are_ visible from the outside (though with "
"different PIDs)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:20
msgid ""
"The IPC namespace prevents the builder from communicating with outside "
"processes using SysV IPC mechanisms (shared memory, message queues, "
"semaphores). It also ensures that all IPC objects are destroyed when the "
"builder exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:25
msgid ""
"The UTS namespace ensures that builders see a hostname of `localhost` rather "
"than the actual hostname."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:28
msgid ""
"The private mount namespace was already used by Nix to ensure that the bind-"
"mounts used to set up the chroot are cleaned up automatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:32
msgid ""
"Build logs are now compressed using `bzip2`. The command `nix-"
"store                 -l` decompresses them on the fly. This can be disabled "
"by setting the option `build-compress-log` to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:36
msgid ""
"The creation of build logs in `/nix/var/log/nix/drvs` can be disabled by "
"setting the new option `build-keep-log` to `false`. This is useful, for "
"instance, for Hydra build machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:40
msgid ""
"Nix now reserves some space in `/nix/var/nix/db/reserved` to ensure that the "
"garbage collector can run successfully if the disk is full. This is "
"necessary because SQLite transactions fail if the disk is full."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:45
msgid ""
"Added a basic `fetchurl` function. This is not intended to replace the "
"`fetchurl` in Nixpkgs, but is useful for bootstrapping; e.g., it will allow "
"us to get rid of the bootstrap binaries in the Nixpkgs source tree and "
"download them instead. You can use it by doing `import <nix/fetchurl.nix> "
"{ url =                 url; sha256 =                 \"hash\"; }`. (Shea "
"Levy)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:53
msgid "Improved RPM spec file. (Michel Alexandre Salim)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:55
msgid ""
"Support for on-demand socket-based activation in the Nix daemon with "
"`systemd`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:58
msgid "Added a manpage for nix.conf5."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.1.md:60
msgid ""
"When using the Nix daemon, the `-s` flag in `nix-env -qa` is now much faster."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:1
msgid "Release 1.10 (2015-09-03)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:3
msgid ""
"This is primarily a bug fix release. It also has a number of new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:6
msgid ""
"A number of builtin functions have been added to reduce Nixpkgs/NixOS "
"evaluation time and memory consumption: `all`, `any`, `concatStringsSep`, "
"`foldl’`, `genList`, `replaceStrings`, `sort`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:10
msgid "The garbage collector is more robust when the disk is full."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:12
msgid ""
"Nix supports a new API for building derivations that doesn’t require a "
"`.drv` file to be present on disk; it only requires an in-memory "
"representation of the derivation. This is used by the Hydra continuous build "
"system to make remote builds more efficient."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:17
msgid ""
"The function `<nix/fetchurl.nix>` now uses a _builtin_ builder (i.e. it "
"doesn’t require starting an external process; the download is performed by "
"Nix itself). This ensures that derivation paths don’t change when Nix is "
"upgraded, and obviates the need for ugly hacks to support chroot execution."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:23
msgid ""
"`--version -v` now prints some configuration information, in particular what "
"compile-time optional features are enabled, and the paths of various "
"directories."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:27
msgid "Build users have their supplementary groups set correctly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.10.md:29
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Eelco Dolstra, Guillaume Maudoux, Iwan "
"Aucamp, Jaka Hudoklin, Kirill Elagin, Ludovic Courtès, Manolis Ragkousis, "
"Nicolas B. Pierron and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:1
msgid "Release 1.11 (2016-01-19)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:6
msgid ""
"`nix-prefetch-url` can now download URLs specified in a Nix expression. For "
"example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:11
msgid ""
"will prefetch the file specified by the `fetchurl` call in the attribute "
"`hello.src` from the Nix expression in the current directory, and print the "
"cryptographic hash of the resulting file on stdout. This differs from `nix-"
"build -A                 hello.src` in that it doesn't verify the hash, and "
"is thus useful when you’re updating a Nix expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:18
msgid ""
"You can also prefetch the result of functions that unpack a tarball, such as "
"`fetchFromGitHub`. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:21
msgid ""
"    $ nix-prefetch-url --unpack https://github.com/NixOS/patchelf/archive/"
"0.8.tar.gz\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:23
msgid "or from a Nix expression:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:27
msgid ""
"The builtin function `<nix/fetchurl.nix>` now supports downloading and "
"unpacking NARs. This removes the need to have multiple downloads in the "
"Nixpkgs stdenv bootstrap process (like a separate busybox binary for Linux, "
"or curl/mkdir/sh/bzip2 for Darwin). Now all those files can be combined into "
"a single NAR, optionally compressed using `xz`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:34
msgid ""
"Nix now supports SHA-512 hashes for verifying fixed-output derivations, and "
"in `builtins.hashString`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:37
msgid ""
"The new flag `--option build-repeat                         N` will cause "
"every build to be executed _N_+1 times. If the build output differs between "
"any round, the build is rejected, and the output paths are not registered as "
"valid. This is primarily useful to verify build determinism. (We already had "
"a `--check` option to repeat a previously succeeded build. However, with `--"
"check`, non-deterministic builds are registered in the DB. Preventing that "
"is useful for Hydra to ensure that non-deterministic builds don't end up "
"getting published to the binary cache.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:47
msgid ""
"The options `--check` and `--option                         build-repeat N`, "
"if they detect a difference between two runs of the same derivation and `-K` "
"is given, will make the output of the other run available under `store-path-"
"check`. This makes it easier to investigate the non-determinism using tools "
"like `diffoscope`, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:68
msgid "Improved FreeBSD support."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:70
msgid "`nix-env -qa --xml --meta` now prints license information."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:72
msgid ""
"The maximum number of parallel TCP connections that the binary cache "
"substituter will use has been decreased from 150 to 25. This should prevent "
"upsetting some broken NAT routers, and also improves performance."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:77
msgid ""
"All \"chroot\"-containing strings got renamed to \"sandbox\". In particular, "
"some Nix options got renamed, but the old names are still accepted as lower-"
"priority aliases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.md:81
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Anders Claesson, Anthony Cowley, Bjørn "
"Forsman, Brian McKenna, Danny Wilson, davidak, Eelco Dolstra, Fabian "
"Schmitthenner, FrankHB, Ilya Novoselov, janus, Jim Garrison, John Ericson, "
"Jude Taylor, Ludovic Courtès, Manuel Jacob, Mathnerd314, Pascal Wittmann, "
"Peter Simons, Philip Potter, Preston Bennes, Rommel M. Martinez, Sander van "
"der Burg, Shea Levy, Tim Cuthbertson, Tuomas Tynkkynen, Utku Demir and "
"Vladimír Čunát."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.10.md:1
msgid "Release 1.11.10 (2017-06-12)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.10.md:3
msgid ""
"This release fixes a security bug in Nix’s “build user” build isolation "
"mechanism. Previously, Nix builders had the ability to create setuid "
"binaries owned by a `nixbld` user. Such a binary could then be used by an "
"attacker to assume a `nixbld` identity and interfere with subsequent builds "
"running under the same UID."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.10.md:9
msgid ""
"To prevent this issue, Nix now disallows builders to create setuid and "
"setgid binaries. On Linux, this is done using a seccomp BPF filter. Note "
"that this imposes a small performance penalty (e.g. 1% when building GNU "
"Hello). Using seccomp, we now also prevent the creation of extended "
"attributes and POSIX ACLs since these cannot be represented in the NAR "
"format and (in the case of POSIX ACLs) allow bypassing regular Nix store "
"permissions. On macOS, the restriction is implemented using the existing "
"sandbox mechanism, which now uses a minimal “allow all except the creation "
"of setuid/setgid binaries” profile when regular sandboxing is disabled. On "
"other platforms, the “build user” mechanism is now disabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.11.10.md:21
msgid "Thanks go to Linus Heckemann for discovering and reporting this bug."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:1
msgid "Release 1.2 (2012-12-06)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:3
msgid "This release has the following improvements and changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:5
msgid ""
"Nix has a new binary substituter mechanism: the _binary cache_. A binary "
"cache contains pre-built binaries of Nix packages. Whenever Nix wants to "
"build a missing Nix store path, it will check a set of binary caches to see "
"if any of them has a pre-built binary of that path. The configuration "
"setting `binary-caches` contains a list of URLs of binary caches. For "
"instance, doing"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:12
msgid ""
"    $ nix-env -i thunderbird --option binary-caches http://cache.nixos.org\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:14
msgid ""
"will install Thunderbird and its dependencies, using the available pre-built "
"binaries in <http://cache.nixos.org>. The main advantage over the old "
"“manifest”-based method of getting pre-built binaries is that you don’t have "
"to worry about your manifest being in sync with the Nix expressions you’re "
"installing from; i.e., you don’t need to run `nix-pull` to update your "
"manifest. It’s also more scalable because you don’t need to redownload a "
"giant manifest file every time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:23
msgid ""
"A Nix channel can provide a binary cache URL that will be used automatically "
"if you subscribe to that channel. If you use the Nixpkgs or NixOS channels "
"(<http://nixos.org/channels>) you automatically get the cache <http://"
"cache.nixos.org>."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:28
msgid ""
"Binary caches are created using `nix-push`. For details on the operation and "
"format of binary caches, see the `nix-push` manpage. More details are "
"provided in [this nix-dev posting](https://nixos.org/nix-dev/2012-September/"
"009826.html)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:33
msgid ""
"Multiple output support should now be usable. A derivation can declare that "
"it wants to produce multiple store paths by saying something like"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:37
msgid ""
"    outputs = [ \"lib\" \"headers\" \"doc\" ];\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:39
msgid ""
"This will cause Nix to pass the intended store path of each output to the "
"builder through the environment variables `lib`, `headers` and `doc`. Other "
"packages can refer to a specific output by referring to `pkg.output`, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:46
msgid ""
"If you install a package with multiple outputs using `nix-env`, each output "
"path will be symlinked into the user environment."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:49
msgid "Dashes are now valid as part of identifiers and attribute names."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:51
msgid ""
"The new operation `nix-store --repair-path` allows corrupted or missing "
"store paths to be repaired by redownloading them. `nix-store --verify --"
"check-contents                 --repair` will scan and repair all paths in "
"the Nix store. Similarly, `nix-env`, `nix-build`, `nix-instantiate` and `nix-"
"store --realise` have a `--repair` flag to detect and fix bad paths by "
"rebuilding or redownloading them."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:59
msgid ""
"Nix no longer sets the immutable bit on files in the Nix store. Instead, the "
"recommended way to guard the Nix store against accidental modification on "
"Linux is to make it a read-only bind mount, like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:67
msgid ""
"Nix will automatically make `/nix/store` writable as needed (using a private "
"mount namespace) to allow modifications."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:70
msgid ""
"Store optimisation (replacing identical files in the store with hard links) "
"can now be done automatically every time a path is added to the store. This "
"is enabled by setting the configuration option `auto-optimise-store` to "
"`true` (disabled by default)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:75
msgid ""
"Nix now supports `xz` compression for NARs in addition to `bzip2`. It "
"compresses about 30% better on typical archives and decompresses about twice "
"as fast."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:79
msgid ""
"Basic Nix expression evaluation profiling: setting the environment variable "
"`NIX_COUNT_CALLS` to `1` will cause Nix to print how many times each primop "
"or function was executed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:83
msgid "New primops: `concatLists`, `elem`, `elemAt` and `filter`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:85
msgid ""
"The command `nix-copy-closure` has a new flag `--use-substitutes` (`-s`) to "
"download missing paths on the target machine using the substitute mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:89
msgid ""
"The command `nix-worker` has been renamed to `nix-daemon`. Support for "
"running the Nix worker in “slave” mode has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:92
msgid "The `--help` flag of every Nix command now invokes `man`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:94
msgid "Chroot builds are now supported on systemd machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.2.md:96
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Eelco Dolstra, Florian Friesdorf, Mats "
"Erik Andersson and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.3.md:1
msgid "Release 1.3 (2013-01-04)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.3.md:3
msgid ""
"This is primarily a bug fix release. When this version is first run on "
"Linux, it removes any immutable bits from the Nix store and increases the "
"schema version of the Nix store. (The previous release removed support for "
"setting the immutable bit; this release clears any remaining immutable bits "
"to make certain operations more efficient.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.3.md:9
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Eelco Dolstra and Stuart Pernsteiner."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.4.md:1
msgid "Release 1.4 (2013-02-26)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.4.md:3
msgid ""
"This release fixes a security bug in multi-user operation. It was possible "
"for derivations to cause the mode of files outside of the Nix store to be "
"changed to 444 (read-only but world-readable) by creating hard links to "
"those files ([details](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"5526a282b5b44e9296e61e07d7d2626a79141ac4))."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.4.md:9
msgid "There are also the following improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.4.md:11
msgid "New built-in function: `builtins.hashString`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.4.md:13
msgid ""
"Build logs are now stored in `/nix/var/log/nix/drvs/XX/`, where _XX_ is the "
"first two characters of the derivation. This is useful on machines that keep "
"a lot of build logs (such as Hydra servers)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.4.md:17
msgid ""
"The function `corepkgs/fetchurl` can now make the downloaded file "
"executable. This will allow getting rid of all bootstrap binaries in the "
"Nixpkgs source tree."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.4.md:21
msgid ""
"Language change: The expression `\"${./path}         ...\"` now evaluates to "
"a string instead of a path."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.5.md:1
msgid "Release 1.5 (2013-02-27)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.5.md:3
msgid ""
"This is a brown paper bag release to fix a regression introduced by the hard "
"link security fix in 1.4."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.5.2.md:1
msgid "Release 1.5.2 (2013-05-13)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.5.2.md:3
msgid ""
"This is primarily a bug fix release. It has contributions from Eelco "
"Dolstra, Lluís Batlle i Rossell and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:1
msgid "Release 1.6 (2013-09-10)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:3
msgid ""
"In addition to the usual bug fixes, this release has several new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:6
msgid "The command `nix-build --run-env` has been renamed to `nix-shell`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:8
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` now sources `$stdenv/setup` _inside_ the interactive shell, "
"rather than in a parent shell. This ensures that shell functions defined by "
"`stdenv` can be used in the interactive shell."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:12
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` has a new flag `--pure` to clear the environment, so you get an "
"environment that more closely corresponds to the “real” Nix build."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:16
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` now sets the shell prompt (`PS1`) to ensure that Nix shells are "
"distinguishable from your regular shells."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:19
msgid ""
"`nix-env` no longer requires a `*` argument to match all packages, so `nix-"
"env -qa` is equivalent to `nix-env                 -qa '*'`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:23
msgid ""
"`nix-env -i` has a new flag `--remove-all` (`-r`) to remove all previous "
"packages from the profile. This makes it easier to do declarative package "
"management similar to NixOS’s `environment.systemPackages`. For instance, if "
"you have a specification `my-packages.nix` like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:35
msgid "then after any change to this file, you can run:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:39
msgid "to update your profile to match the specification."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:41
msgid ""
"The ‘`with`’ language construct is now more lazy. It only evaluates its "
"argument if a variable might actually refer to an attribute in the argument. "
"For instance, this now works:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:45
msgid ""
"    let\n"
"      pkgs = with pkgs; { foo = \"old\"; bar = foo; } // overrides;\n"
"      overrides = { foo = \"new\"; };\n"
"    in pkgs.bar\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:50
msgid ""
"This evaluates to `\"new\"`, while previously it gave an “infinite "
"recursion” error."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:53
msgid ""
"Nix now has proper integer arithmetic operators. For instance, you can write "
"`x + y` instead of `builtins.add x y`, or `x <                 y` instead of "
"`builtins.lessThan x y`. The comparison operators also work on strings."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:58
msgid "On 64-bit systems, Nix integers are now 64 bits rather than 32 bits."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:60
msgid ""
"When using the Nix daemon, the `nix-daemon` worker process now runs on the "
"same CPU as the client, on systems that support setting CPU affinity. This "
"gives a significant speedup on some systems."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:64
msgid ""
"If a stack overflow occurs in the Nix evaluator, you now get a proper error "
"message (rather than “Segmentation fault”) on some systems."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:68
msgid ""
"In addition to directories, you can now bind-mount regular files in chroots "
"through the (now misnamed) option `build-chroot-dirs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.md:71
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Domen Kožar, Eelco Dolstra, Florian "
"Friesdorf, Gergely Risko, Ivan Kozik, Ludovic Courtès and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:1
msgid "Release 1.6.1 (2013-10-28)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:3
msgid "This is primarily a bug fix release. Changes of interest are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:5
msgid ""
"Nix 1.6 accidentally changed the semantics of antiquoted paths in strings, "
"such as `\"${/foo}/bar\"`. This release reverts to the Nix 1.5.3 behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:9
msgid ""
"Previously, Nix optimised expressions such as `\"${expr}\"` to _expr_. Thus "
"it neither checked whether _expr_ could be coerced to a string, nor applied "
"such coercions. This meant that `\"${123}\"` evaluatued to `123`, and `\"${./"
"foo}\"` evaluated to `./foo` (even though `\"${./foo} \"` evaluates to `\"/"
"nix/store/hash-foo \"`). Nix now checks the type of antiquoted expressions "
"and applies coercions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:16
msgid ""
"Nix now shows the exact position of undefined variables. In particular, "
"undefined variable errors in a `with` previously didn't show _any_ position "
"information, so this makes it a lot easier to fix such errors."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:21
msgid ""
"Undefined variables are now treated consistently. Previously, the `tryEval` "
"function would catch undefined variables inside a `with` but not outside. "
"Now `tryEval` never catches undefined variables."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:25
msgid "Bash completion in `nix-shell` now works correctly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:27
msgid ""
"Stack traces are less verbose: they no longer show calls to builtin "
"functions and only show a single line for each derivation on the call stack."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:31
msgid ""
"New built-in function: `builtins.typeOf`, which returns the type of its "
"argument as a string."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:1
msgid "Release 1.7 (2014-04-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:3
msgid ""
"In addition to the usual bug fixes, this release has the following new "
"features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:6
msgid ""
"Antiquotation is now allowed inside of quoted attribute names (e.g. `set.\"$"
"{foo}\"`). In the case where the attribute name is just a single "
"antiquotation, the quotes can be dropped (e.g. the above example can be "
"written `set.${foo}`). If an attribute name inside of a set declaration "
"evaluates to `null` (e.g. `{ ${null} = false; }`), then that attribute is "
"not added to the set."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:13
msgid ""
"Experimental support for cryptographically signed binary caches. See [the "
"commit for details](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"0fdf4da0e979f992db75cc17376e455ddc5a96d8)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:17
msgid ""
"An experimental new substituter, `download-via-ssh`, that fetches binaries "
"from remote machines via SSH. Specifying the flags `--option                 "
"use-ssh-substituter true --option ssh-substituter-hosts                 "
"user@hostname` will cause Nix to download binaries from the specified "
"machine, if it has them."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:24
msgid ""
"`nix-store -r` and `nix-build` have a new flag, `--check`, that builds a "
"previously built derivation again, and prints an error message if the output "
"is not exactly the same. This helps to verify whether a derivation is truly "
"deterministic. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:36
msgid ""
"The `nix-instantiate` flags `--eval-only` and `--parse-only` have been "
"renamed to `--eval` and `--parse`, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:39
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` now have a flag `--expr` (or "
"`-E`) that allows you to specify the expression to be evaluated as a command "
"line argument. For instance, `nix-instantiate --eval -E                 '1 + "
"2'` will print `3`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:45
msgid "`nix-shell` improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:47
msgid ""
"It has a new flag, `--packages` (or `-p`), that sets up a build environment "
"containing the specified packages from Nixpkgs. For example, the command"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:53
msgid "will start a shell in which the given packages are present."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:55
msgid ""
"It now uses `shell.nix` as the default expression, falling back to "
"`default.nix` if the former doesn’t exist. This makes it convenient to have "
"a `shell.nix` in your project to set up a nice development environment."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:60
msgid ""
"It evaluates the derivation attribute `shellHook`, if set. Since `stdenv` "
"does not normally execute this hook, it allows you to do `nix-shell`\\-"
"specific setup."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:64
msgid "It preserves the user’s timezone setting."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:66
msgid ""
"In chroots, Nix now sets up a `/dev` containing only a minimal set of "
"devices (such as `/dev/null`). Note that it only does this if you _don’t_ "
"have `/dev` listed in your `build-chroot-dirs` setting; otherwise, it will "
"bind-mount the `/dev` from outside the chroot."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:71
msgid ""
"Similarly, if you don’t have `/dev/pts` listed in `build-chroot-dirs`, Nix "
"will mount a private `devpts` filesystem on the chroot’s `/dev/pts`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:75
msgid ""
"New built-in function: `builtins.toJSON`, which returns a JSON "
"representation of a value."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:78
msgid ""
"`nix-env -q` has a new flag `--json` to print a JSON representation of the "
"installed or available packages."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:81
msgid ""
"`nix-env` now supports meta attributes with more complex values, such as "
"attribute sets."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:84
msgid "The `-A` flag now allows attribute names with dots in them, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:86
msgid ""
"    $ nix-instantiate --eval '<nixos>' -A 'config.systemd.units."
"\"nscd.service\".text'\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:88
msgid ""
"The `--max-freed` option to `nix-store --gc` now accepts a unit specifier. "
"For example, `nix-store --gc --max-freed                 1G` will free up to "
"1 gigabyte of disk space."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:92
msgid ""
"`nix-collect-garbage` has a new flag `--delete-older-than` _N_`d`, which "
"deletes all user environment generations older than _N_ days. Likewise, `nix-"
"env                 --delete-generations` accepts a _N_`d` age limit."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:97
msgid ""
"Nix now heuristically detects whether a build failure was due to a disk-full "
"condition. In that case, the build is not flagged as “permanently failed”. "
"This is mostly useful for Hydra, which needs to distinguish between "
"permanent and transient build failures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:102
msgid ""
"There is a new symbol `__curPos` that expands to an attribute set containing "
"its file name and line and column numbers, e.g. `{ file = \"foo.nix\"; line "
"= 10;                 column = 5; }`. There also is a new builtin function, "
"`unsafeGetAttrPos`, that returns the position of an attribute. This is used "
"by Nixpkgs to provide location information in error messages, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:114
msgid ""
"The garbage collector is now more concurrent with other Nix processes "
"because it releases certain locks earlier."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:117
msgid ""
"The binary tarball installer has been improved. You can now install Nix by "
"running:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:120
msgid ""
"    $ bash <(curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install)\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:122
msgid ""
"More evaluation errors include position information. For instance, selecting "
"a missing attribute will print something like"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:127
msgid "The command `nix-setuid-helper` is gone."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:129
msgid ""
"Nix no longer uses Automake, but instead has a non-recursive, GNU Make-based "
"build system."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:132
msgid ""
"All installed libraries now have the prefix `libnix`. In particular, this "
"gets rid of `libutil`, which could clash with libraries with the same name "
"from other packages."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:136
msgid "Nix now requires a compiler that supports C++11."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.7.md:138
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Danny Wilson, Domen Kožar, Eelco "
"Dolstra, Ian-Woo Kim, Ludovic Courtès, Maxim Ivanov, Petr Rockai, Ricardo M. "
"Correia and Shea Levy."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:1
msgid "Release 1.8 (2014-12-14)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:3
msgid ""
"Breaking change: to address a race condition, the remote build hook "
"mechanism now uses `nix-store         --serve` on the remote machine. This "
"requires build slaves to be updated to Nix 1.8."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:8
msgid ""
"Nix now uses HTTPS instead of HTTP to access the default binary cache, "
"`cache.nixos.org`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:11
msgid ""
"`nix-env` selectors are now regular expressions. For instance, you can do"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:16
msgid "to query all packages with a name containing `zip`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:18
msgid ""
"`nix-store --read-log` can now fetch remote build logs. If a build log is "
"not available locally, then ‘nix-store -l’ will now try to download it from "
"the servers listed in the ‘log-servers’ option in nix.conf. For instance, if "
"you have the configuration option"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:23
msgid ""
"    log-servers = http://hydra.nixos.org/log\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:25
msgid ""
"then it will try to get logs from `http://hydra.nixos.org/log/base name of "
"the store path`. This allows you to do things like:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:31
msgid "and get a log even if `xterm` wasn't built locally."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:33
msgid ""
"New builtin functions: `attrValues`, `deepSeq`, `fromJSON`, `readDir`, `seq`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:36
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate --eval` now has a `--json` flag to print the resulting "
"value in JSON format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:39
msgid ""
"`nix-copy-closure` now uses `nix-store --serve` on the remote side to send "
"or receive closures. This fixes a race condition between `nix-copy-closure` "
"and the garbage collector."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:43
msgid ""
"Derivations can specify the new special attribute `allowedRequisites`, which "
"has a similar meaning to `allowedReferences`. But instead of only enforcing "
"to explicitly specify the immediate references, it requires the derivation "
"to specify all the dependencies recursively (hence the name, requisites) "
"that are used by the resulting output."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:50
msgid ""
"On Mac OS X, Nix now handles case collisions when importing closures from "
"case-sensitive file systems. This is mostly useful for running NixOps on Mac "
"OS X."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:54
msgid ""
"The Nix daemon has new configuration options `allowed-users` (specifying the "
"users and groups that are allowed to connect to the daemon) and `trusted-"
"users` (specifying the users and groups that can perform privileged "
"operations like specifying untrusted binary caches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:60
msgid ""
"The configuration option `build-cores` now defaults to the number of "
"available CPU cores."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:63
msgid ""
"Build users are now used by default when Nix is invoked as root. This "
"prevents builds from accidentally running as root."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:66
msgid "Nix now includes systemd units and Upstart jobs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:68
msgid "Speed improvements to `nix-store         --optimise`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:71
msgid ""
"Language change: the `==` operator now ignores string contexts (the "
"“dependencies” of a string)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:74
msgid ""
"Nix now filters out Nix-specific ANSI escape sequences on standard error. "
"They are supposed to be invisible, but some terminals show them anyway."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:78
msgid ""
"Various commands now automatically pipe their output into the pager as "
"specified by the `PAGER` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:81
msgid "Several improvements to reduce memory consumption in the evaluator."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:83
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Adam Szkoda, Aristid Breitkreuz, Bob van "
"der Linden, Charles Strahan, darealshinji, Eelco Dolstra, Gergely Risko, "
"Joel Taylor, Ludovic Courtès, Marko Durkovic, Mikey Ariel, Paul Colomiets, "
"Ricardo M. Correia, Ricky Elrod, Robert Helgesson, Rob Vermaas, Russell "
"O'Connor, Shea Levy, Shell Turner, Sönke Hahn, Steve Purcell, Vladimír Čunát "
"and Wout Mertens."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:1
msgid "Release 1.9 (2015-06-12)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:6
msgid ""
"Signed binary cache support. You can enable signature checking by adding the "
"following to `nix.conf`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:12
msgid ""
"This will prevent Nix from downloading any binary from the cache that is not "
"signed by one of the keys listed in `binary-cache-public-keys`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:16
msgid ""
"Signature checking is only supported if you built Nix with the `libsodium` "
"package."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:19
msgid ""
"Note that while Nix has had experimental support for signed binary caches "
"since version 1.7, this release changes the signature format in a backwards-"
"incompatible way."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:23
msgid ""
"Automatic downloading of Nix expression tarballs. In various places, you can "
"now specify the URL of a tarball containing Nix expressions (such as "
"Nixpkgs), which will be downloaded and unpacked automatically. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:28
msgid "In `nix-env`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:30
msgid ""
"    $ nix-env -f https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-channels/archive/"
"nixos-14.12.tar.gz -iA firefox\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:32
msgid ""
"This installs Firefox from the latest tested and built revision of the NixOS "
"14.12 channel."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:35
msgid "In `nix-build` and `nix-shell`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:37
msgid ""
"    $ nix-build https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/archive/master.tar.gz -A "
"hello\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:39
msgid ""
"This builds GNU Hello from the latest revision of the Nixpkgs master branch."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:42
msgid ""
"In the Nix search path (as specified via `NIX_PATH` or `-I`). For example, "
"to start a shell containing the Pan package from a specific version of "
"Nixpkgs:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:46
msgid ""
"    $ nix-shell -p pan -I nixpkgs=https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-channels/"
"archive/8a3eea054838b55aca962c3fbde9c83c102b8bf2.tar.gz\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:48
msgid "In `nixos-rebuild` (on NixOS):"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:50
msgid ""
"    $ nixos-rebuild test -I nixpkgs=https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-"
"channels/archive/nixos-unstable.tar.gz\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:52
msgid "In Nix expressions, via the new builtin function `fetchTarball`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:54
msgid ""
"    with import (fetchTarball https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs-channels/"
"archive/nixos-14.12.tar.gz) {}; …\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:56
msgid "(This is not allowed in restricted mode.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:60
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` now has a flag `--run` to execute a command in the `nix-shell` "
"environment, e.g. `nix-shell --run make`. This is like the existing `--"
"command` flag, except that it uses a non-interactive shell (ensuring that "
"hitting Ctrl-C won’t drop you into the child shell)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:66
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` can now be used as a `#!`\\-interpreter. This allows you to "
"write scripts that dynamically fetch their own dependencies. For example, "
"here is a Haskell script that, when invoked, first downloads GHC and the "
"Haskell packages on which it depends:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:72
msgid ""
"    #! /usr/bin/env nix-shell\n"
"    #! nix-shell -i runghc -p haskellPackages.ghc haskellPackages.HTTP\n"
"    \n"
"    import Network.HTTP\n"
"    \n"
"    main = do\n"
"      resp <- Network.HTTP.simpleHTTP (getRequest \"http://nixos.org/\")\n"
"      body <- getResponseBody resp\n"
"      print (take 100 body)\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:82
msgid ""
"Of course, the dependencies are cached in the Nix store, so the second "
"invocation of this script will be much faster."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:85
msgid "Chroot improvements:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:87
msgid ""
"Chroot builds are now supported on Mac OS X (using its sandbox mechanism)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:90
msgid ""
"If chroots are enabled, they are now used for all derivations, including "
"fixed-output derivations (such as `fetchurl`). The latter do have network "
"access, but can no longer access the host filesystem. If you need the old "
"behaviour, you can set the option `build-use-chroot` to `relaxed`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:96
msgid ""
"On Linux, if chroots are enabled, builds are performed in a private PID "
"namespace once again. (This functionality was lost in Nix 1.8.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:100
msgid ""
"Store paths listed in `build-chroot-dirs` are now automatically expanded to "
"their closure. For instance, if you want `/nix/store/…-bash/bin/sh` mounted "
"in your chroot as `/bin/sh`, you only need to say `build-chroot-dirs "
"=                                                 /bin/sh=/nix/store/…-bash/"
"bin/sh`; it is no longer necessary to specify the dependencies of Bash."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:107
msgid ""
"The new derivation attribute `passAsFile` allows you to specify that the "
"contents of derivation attributes should be passed via files rather than "
"environment variables. This is useful if you need to pass very long strings "
"that exceed the size limit of the environment. The Nixpkgs function "
"`writeTextFile` uses this."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:113
msgid ""
"You can now use `~` in Nix file names to refer to your home directory, e.g. "
"`import         ~/.nixpkgs/config.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:117
msgid ""
"Nix has a new option `restrict-eval` that allows limiting what paths the Nix "
"evaluator has access to. By passing `--option restrict-eval true` to Nix, "
"the evaluator will throw an exception if an attempt is made to access any "
"file outside of the Nix search path. This is primarily intended for Hydra to "
"ensure that a Hydra jobset only refers to its declared inputs (and is "
"therefore reproducible)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:124
msgid ""
"`nix-env` now only creates a new “generation” symlink in `/nix/var/nix/"
"profiles` if something actually changed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:127
msgid ""
"The environment variable `NIX_PAGER` can now be set to override `PAGER`. You "
"can set it to `cat` to disable paging for Nix commands only."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:131
msgid "Failing `<...>` lookups now show position information."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:133
msgid ""
"Improved Boehm GC use: we disabled scanning for interior pointers, which "
"should reduce the “`Repeated         allocation of very large block`” "
"warnings and associated retention of memory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.9.md:138
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from aszlig, Benjamin Staffin, Charles "
"Strahan, Christian Theune, Daniel Hahler, Danylo Hlynskyi Daniel Peebles, "
"Dan Peebles, Domen Kožar, Eelco Dolstra, Harald van Dijk, Hoang Xuan Phu, "
"Jaka Hudoklin, Jeff Ramnani, j-keck, Linquize, Luca Bruno, Michael Merickel, "
"Oliver Dunkl, Rob Vermaas, Rok Garbas, Shea Levy, Tobias Geerinckx-Rice and "
"William A. Kennington III."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:1
msgid "Release 2.0 (2018-02-22)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:3
msgid "The following incompatible changes have been made:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:5
msgid ""
"The manifest-based substituter mechanism (`download-using-manifests`) has "
"been [removed](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"867967265b80946dfe1db72d40324b4f9af988ed). It has been superseded by the "
"binary cache substituter mechanism since several years. As a result, the "
"following programs have been removed:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:12
msgid "`nix-pull`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:14
msgid "`nix-generate-patches`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:16
msgid "`bsdiff`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:18
msgid "`bspatch`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:20
msgid ""
"The “copy from other stores” substituter mechanism (`copy-from-other-stores` "
"and the `NIX_OTHER_STORES` environment variable) has been removed. It was "
"primarily used by the NixOS installer to copy available paths from the "
"installation medium. The replacement is to use a chroot store as a "
"substituter (e.g. `--substituters /mnt`), or to build into a chroot store "
"(e.g. `--store /mnt --substituters /`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:28
msgid ""
"The command `nix-push` has been removed as part of the effort to eliminate "
"Nix's dependency on Perl. You can use `nix copy` instead, e.g. `nix "
"copy                 --to file:///tmp/my-binary-cache paths…`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:33
msgid ""
"The “nested” log output feature (`--log-type                 pretty`) has "
"been removed. As a result, `nix-log2xml` was also removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:37
msgid ""
"OpenSSL-based signing has been [removed](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"f435f8247553656774dd1b2c88e9de5d59cab203). This feature was never well-"
"supported. A better alternative is provided by the `secret-key-files` and "
"`trusted-public-keys` options."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:43
msgid ""
"Failed build caching has been [removed](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"8cffec84859cec8b610a2a22ab0c4d462a9351ff). This feature was introduced to "
"support the Hydra continuous build system, but Hydra no longer uses it."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:48
msgid ""
"`nix-mode.el` has been removed from Nix. It is now [a separate repository]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix-mode) and can be installed through the MELPA "
"package repository."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:52
msgid "This release has the following new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:54
msgid ""
"It introduces a new command named `nix`, which is intended to eventually "
"replace all `nix-*` commands with a more consistent and better designed user "
"interface. It currently provides replacements for some (but not all) of the "
"functionality provided by `nix-store`, `nix-build`, `nix-shell -p`, `nix-env "
"-qa`, `nix-instantiate --eval`, `nix-push` and `nix-copy-closure`. It has "
"the following major features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:62
msgid ""
"Unlike the legacy commands, it has a consistent way to refer to packages and "
"package-like arguments (like store paths). For example, the following "
"commands all copy the GNU Hello package to a remote machine:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:67
msgid ""
"    nix copy --to ssh://machine nixpkgs.hello\n"
"    \n"
"    nix copy --to ssh://machine /nix/store/qbhyj3blxpw2i6pb7c6grc9185nbnpvy-"
"hello-2.10\n"
"    \n"
"    nix copy --to ssh://machine '(with import <nixpkgs> {}; hello)'\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:73
msgid "By contrast, `nix-copy-closure` only accepted store paths as arguments."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:76
msgid ""
"It is self-documenting: `--help` shows all available command-line arguments. "
"If `--help` is given after a subcommand, it shows examples for that "
"subcommand. "
"`nix                                                                 --help-"
"config` shows all configuration options."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:81
msgid ""
"It is much less verbose. By default, it displays a single-line progress "
"indicator that shows how many packages are left to be built or downloaded, "
"and (if there are running builds) the most recent line of builder output. If "
"a build fails, it shows the last few lines of builder output. The full build "
"log can be retrieved using "
"`nix                                                                 log`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:89
msgid ""
"It [provides](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"b8283773bd64d7da6859ed520ee19867742a03ba) all `nix.conf` configuration "
"options as command line flags. For example, instead of `--"
"option                                                                 http-"
"connections 100` you can write `--http-connections 100`. Boolean options can "
"be written as `--foo` or `--no-foo` (e.g. `--no-auto-optimise-store`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:97
msgid ""
"Many subcommands have a `--json` flag to write results to stdout in JSON "
"format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:102
msgid ""
"Please note that the `nix` command is a work in progress and the interface "
"is subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:105
msgid "It provides the following high-level (“porcelain”) subcommands:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:107
msgid "`nix build` is a replacement for `nix-build`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:109
msgid ""
"`nix run` executes a command in an environment in which the specified "
"packages are available. It is (roughly) a replacement for `nix-"
"shell                                                                 -p`. "
"Unlike that command, it does not execute the command in a shell, and has a "
"flag (`-c`) that specifies the unquoted command line to be executed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:116
msgid ""
"It is particularly useful in conjunction with chroot stores, allowing Linux "
"users who do not have permission to install Nix in `/nix/store` to still use "
"binary substitutes that assume `/nix/store`. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:123
msgid ""
"downloads (or if not substitutes are available, builds) the GNU Hello "
"package into `~/my-nix/nix/store`, then runs `hello` in a mount namespace "
"where `~/my-nix/nix/store` is mounted onto `/nix/store`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:128
msgid ""
"`nix search` replaces `nix-"
"env                                                                 -qa`. It "
"searches the available packages for occurrences of a search string in the "
"attribute name, package name or description. Unlike `nix-env -qa`, it has a "
"cache to speed up subsequent searches."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:134
msgid ""
"`nix copy` copies paths between arbitrary Nix stores, generalising `nix-copy-"
"closure` and `nix-push`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:137
msgid ""
"`nix repl` replaces the external program `nix-repl`. It provides an "
"interactive environment for evaluating and building Nix expressions. Note "
"that it uses `linenoise-ng` instead of GNU Readline."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:142
msgid ""
"`nix upgrade-nix` upgrades Nix to the latest stable version. This requires "
"that Nix is installed in a profile. (Thus it won’t work on NixOS, or if it’s "
"installed outside of the Nix store.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:146
msgid ""
"`nix verify` checks whether store paths are unmodified and/or “trusted” (see "
"below). It replaces `nix-store --verify` and `nix-"
"store                                                                 --"
"verify-path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:151
msgid ""
"`nix log` shows the build log of a package or path. If the build log is not "
"available locally, it will try to obtain it from the configured substituters "
"(such as [cache.nixos.org](https://cache.nixos.org/), which now provides "
"build logs)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:157
msgid "`nix edit` opens the source code of a package in your editor."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:159
msgid "`nix eval` replaces `nix-instantiate --eval`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:161
msgid ""
"`nix                                                                 why-"
"depends` shows why one store path has another in its closure. This is "
"primarily useful to finding the causes of closure bloat. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:168
msgid ""
"shows a chain of files and fragments of file contents that cause the VLC "
"package to have the “dev” output of `libdrm` in its closure — an undesirable "
"situation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:172
msgid ""
"`nix path-info` shows information about store paths, replacing `nix-store "
"-q`. A useful feature is the option `--closure-size` (`-S`). For example, "
"the following command show the closure sizes of every path in the current "
"NixOS system closure, sorted by size:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:180
msgid ""
"`nix optimise-store` replaces `nix-store --optimise`. The main difference is "
"that it has a progress indicator."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:183
msgid "A number of low-level (“plumbing”) commands are also available:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:185
msgid ""
"`nix ls-store` and "
"`nix                                                                 ls-nar` "
"list the contents of a store path or NAR file. The former is primarily "
"useful in conjunction with remote stores, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:190
msgid ""
"    nix ls-store --store https://cache.nixos.org/ -lR /nix/store/"
"qbhyj3blxpw2i6pb7c6grc9185nbnpvy-hello-2.10\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:192
msgid "lists the contents of path in a binary cache."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:194
msgid ""
"`nix cat-store` and "
"`nix                                                                 cat-"
"nar` allow extracting a file from a store path or NAR file."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:197
msgid ""
"`nix dump-path` writes the contents of a store path to stdout in NAR format. "
"This replaces `nix-store --dump`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:200
msgid ""
"`nix                                                                 show-"
"derivation` displays a store derivation in JSON format. This is an "
"alternative to `pp-aterm`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:204
msgid ""
"`nix                                                                 add-to-"
"store` replaces `nix-"
"store                                                                 --add`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:208
msgid "`nix sign-paths` signs store paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:210
msgid "`nix copy-sigs` copies signatures from one store to another."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:212
msgid ""
"`nix show-config` shows all configuration options and their current values."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:215
msgid ""
"The store abstraction that Nix has had for a long time to support store "
"access via the Nix daemon has been extended significantly. In particular, "
"substituters (which used to be external programs such as `download-from-"
"binary-cache`) are now subclasses of the abstract `Store` class. This allows "
"many Nix commands to operate on such store types. For example, `nix path-"
"info` shows information about paths in your local Nix store, while `nix path-"
"info --store https://cache.nixos.org/` shows information about paths in the "
"specified binary cache. Similarly, `nix-copy-closure`, `nix-push` and "
"substitution are all instances of the general notion of copying paths "
"between different kinds of Nix stores."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:228
msgid ""
"Stores are specified using an URI-like syntax, e.g. <https://cache.nixos.org/"
"> or <ssh://machine>. The following store types are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:232
msgid ""
"`LocalStore` (stori URI `local` or an absolute path) and the misnamed "
"`RemoteStore` (`daemon`) provide access to a local Nix store, the latter via "
"the Nix daemon. You can use `auto` or the empty string to auto-select a "
"local or daemon store depending on whether you have write permission to the "
"Nix store. It is no longer necessary to set the `NIX_REMOTE` environment "
"variable to use the Nix daemon."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:240
msgid ""
"As noted above, `LocalStore` now supports chroot builds, allowing the "
"“physical” location of the Nix store (e.g. `/home/alice/nix/store`) to "
"differ from its “logical” location (typically `/nix/store`). This allows non-"
"root users to use Nix while still getting the benefits from prebuilt "
"binaries from [cache.nixos.org](https://cache.nixos.org/)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:247
msgid ""
"`BinaryCacheStore` is the abstract superclass of all binary cache stores. It "
"supports writing build logs and NAR content listings in JSON format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:251
msgid ""
"`HttpBinaryCacheStore` (`http://`, `https://`) supports binary caches via "
"HTTP or HTTPS. If the server supports `PUT` requests, it supports uploading "
"store paths via commands such as "
"`nix                                                                 copy`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:256
msgid ""
"`LocalBinaryCacheStore` (`file://`) supports binary caches in the local "
"filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:259
msgid ""
"`S3BinaryCacheStore` (`s3://`) supports binary caches stored in Amazon S3, "
"if enabled at compile time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:262
msgid ""
"`LegacySSHStore` (`ssh://`) is used to implement remote builds and `nix-copy-"
"closure`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:265
msgid ""
"`SSHStore` (`ssh-ng://`) supports arbitrary Nix operations on a remote "
"machine via the same protocol used by `nix-daemon`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:268
msgid "Security has been improved in various ways:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:270
msgid ""
"Nix now stores signatures for local store paths. When paths are copied "
"between stores (e.g., copied from a binary cache to a local store), "
"signatures are propagated."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:274
msgid ""
"Locally-built paths are signed automatically using the secret keys specified "
"by the `secret-key-files` store option. Secret/public key pairs can be "
"generated using `nix-"
"store                                                                 --"
"generate-binary-cache-key`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:279
msgid ""
"In addition, locally-built store paths are marked as “ultimately trusted”, "
"but this bit is not propagated when paths are copied between stores."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:283
msgid ""
"Content-addressable store paths no longer require signatures — they can be "
"imported into a store by unprivileged users even if they lack signatures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:287
msgid ""
"The command `nix verify` checks whether the specified paths are trusted, "
"i.e., have a certain number of trusted signatures, are ultimately trusted, "
"or are content-addressed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:291
msgid ""
"Substitutions from binary caches [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"ecbc3fedd3d5bdc5a0e1a0a51b29062f2874ac8b) require signatures by default. "
"This was already the case on NixOS."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:296
msgid ""
"In Linux sandbox builds, we [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"eba840c8a13b465ace90172ff76a0db2899ab11b) use `/build` instead of `/tmp` as "
"the temporary build directory. This fixes potential security problems when a "
"build accidentally stores its `TMPDIR` in some security-sensitive place, "
"such as an RPATH."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:303
msgid ""
"_Pure evaluation mode_. With the `--pure-eval` flag, Nix enables a variant "
"of the existing restricted evaluation mode that forbids access to anything "
"that could cause different evaluations of the same command line arguments to "
"produce a different result. This includes builtin functions such as "
"`builtins.getEnv`, but more importantly, _all_ filesystem or network access "
"unless a content hash or commit hash is specified. For example, calls to "
"`builtins.fetchGit` are only allowed if a `rev` attribute is specified."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:313
msgid ""
"The goal of this feature is to enable true reproducibility and traceability "
"of builds (including NixOS system configurations) at the evaluation level. "
"For example, in the future, `nixos-rebuild` might build configurations from "
"a Nix expression in a Git repository in pure mode. That expression might "
"fetch other repositories such as Nixpkgs via `builtins.fetchGit`. The commit "
"hash of the top-level repository then uniquely identifies a running system, "
"and, in conjunction with that repository, allows it to be reproduced or "
"modified."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:323
msgid ""
"There are several new features to support binary reproducibility (i.e. to "
"help ensure that multiple builds of the same derivation produce exactly the "
"same output). When `enforce-determinism` is set to `false`, it’s [no longer]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"8bdf83f936adae6f2c907a6d2541e80d4120f051) a fatal error if build rounds "
"produce different output. Also, a hook named `diff-hook` is [provided]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"9a313469a4bdea2d1e8df24d16289dc2a172a169) to allow you to run tools such as "
"`diffoscope` when build rounds produce different output."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:334
msgid ""
"Configuring remote builds is a lot easier now. Provided you are not using "
"the Nix daemon, you can now just specify a remote build machine on the "
"command line, e.g. `--option builders                 'ssh://my-mac x86_64-"
"darwin'`. The environment variable `NIX_BUILD_HOOK` has been removed and is "
"no longer needed. The environment variable `NIX_REMOTE_SYSTEMS` is still "
"supported for compatibility, but it is also possible to specify builders in "
"`nix.conf` by setting the option `builders =                 @path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:344
msgid ""
"If a fixed-output derivation produces a result with an incorrect hash, the "
"output path is moved to the location corresponding to the actual hash and "
"registered as valid. Thus, a subsequent build of the fixed-output derivation "
"with the correct hash is unnecessary."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:349
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"ea59f39326c8e9dc42dfed4bcbf597fbce58797c) sets the `IN_NIX_SHELL` "
"environment variable during evaluation and in the shell itself. This can be "
"used to perform different actions depending on whether you’re in a Nix shell "
"or in a regular build. Nixpkgs provides `lib.inNixShell` to check this "
"variable during evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:357
msgid ""
"`NIX_PATH` is now lazy, so URIs in the path are only downloaded if they are "
"needed for evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:360
msgid ""
"You can now use `channel:` as a short-hand for <https://nixos.org/channels//"
"nixexprs.tar.xz> \\[now <https://channels.nixos.org//nixexprs.tar.xz>\\]. "
"For example, `nix-build channel:nixos-15.09 -A hello` will build the GNU "
"Hello package from the `nixos-15.09` channel. In the future, this may use "
"Git to fetch updates more efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:366
msgid ""
"When `--no-build-output` is given, the last 10 lines of the build log will "
"be shown if a build fails."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:369
msgid "Networking has been improved:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:371
msgid ""
"HTTP/2 is now supported. This makes binary cache lookups [much more "
"efficient](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"90ad02bf626b885a5dd8967894e2eafc953bdf92)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:375
msgid ""
"We now retry downloads on many HTTP errors, making binary caches "
"substituters more resilient to temporary failures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:378
msgid ""
"HTTP credentials can now be configured via the standard `netrc` mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:381
msgid ""
"If S3 support is enabled at compile time, <s3://> URIs are [supported]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"9ff9c3f2f80ba4108e9c945bbfda2c64735f987b) in all places where Nix allows "
"URIs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:385
msgid ""
"Brotli compression is now supported. In particular, [cache.nixos.org]"
"(https://cache.nixos.org/) build logs are now compressed using Brotli."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:389
msgid ""
"`nix-env` [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"b0cb11722626e906a73f10dd9a0c9eea29faf43a) ignores packages with bad "
"derivation names (in particular those starting with a digit or containing a "
"dot)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:394
msgid ""
"Many configuration options have been renamed, either because they were "
"unnecessarily verbose (e.g. `build-use-sandbox` is now just `sandbox`) or to "
"reflect generalised behaviour (e.g. `binary-caches` is now `substituters` "
"because it allows arbitrary store URIs). The old names are still supported "
"for compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:400
msgid ""
"The `max-jobs` option can [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"7251d048fa812d2551b7003bc9f13a8f5d4c95a5) be set to `auto` to use the number "
"of CPUs in the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:404
msgid ""
"Hashes can [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"c0015e87af70f539f24d2aa2bc224a9d8b84276b) be specified in base-64 format, in "
"addition to base-16 and the non-standard base-32."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:409
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` now uses `bashInteractive` from Nixpkgs, rather than the `bash` "
"command that happens to be in the caller’s `PATH`. This is especially "
"important on macOS where the `bash` provided by the system is seriously "
"outdated and cannot execute `stdenv`’s setup script."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:415
msgid ""
"Nix can now automatically trigger a garbage collection if free disk space "
"drops below a certain level during a build. This is configured using the "
"`min-free` and `max-free` options."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:419
msgid ""
"`nix-store -q --roots` and `nix-store --gc --print-roots` now show temporary "
"and in-memory roots."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:422
msgid ""
"Nix can now be extended with plugins. See the documentation of the `plugin-"
"files` option for more details."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:425
msgid "The Nix language has the following new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:427
msgid ""
"It supports floating point numbers. They are based on the C++ `float` type "
"and are supported by the existing numerical operators. Export and import to "
"and from JSON and XML works, too."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:431
msgid ""
"Derivation attributes can now reference the outputs of the derivation using "
"the `placeholder` builtin function. For example, the attribute"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:435
msgid ""
"    configureFlags = \"--prefix=${placeholder \"out\"} --includedir=$"
"{placeholder \"dev\"}\";\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:437
msgid ""
"will cause the `configureFlags` environment variable to contain the actual "
"store paths corresponding to the `out` and `dev` outputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:440
msgid "The following builtin functions are new or extended:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:442
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchGit` allows Git repositories to be fetched at evaluation "
"time. Thus it differs from the `fetchgit` function in Nixpkgs, which fetches "
"at build time and cannot be used to fetch Nix expressions during evaluation. "
"A typical use case is to import external NixOS modules from your "
"configuration, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:448
msgid ""
"    imports = [ (builtins.fetchGit https://github.com/edolstra/dwarffs + \"/"
"module.nix\") ];\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:450
msgid ""
"Similarly, `builtins.fetchMercurial` allows you to fetch Mercurial "
"repositories."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:453
msgid ""
"`builtins.path` generalises `builtins.filterSource` and path literals (e.g. "
"`./foo`). It allows specifying a store path name that differs from the "
"source path name (e.g. `builtins.path { path = ./foo; name = "
"\"bar\";                 }`) and also supports filtering out unwanted files."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:459
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchurl` and `builtins.fetchTarball` now support `sha256` and "
"`name` attributes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:462
msgid ""
"`builtins.split` splits a string using a POSIX extended regular expression "
"as the separator."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:465
msgid ""
"`builtins.partition` partitions the elements of a list into two lists, "
"depending on a Boolean predicate."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:468
msgid ""
"`<nix/fetchurl.nix>` now uses the content-addressable tarball cache at "
"<http://tarballs.nixos.org/>, just like `fetchurl` in Nixpkgs. "
"(f2682e6e18a76ecbfb8a12c17e3a0ca15c084197)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:472
msgid ""
"In restricted and pure evaluation mode, builtin functions that download from "
"the network (such as `fetchGit`) are permitted to fetch underneath a list of "
"URI prefixes specified in the option `allowed-uris`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:477
msgid "The Nix build environment has the following changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:479
msgid ""
"Values such as Booleans, integers, (nested) lists and attribute sets can "
"[now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"6de33a9c675b187437a2e1abbcb290981a89ecb1) be passed to builders in a non-"
"lossy way. If the special attribute `__structuredAttrs` is set to `true`, "
"the other derivation attributes are serialised in JSON format and made "
"available to the builder via the file `.attrs.json` in the builder’s "
"temporary directory. This obviates the need for `passAsFile` since JSON "
"files have no size restrictions, unlike process environments."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:489
msgid ""
"[As a convenience to Bash builders](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"2d5b1b24bf70a498e4c0b378704cfdb6471cc699), Nix writes a script named "
"`.attrs.sh` to the builder’s directory that initialises shell variables "
"corresponding to all attributes that are representable in Bash. This "
"includes non-nested (associative) arrays. For example, the attribute "
"`hardening.format =                 true` ends up as the Bash associative "
"array element `${hardening[format]}`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:498
msgid ""
"Builders can [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"88e6bb76de5564b3217be9688677d1c89101b2a3) communicate what build phase they "
"are in by writing messages to the file descriptor specified in `NIX_LOG_FD`. "
"The current phase is shown by the `nix` progress indicator."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:504
msgid ""
"In Linux sandbox builds, we [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"a2d92bb20e82a0957067ede60e91fab256948b41) provide a default `/bin/sh` "
"(namely `ash` from BusyBox)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:508
msgid ""
"In structured attribute mode, `exportReferencesGraph` [exports](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/c2b0d8749f7e77afc1c4b3e8dd36b7ee9720af4a) "
"extended information about closures in JSON format. In particular, it "
"includes the sizes and hashes of paths. This is primarily useful for NixOS "
"image builders."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:514
msgid ""
"Builds are [now](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/commit/"
"21948deed99a3295e4d5666e027a6ca42dc00b40) killed as soon as Nix receives EOF "
"on the builder’s stdout or stderr. This fixes a bug that allowed builds to "
"hang Nix indefinitely, regardless of timeouts."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:520
msgid ""
"The `sandbox-paths` configuration option can now specify optional paths by "
"appending a `?`, e.g. `/dev/nvidiactl?` will bind-mount `/dev/nvidiactl` "
"only if it exists."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:524
msgid ""
"On Linux, builds are now executed in a user namespace with UID 1000 and GID "
"100."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:527
msgid "A number of significant internal changes were made:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:529
msgid ""
"Nix no longer depends on Perl and all Perl components have been rewritten in "
"C++ or removed. The Perl bindings that used to be part of Nix have been "
"moved to a separate package, `nix-perl`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:533
msgid ""
"All `Store` classes are now thread-safe. `RemoteStore` supports multiple "
"concurrent connections to the daemon. This is primarily useful in multi-"
"threaded programs such as `hydra-queue-runner`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.0.md:537
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Adrien Devresse, Alexander Ried, Alex "
"Cruice, Alexey Shmalko, AmineChikhaoui, Andy Wingo, Aneesh Agrawal, Anthony "
"Cowley, Armijn Hemel, aszlig, Ben Gamari, Benjamin Hipple, Benjamin Staffin, "
"Benno Fünfstück, Bjørn Forsman, Brian McKenna, Charles Strahan, Chase Adams, "
"Chris Martin, Christian Theune, Chris Warburton, Daiderd Jordan, Dan "
"Connolly, Daniel Peebles, Dan Peebles, davidak, David McFarland, Dmitry "
"Kalinkin, Domen Kožar, Eelco Dolstra, Emery Hemingway, Eric Litak, Eric "
"Wolf, Fabian Schmitthenner, Frederik Rietdijk, Gabriel Gonzalez, Giorgio "
"Gallo, Graham Christensen, Guillaume Maudoux, Harmen, Iavael, James "
"Broadhead, James Earl Douglas, Janus Troelsen, Jeremy Shaw, Joachim Schiele, "
"Joe Hermaszewski, Joel Moberg, Johannes 'fish' Ziemke, Jörg Thalheim, Jude "
"Taylor, kballou, Keshav Kini, Kjetil Orbekk, Langston Barrett, Linus "
