#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:1
msgid "Release 2.1 (2018-09-02)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:3
msgid ""
"This is primarily a bug fix release. It also reduces memory consumption in "
"certain situations. In addition, it has the following new features:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:6
msgid ""
"The Nix installer will no longer default to the Multi-User installation for "
"macOS. You can still instruct the installer to run in multi-user mode."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:10
msgid ""
"The Nix installer now supports performing a Multi-User installation for "
"Linux computers which are running systemd. You can select a Multi-User "
"installation by passing the `--daemon` flag to the installer: `sh <(curl -L "
"https://nixos.org/nix/install) --daemon`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:16
msgid ""
"The multi-user installer cannot handle systems with SELinux. If your system "
"has SELinux enabled, you can force the installer to run in single-user mode."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:20
msgid ""
"New builtin functions: `builtins.bitAnd`, `builtins.bitOr`, "
"`builtins.bitXor`, `builtins.fromTOML`, `builtins.concatMap`, "
"`builtins.mapAttrs`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:24
msgid ""
"The S3 binary cache store now supports uploading NARs larger than 5 GiB."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:27
msgid ""
"The S3 binary cache store now supports uploading to S3-compatible services "
"with the `endpoint` option."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:30
msgid ""
"The flag `--fallback` is no longer required to recover from disappeared NARs "
"in binary caches."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:33
msgid "`nix-daemon` now respects `--store`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:35
msgid "`nix run` now respects `nix-support/propagated-user-env-packages`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.1.md:37
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Adrien Devresse, Aleksandr Pashkov, "
"Alexandre Esteves, Amine Chikhaoui, Andrew Dunham, Asad Saeeduddin, aszlig, "
"Ben Challenor, Ben Gamari, Benjamin Hipple, Bogdan Seniuc, Corey O'Connor, "
"Daiderd Jordan, Daniel Peebles, Daniel Poelzleithner, Danylo Hlynskyi, "
"Dmitry Kalinkin, Domen Kožar, Doug Beardsley, Eelco Dolstra, Erik Arvstedt, "
"Félix Baylac-Jacqué, Gleb Peregud, Graham Christensen, Guillaume Maudoux, "
"Ivan Kozik, John Arnold, Justin Humm, Linus Heckemann, Lorenzo Manacorda, "
"Matthew Justin Bauer, Matthew O'Gorman, Maximilian Bosch, Michael Bishop, "
"Michael Fiano, Michael Mercier, Michael Raskin, Michael Weiss, Nicolas "
"Dudebout, Peter Simons, Ryan Trinkle, Samuel Dionne-Riel, Sean Seefried, "
"Shea Levy, Symphorien Gibol, Tim Engler, Tim Sears, Tuomas Tynkkynen, volth, "
"Will Dietz, Yorick van Pelt and zimbatm."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:1
msgid "Release 2.10 (2022-07-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix repl` now takes installables on the command line, unifying the usage "
"with other commands that use `--file` and `--expr`. Primary breaking change "
"is for the common usage of `nix repl '<nixpkgs>'` which can be recovered "
"with `nix repl --file '<nixpkgs>'` or `nix repl --expr 'import <nixpkgs>{}'`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:8
msgid "This is currently guarded by the `repl-flake` experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:10
msgid ""
"A new function `builtins.traceVerbose` is available. It is similar to "
"`builtins.trace` if the `trace-verbose` setting is set to true, and it is a "
"no-op otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:14
msgid "`nix search` has a new flag `--exclude` to filter out packages."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:16
msgid ""
"On Linux, if `/nix` doesn't exist and cannot be created and you're not "
"running as root, Nix will automatically use `~/.local/share/nix/root` as a "
"chroot store. This enables non-root users to download the statically linked "
"Nix binary and have it work out of the box, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:28
msgid "`flake-registry.json` is now fetched from `channels.nixos.org`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.10.md:30
msgid ""
"Nix can now be built with LTO by passing `--enable-lto` to `configure`. LTO "
"is currently only supported when building with GCC."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.11.md:1
msgid "Release 2.11 (2022-08-24)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.11.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix copy` now copies the store paths in parallel as much as possible "
"(again). This doesn't apply for the `daemon` and `ssh-ng` stores which copy "
"everything in one batch to avoid latencies issues."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:1
msgid "Release 2.12 (2022-12-06)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:3
msgid ""
"On Linux, Nix can now run builds in a user namespace where they run as root "
"(UID 0) and have 65,536 UIDs available. This is primarily useful for running "
"containers such as `systemd-nspawn` inside a Nix build. For an example, see "
"[`tests/systemd-nspawn/nix`](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/blob/"
"67bcb99700a0da1395fa063d7c6586740b304598/tests/systemd-nspawn.nix.)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:10
msgid "A build can enable this by setting the derivation attribute:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:12
msgid ""
"```\n"
"requiredSystemFeatures = [ \"uid-range\" ];\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:16
msgid ""
"The `uid-range` [system feature](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-system-"
"features) requires the [`auto-allocate-uids`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-auto-allocate-uids) setting to be enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:21
msgid ""
"Nix can now automatically pick UIDs for builds, removing the need to create "
"`nixbld*` user accounts. See [`auto-allocate-uids`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-auto-allocate-uids)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:26
msgid ""
"On Linux, Nix has experimental support for running builds inside a cgroup. "
"See [`use-cgroups`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-cgroups)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:30
msgid ""
"`<nix/fetchurl.nix>` now accepts an additional argument `impure` which "
"defaults to `false`.  If it is set to `true`, the `hash` and `sha256` "
"arguments will be ignored and the resulting derivation will have `__impure` "
"set to `true`, making it an impure derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:35
msgid ""
"If `builtins.readFile` is called on a file with context, then only the parts "
"of the context that appear in the content of the file are retained.  This "
"avoids a lot of spurious errors where strings end up having a context just "
"because they are read from a store path ([\\#7260](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/7260))."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.12.md:41
msgid ""
"`nix build --json` now prints some statistics about top-level derivations, "
"such as CPU statistics when cgroups are enabled."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:1
msgid "Release 2.13 (2023-01-17)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:3
msgid ""
"The `repeat` and `enforce-determinism` options have been removed since they "
"had been broken under many circumstances for a long time."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:6
msgid ""
"You can now use [flake references](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"flake.md#flake-references) in the [old command line interface](../command-"
"ref/main-commands.md), e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:18
msgid ""
"Instead of \"antiquotation\", the more common term [string interpolation](../"
"language/string-interpolation.md) is now used consistently. Historical "
"release notes were not changed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:21
msgid ""
"Error traces have been reworked to provide detailed explanations and more "
"accurate error locations. A short excerpt of the trace is now shown by "
"default when an error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:25
msgid ""
"Allow explicitly selecting outputs in a store derivation installable, just "
"like we can do with other sorts of installables. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:30
msgid "now works just as"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:34
msgid "does already."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:36
msgid ""
"On Linux, `nix develop` now sets the [_personality_](https://man7.org/linux/"
"man-pages/man2/personality.2.html) for the development shell in the same way "
"as the actual build of the derivation. This makes shells for `i686-linux` "
"derivations work correctly on `x86_64-linux`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.13.md:42
msgid ""
"You can now disable the global flake registry by setting the `flake-"
"registry` configuration option to an empty string. The same can be achieved "
"at runtime with `--flake-registry \"\"`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:1
msgid "Release 2.14 (2023-02-28)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:3
msgid ""
"A new function `builtins.readFileType` is available. It is similar to "
"`builtins.readDir` but acts on a single file or directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:6
msgid ""
"In flakes, the `.outPath` attribute of a flake now always refers to the "
"directory containing the `flake.nix`. This was not the case for when "
"`flake.nix` was in a subdirectory of e.g. a Git repository. The root of the "
"source of a flake in a subdirectory is still available in "
"`.sourceInfo.outPath`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:12
msgid ""
"In derivations that use structured attributes, you can now use "
"`unsafeDiscardReferences` to disable scanning a given output for runtime "
"dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:18
msgid ""
"This is useful e.g. when generating self-contained filesystem images with "
"their own embedded Nix store: hashes found inside such an image refer to the "
"embedded store and not to the host's Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.14.md:22
msgid "This requires the `discard-references` experimental feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:1
msgid "Release 2.15 (2023-04-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:3
msgid ""
"Commands which take installables on the command line can now read them from "
"the standard input if passed the `--stdin` flag. This is primarily useful "
"when you have a large amount of paths which exceed the OS argument limit."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:7
msgid ""
"The `nix-hash` command now supports Base64 and SRI. Use the flags `--base64` "
"or `--sri` to specify the format of output hash as Base64 or SRI, and `--to-"
"base64` or `--to-sri` to convert a hash to Base64 or SRI format, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:11
msgid ""
"As the choice of hash formats is no longer binary, the `--base16` flag is "
"also added to explicitly specify the Base16 format, which is still the "
"default."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:14
msgid ""
"The special handling of an [installable](../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix.md#installables) with `.drv` suffix being interpreted as all of the "
"given [store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-store-derivation)'s output "
"paths is removed, and instead taken as the literal store path that it "
"represents."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:16
msgid ""
"The new `^` syntax for store paths introduced in Nix 2.13 allows explicitly "
"referencing output paths of a derivation. Using this is better and more "
"clear than relying on the now-removed `.drv` special handling."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:24
msgid "now gives info about the derivation itself, while"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:29
msgid "provides information about each of its outputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:31
msgid "The experimental command `nix describe-stores` has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:33
msgid ""
"Nix stores and their settings are now documented in [`nix help-stores`](../"
"command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-stores.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:35
msgid ""
"Documentation for operations of `nix-store` and `nix-env` are now available "
"on separate pages of the manual. They include all common options that can be "
"specified and common environment variables that affect these commands."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:38
msgid "These pages can be viewed offline with `man` using"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:40
msgid "`man nix-store-<operation>` and `man nix-env-<operation>`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:41
msgid "`nix-store --help --<operation>` and `nix-env --help --<operation>`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:43
msgid ""
"Nix when used as a client now checks whether the store (the server) trusts "
"the client. (The store always had to check whether it trusts the client, but "
"now the client is informed of the store's decision.) This is useful for "
"scripting interactions with (non-legacy-ssh) remote Nix stores."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:47
msgid "`nix store ping` and `nix doctor` now display this information."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:49
msgid ""
"The new command `nix derivation add` allows adding derivations to the store "
"without involving the Nix language. It exists to round out our collection of "
"basic utility/plumbing commands, and allow for a low barrier-to-entry way of "
"experimenting with alternative front-ends to the Nix Store. It uses the same "
"JSON layout as `nix derivation show`, and is its inverse."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:53
msgid ""
"`nix show-derivation` has been renamed to `nix derivation show`. This "
"matches `nix derivation add`, and avoids bloating the top-level namespace. "
"The old name is still kept as an alias for compatibility, however."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.15.md:57
msgid ""
"The `nix derivation {add,show}` JSON format now includes the derivation name "
"as a top-level field. This is useful in general, but especially necessary "
"for the `add` direction, as otherwise we would need to pass in the name out "
"of band for certain cases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.16.md:1
msgid "Release 2.16 (2023-05-31)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.16.md:3
msgid ""
"Speed-up of downloads from binary caches. The number of parallel downloads "
"(also known as substitutions) has been separated from the [`--max-jobs` "
"setting](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-max-jobs). The new setting is "
"called [`max-substitution-jobs`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-max-"
"substitution-jobs). The number of parallel downloads is now set to 16 by "
"default (previously, the default was 1 due to the coupling to build jobs)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.16.md:8
msgid ""
"The function [`builtins.replaceStrings`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-"
"replaceStrings) is now lazy in the value of its second argument `to`. That "
"is, `to` is only evaluated when its corresponding pattern in `from` is "
"matched in the string `s`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:1
msgid "Release 2.17 (2023-07-24)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:3
msgid ""
"[`nix-channel`](../command-ref/nix-channel.md) now supports a `--list-"
"generations` subcommand."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:5
msgid ""
"The function [`builtins.fetchClosure`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-"
"fetchClosure) can now fetch input-addressed paths in [pure evaluation mode]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-pure-eval), as those are not impure."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:7
msgid ""
"Nix now allows unprivileged/[`allowed-users`](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-allowed-users) to sign paths. Previously, only [`trusted-users`]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-trusted-users) users could sign paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:10
msgid ""
"Nested dynamic attributes are now merged correctly by the parser. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:12
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{\n"
"  nested = {\n"
"    foo = 1;\n"
"  };\n"
"  nested = {\n"
"    ${\"ba\" + \"r\"} = 2;\n"
"  };\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:23
msgid ""
"This used to silently discard `nested.bar`, but now behaves as one would "
"expect and evaluates to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:29
msgid ""
"Note that the feature of merging multiple _full declarations_ of attribute "
"sets like `nested` in the example is of questionable value. It allows "
"writing expressions that are very hard to read, for instance when there are "
"many lines of code between two declarations of the same attribute. This has "
"been around for a long time and is therefore supported for backwards "
"compatibility, but should not be relied upon."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:33
msgid "Instead, consider using the _nested attribute path_ syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:35
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"{\n"
"  nested.foo = 1;\n"
"  nested.${\"ba\" + \"r\"} = 2;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.17.md:42
msgid ""
"Tarball flakes can now redirect to an \"immutable\" URL that will be "
"recorded in lock files. This allows the use of \"mutable\" tarball URLs like "
"`https://example.org/hello/latest.tar.gz` in flakes. See the [tarball "
"fetcher](../protocols/tarball-fetcher.md) for details."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:1
msgid "Release 2.18 (2023-09-20)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:3
msgid ""
"Two new builtin functions, [`builtins.parseFlakeRef`](../language/"
"builtins.md#builtins-parseFlakeRef) and [`builtins.flakeRefToString`](../"
"language/builtins.md#builtins-flakeRefToString), have been added. These "
"functions are useful for converting between flake references encoded as "
"attribute sets and URLs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:10
msgid ""
"[`builtins.toJSON`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-parseFlakeRef) now "
"prints [\\--show-trace](../command-ref/conf-file.html#conf-show-trace) items "
"for the path in which it finds an evaluation error."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:12
msgid ""
"Error messages regarding malformed input to [`nix derivation add`](../"
"command-ref/new-cli/nix3-derivation-add.md) are now clearer and more "
"detailed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:14
msgid ""
"The `discard-references` feature has been stabilized. This means that the "
"[unsafeDiscardReferences](../language/advanced-attributes.md#adv-attr-"
"unsafeDiscardReferences) attribute is no longer guarded by an experimental "
"flag and can be used freely."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:20
msgid ""
"The JSON output for derived paths which are store paths is now a string, not "
"an object with a single `path` field. This only affects `nix-build --json` "
"when \"building\" non-derivation things like fetched sources, which is a no-"
"op."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:23
msgid ""
"A new builtin [`outputOf`](../language/builtins.md#builtins-outputOf) has "
"been added. It is part of the [`dynamic-derivations`](../development/"
"experimental-features.md#xp-feature-dynamic-derivations) experimental "
"feature."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:26
msgid ""
"Flake follow paths at depths greater than 2 are now handled correctly, "
"preventing \"follows a non-existent input\" errors."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.18.md:28
msgid ""
"[`nix-store --query`](../command-ref/nix-store/query.md) gained a new type "
"of query: `--valid-derivers`. It returns all `.drv` files in the local store "
"that _can be_ used to build the output passed in argument. This is in "
"contrast to `--deriver`, which returns the single `.drv` file that _was "
"actually_ used to build the output passed in argument. In case the output "
"was substituted from a binary cache, this `.drv` file may only exist on said "
"binary cache and not locally."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:1
msgid "Release 2.19 (2023-11-17)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:3
msgid ""
"The experimental `nix` command can now act as a [shebang interpreter](../"
"command-ref/new-cli/nix.md#shebang-interpreter) by appending the contents of "
"any `#! nix` lines and the script's location into a single call."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:6
msgid ""
"[URL flake references](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md#flake-"
"references) now support [percent-encoded](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/"
"html/rfc3986#section-2.1) characters."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:8
msgid ""
"[Path-like flake references](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake.md#path-like-"
"syntax) now accept arbitrary unicode characters (except `#` and `?`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:10
msgid ""
"The experimental feature `repl-flake` is no longer needed, as its "
"functionality is now part of the `flakes` experimental feature. To get the "
"previous behavior, use the `--file/--expr` flags accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:12
msgid ""
"There is a new flake installable syntax `flakeref#.attrPath` where the \".\" "
"prefix specifies that `attrPath` is interpreted from the root of the flake "
"outputs, with no searching of default attribute prefixes like `packages."
"<SYSTEM>` or `legacyPackages.<SYSTEM>`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:14
msgid ""
"Nix adds `apple-virt` to the default system features on macOS systems that "
"support virtualization. This is similar to what's done for the `kvm` system "
"feature on Linux hosts."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:16
msgid ""
"Add a new built-in function [`builtins.convertHash`](../language/"
"builtins.md#builtins-convertHash)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:18
msgid "`nix-shell` shebang lines now support single-quoted arguments."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:20
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchTree` is now its own experimental feature, [`fetch-tree`](../"
"development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-fetch-tree). This allows "
"stabilising it independently of the rest of what is encompassed by [`flakes`]"
"(../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-flakes)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:23
msgid "The interface for creating and updating lock files has been overhauled:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:25
msgid ""
"[`nix flake lock`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-lock.md) only creates "
"lock files and adds missing inputs now. It will _never_ update existing "
"inputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:28
msgid ""
"[`nix flake update`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-update.md) does the "
"same, but _will_ update inputs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:29
msgid ""
"Passing no arguments will update all inputs of the current flake, just like "
"it already did."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:30
msgid ""
"Passing input names as arguments will ensure only those are updated. This "
"replaces the functionality of `nix flake lock --update-input`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:31
msgid ""
"To operate on a flake outside the current directory, you must now pass `--"
"flake path/to/flake`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:33
msgid ""
"The flake-specific flags `--recreate-lock-file` and `--update-input` have "
"been removed from all commands operating on installables. They are "
"superseded by `nix flake update`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:36
msgid ""
"Commit signature verification for the [`builtins.fetchGit`](../language/"
"builtins.md#builtins-fetchGit) is added as the new [`verified-fetches` "
"experimental feature](../development/experimental-features.md#xp-feature-"
"verified-fetches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:38
msgid ""
"[`nix path-info --json`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-path-info.md) "
"(experimental) now returns a JSON map rather than JSON list. The `path` "
"field of each object has instead become the key in the outer map, since it "
"is unique. The `valid` field also goes away because we just use `null` "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:43
msgid "Old way:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:45
msgid ""
"```json5\n"
"[\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"path\": \"/nix/store/fvqsvk65d38p8qqir371ii0hyqxvjcw6-bash-5.2-p15\",\n"
"    \"valid\": true,\n"
"    // ...\n"
"  },\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"path\": \"/nix/store/wffw7l0alvs3iw94cbgi1gmmbmw99sqb-home-manager-"
"path\",\n"
"    \"valid\": false\n"
"  }\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:59
msgid "New way"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:61
msgid ""
"```json5\n"
"{\n"
"  \"/nix/store/fvqsvk65d38p8qqir371ii0hyqxvjcw6-bash-5.2-p15\": {\n"
"    // ...\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"/nix/store/wffw7l0alvs3iw94cbgi1gmmbmw99sqb-home-manager-path\": null,\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:70
msgid ""
"This makes it match `nix derivation show`, which also maps store paths to "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:72
msgid ""
"When Nix is installed using the [binary installer](../installation/"
"installing-binary.md), in supported shells (Bash, Zsh, Fish) "
"[`XDG_DATA_DIRS`](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/"
"basedir-spec-latest.html#variables) is now populated with the path to the `/"
"share` subdirectory of the current profile. This means that command "
"completion scripts, `.desktop` files, and similar artifacts installed via "
"[`nix-env`](../command-ref/nix-env.md) or [`nix profile`](../command-ref/new-"
"cli/nix3-profile.md) (experimental) can be found by any program that follows "
"the [XDG Base Directory Specification](https://"
"specifications.freedesktop.org/basedir-spec/basedir-spec-latest.html)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:77
msgid ""
"A new command `nix store add` has been added. It replaces `nix store add-"
"file` and `nix store add-path` which are now deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:79
msgid ""
"A new option [`always-allow-substitutes`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"always-allow-substitutes) has been added."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.19.md:81
msgid ""
"When set to `true`, Nix will always try to substitute a derivation, even if "
"it has the \\[`allowSubstitutes`\\]{#adv-attr-allowSubstitutes} attribute "
"set to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:1
msgid "Release 2.2 (2019-01-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:3
msgid "This is primarily a bug fix release. It also has the following changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:5
msgid ""
"In derivations that use structured attributes (i.e. that specify set the "
"`__structuredAttrs` attribute to `true` to cause all attributes to be passed "
"to the builder in JSON format), you can now specify closure checks per "
"output, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:10
msgid ""
"    outputChecks.\"out\" = {\n"
"      # The closure of 'out' must not be larger than 256 MiB.\n"
"      maxClosureSize = 256 * 1024 * 1024;\n"
"    \n"
"      # It must not refer to C compiler or to the 'dev' output.\n"
"      disallowedRequisites = [ stdenv.cc \"dev\" ];\n"
"    };\n"
"    \n"
"    outputChecks.\"dev\" = {\n"
"      # The 'dev' output must not be larger than 128 KiB.\n"
"      maxSize = 128 * 1024;\n"
"    };\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:23
msgid ""
"The derivation attribute `requiredSystemFeatures` is now enforced for local "
"builds, and not just to route builds to remote builders. The supported "
"features of a machine can be specified through the configuration setting "
"`system-features`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:28
msgid ""
"By default, `system-features` includes `kvm` if `/dev/kvm` exists. For "
"compatibility, it also includes the pseudo-features `nixos-test`, "
"`benchmark` and `big-parallel` which are used by Nixpkgs to route builds to "
"particular Hydra build machines."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:33
msgid "Sandbox builds are now enabled by default on Linux."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:35
msgid ""
"The new command `nix doctor` shows potential issues with your Nix "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:38
msgid ""
"The `fetchGit` builtin function now uses a caching scheme that puts "
"different remote repositories in distinct local repositories, rather than a "
"single shared repository. This may require more disk space but is faster."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:43
msgid "The `dirOf` builtin function now works on relative paths."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:45
msgid ""
"Nix now supports [SRI hashes](https://www.w3.org/TR/SRI/), allowing the hash "
"algorithm and hash to be specified in a single string. For example, you can "
"write:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:49
msgid ""
"    import <nix/fetchurl.nix> {\n"
"      url = https://nixos.org/releases/nix/nix-2.1.3/nix-2.1.3.tar.xz;\n"
"      hash = \"sha256-XSLa0FjVyADWWhFfkZ2iKTjFDda6mMXjoYMXLRSYQKQ=\";\n"
"    };\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:54
msgid "instead of"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:56
msgid ""
"    import <nix/fetchurl.nix> {\n"
"      url = https://nixos.org/releases/nix/nix-2.1.3/nix-2.1.3.tar.xz;\n"
"      sha256 = "
"\"5d22dad058d5c800d65a115f919da22938c50dd6ba98c5e3a183172d149840a4\";\n"
"    };\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:61
msgid ""
"In fixed-output derivations, the `outputHashAlgo` attribute is no longer "
"mandatory if `outputHash` specifies the hash."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:64
msgid ""
"`nix hash-file` and `nix                 hash-path` now print hashes in SRI "
"format by default. They also use SHA-256 by default instead of SHA-512 "
"because that's what we use most of the time in Nixpkgs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:69
msgid "Integers are now 64 bits on all platforms."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:71
msgid ""
"The evaluator now prints profiling statistics (enabled via the "
"`NIX_SHOW_STATS` and `NIX_COUNT_CALLS` environment variables) in JSON format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:75
msgid ""
"The option `--xml` in `nix-store                 --query` has been removed. "
"Instead, there now is an option `--graphml` to output the dependency graph "
"in GraphML format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:79
msgid ""
"All `nix-*` commands are now symlinks to `nix`. This saves a bit of disk "
"space."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.2.md:82
msgid "`nix repl` now uses `libeditline` or `libreadline`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:1
msgid "Release 2.20.0 (2024-01-29)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:3
msgid ""
"Option `allowed-uris` can now match whole schemes in URIs without slashes "
"[\\#9547](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9547)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:5
msgid ""
"If a scheme, such as `github:` is specified in the `allowed-uris` option, "
"all URIs starting with `github:` are allowed. Previously this only worked "
"for schemes whose URIs used the `://` syntax."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:8
msgid ""
"Include cgroup stats when building through the daemon [\\#9598](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9598)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:10
msgid ""
"Nix now also reports cgroup statistics when building through the Nix daemon "
"and when doing remote builds using `ssh-ng`, if both sides of the connection "
"are using Nix 2.20 or newer."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:13
msgid ""
"Disallow empty search regex in `nix search` [\\#9481](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/9481)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:15
msgid ""
"[`nix search`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-search.md) now requires a search "
"regex to be passed. To show all packages, use `^`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:17
msgid ""
"Add new `eval-system` setting [\\#4093](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"4093)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:19
msgid ""
"Add a new `eval-system` option. Unlike `system`, it just overrides the value "
"of `builtins.currentSystem`. This is more useful than overriding `system`, "
"because you can build these derivations on remote builders which can work on "
"the given system. In contrast, `system` also affects scheduling which will "
"cause Nix to build those derivations locally even if that doesn't make sense."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:24
msgid ""
"`eval-system` only takes effect if it is non-empty. If empty (the default) "
"`system` is used as before, so there is no breakage."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:27
msgid ""
"Import-from-derivation builds the derivation in the build store [\\#9661]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9661)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:29
msgid ""
"When using `--eval-store`, `import`ing from a derivation will now result in "
"the derivation being built on the build store, i.e. the store specified in "
"the `store` Nix option."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:31
msgid ""
"Because the resulting Nix expression must be copied back to the evaluation "
"store in order to be imported, this requires the evaluation store to trust "
"the build store's signatures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:33
msgid ""
"Mounted SSH Store [\\#7890](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/7890) "
"[\\#7912](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/7912)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:35
msgid ""
"Introduced the store [`mounted-ssh-ng://`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-"
"stores.md). This store allows full access to a Nix store on a remote machine "
"and additionally requires that the store be mounted in the local filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:38
msgid ""
"Rename `nix show-config` to `nix config show` [\\#7672](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/7672) [\\#9477](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9477)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:40
msgid ""
"`nix show-config` was renamed to `nix config show`, and `nix doctor` was "
"renamed to `nix config check`, to be more consistent with the rest of the "
"command line interface."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:42
msgid ""
"Add command `nix hash convert` [\\#9452](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"9452)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:44
msgid ""
"This replaces the old `nix hash to-*` commands, which are still available "
"but will emit a deprecation warning. Please convert as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:46
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-base16 $hash1 $hash2`: Use `nix hash convert --to base16 $hash1 "
"$hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:47
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-base32 $hash1 $hash2`: Use `nix hash convert --to nix32 $hash1 "
"$hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:48
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-base64 $hash1 $hash2`: Use `nix hash convert --to base64 $hash1 "
"$hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:49
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-sri $hash1 $hash2`: : Use `nix hash convert --to sri $hash1 "
"$hash2` or even just `nix hash convert $hash1 $hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:51
msgid ""
"Rename hash format `base32` to `nix32` [\\#9452](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9452)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:53
msgid ""
"Hash format `base32` was renamed to `nix32` since it used a special Nix-"
"specific character set for [Base32](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base32)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:56
msgid ""
"`nix profile` now allows referring to elements by human-readable names "
"[\\#8678](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/8678)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:58
msgid ""
"[`nix profile`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md) now uses names to "
"refer to installed packages when running [`list`](../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix3-profile-list.md), [`remove`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-"
"remove.md) or [`upgrade`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-upgrade.md) as "
"opposed to indices. Profile element names are generated when a package is "
"installed and remain the same until the package is removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:60
msgid ""
"**Warning**: The `manifest.nix` file used to record the contents of profiles "
"has changed. Nix will automatically upgrade profiles to the new version when "
"you modify the profile. After that, the profile can no longer be used by "
"older versions of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:62
msgid ""
"Give `nix store add` a `--hash-algo` flag [\\#9809](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9809)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:64
msgid ""
"Adds a missing feature that was present in the old CLI, and matches our "
"plans to have similar flags for `nix hash convert` and `nix hash path`."
