#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:156
msgid ""
"Better error reporting for `with` expressions [\\#9658](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/9658)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:158
msgid ""
"`with` expressions using non-attrset values to resolve variables are now "
"reported with proper positions, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:171
msgid ""
"Functions are printed with more detail [\\#7145](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/7145) [\\#9606](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9606)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:173
msgid ""
"`nix repl`, `nix eval`, `builtins.trace`, and most other places values are "
"printed will now include function names and source location information:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:176
msgid ""
"```\n"
"$ nix repl nixpkgs\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.map\n"
"«primop map»\n"
"\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.map lib.id\n"
"«partially applied primop map»\n"
"\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.trace lib.id \"my-value\"\n"
"trace: «lambda id @ /nix/store/kgr5lnaiiv08wb7k324yv1i1npjmrvjc-source/lib/"
"trivial.nix:26:5»\n"
"\"my-value\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:189
msgid ""
"Flake operations like `nix develop` will no longer fail when run in a Git "
"repository where the `flake.lock` file is `.gitignore`d [\\#8854](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/8854) [\\#9324](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/9324)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:194
msgid ""
"Nix commands will now respect Ctrl-C [\\#7145](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/7145) [\\#6995](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/6995) [\\#9687]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9687)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:199
msgid ""
"Previously, many Nix commands would hang indefinitely if Ctrl-C was pressed "
"while performing various operations (including `nix develop`, `nix flake "
"update`, and so on). With several fixes to Nix's signal handlers, Nix "
"commands will now exit quickly after Ctrl-C is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:204
msgid ""
"`nix copy` to a `ssh-ng` store now needs `--substitute-on-destination` "
"(a.k.a. `-s`) in order to substitute paths on the remote store instead of "
"copying them. The behavior is consistent with `nix copy` to a different kind "
"of remote store. Previously this behavior was controlled by the `builders-"
"use-substitutes` setting and `--substitute-on-destination` was ignored."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:1
msgid "Release 2.21.0 (2024-03-11)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:3
msgid "Fix a fixed-output derivation sandbox escape (CVE-2024-27297)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:5
msgid ""
"Cooperating Nix derivations could send file descriptors to files in the Nix "
"store to each other via Unix domain sockets in the abstract namespace. This "
"allowed one derivation to modify the output of the other derivation, after "
"Nix has registered the path as \"valid\" and immutable in the Nix database. "
"In particular, this allowed the output of fixed-output derivations to be "
"modified from their expected content."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:12
msgid "This isn't the case any more."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:14
msgid ""
"CLI options `--arg-from-file` and `--arg-from-stdin` [\\#10122](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10122)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:16
msgid ""
"The new CLI option `--arg-from-file` _name_ _path_ passes the contents of "
"file _path_ as a string value via the function argument _name_ to a Nix "
"expression. Similarly, the new option `--arg-from-stdin` _name_ reads the "
"contents of the string from standard input."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:21
msgid ""
"Concise error printing in `nix repl` [\\#9928](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/9928)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:23
msgid ""
"Previously, if an element of a list or attribute set threw an error while "
"evaluating, `nix repl` would print the entire error (including source "
"location information) inline. This output was clumsy and difficult to parse:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:27
msgid ""
"```\n"
"nix-repl> { err = builtins.throw \"uh oh!\"; }\n"
"{ err = «error:\n"
"       … while calling the 'throw' builtin\n"
"         at «string»:1:9:\n"
"            1| { err = builtins.throw \"uh oh!\"; }\n"
"             |         ^\n"
"\n"
"       error: uh oh!»; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:38
msgid ""
"Now, only the error message is displayed, making the output much more "
"readable."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:39
msgid ""
"```\n"
"nix-repl> { err = builtins.throw \"uh oh!\"; }\n"
"{ err = «error: uh oh!»; }\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:44
msgid ""
"However, if the whole expression being evaluated throws an error, source "
"locations and (if applicable) a stack trace are printed, just like you'd "
"expect:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:47
msgid ""
"```\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.throw \"uh oh!\"\n"
"error:\n"
"       … while calling the 'throw' builtin\n"
"         at «string»:1:1:\n"
"            1| builtins.throw \"uh oh!\"\n"
"             | ^\n"
"\n"
"       error: uh oh!\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:58
msgid ""
"`--debugger` can now access bindings from `let` expressions [\\#8827]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/8827) [\\#9918](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/9918)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:60
msgid ""
"Breakpoints and errors in the bindings of a `let` expression can now access "
"those bindings in the debugger. Previously, only the body of `let` "
"expressions could access those bindings."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:64
msgid ""
"Enter the `--debugger` when `builtins.trace` is called if `debugger-on-"
"trace` is set [\\#9914](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9914)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:66
msgid ""
"If the `debugger-on-trace` option is set and `--debugger` is given, "
"`builtins.trace` calls will behave similarly to `builtins.break` and will "
"enter the debug REPL. This is useful for determining where warnings are "
"being emitted from."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:71
msgid ""
"Debugger prints source position information [\\#9913](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/9913)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:73
msgid ""
"The `--debugger` now prints source location information, instead of the "
"pointers of source location information. Before:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:94
msgid ""
"The `--debugger` will start more reliably in `let` expressions and function "
"calls [\\#6649](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/6649) [\\#9917](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9917)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:96
msgid "Previously, if you attempted to evaluate this file with the debugger:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:98
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"let\n"
"  a = builtins.trace \"before inner break\" (\n"
"    builtins.break \"hello\"\n"
"  );\n"
"  b = builtins.trace \"before outer break\" (\n"
"    builtins.break a\n"
"  );\n"
"in\n"
"  b\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:110
msgid ""
"Nix would correctly enter the debugger at `builtins.break a`, but if you "
"asked it to `:continue`, it would skip over the `builtins.break \"hello\"` "
"expression entirely."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:114
msgid "Now, Nix will correctly enter the debugger at both breakpoints."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:116
msgid ""
"Nested debuggers are no longer supported [\\#9920](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9920)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:118
msgid ""
"Previously, evaluating an expression that throws an error in the debugger "
"would enter a second, nested debugger:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:121
msgid ""
"```\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.throw \"what\"\n"
"error: what\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Starting REPL to allow you to inspect the current state of the evaluator.\n"
"\n"
"Welcome to Nix 2.18.1. Type :? for help.\n"
"\n"
"nix-repl>\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:133
msgid "Now, it just prints the error message like `nix repl`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:135
msgid ""
"```\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.throw \"what\"\n"
"error:\n"
"       … while calling the 'throw' builtin\n"
"         at «string»:1:1:\n"
"            1| builtins.throw \"what\"\n"
"             | ^\n"
"\n"
"       error: what\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:146
msgid ""
"Consistent order of function arguments in printed expressions [\\#9874]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9874)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:148
msgid ""
"Function arguments are now printed in lexicographic order rather than the "
"internal, creation-time based symbol order."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:150
msgid ""
"Fix duplicate attribute error positions for `inherit` [\\#9874](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9874)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:152
msgid ""
"When an `inherit` caused a duplicate attribute error the position of the "
"error was not reported correctly, placing the error with the inherit itself "
"or at the start of the bindings block instead of the offending attribute "
"name."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:154
msgid ""
"`inherit (x) ...` evaluates `x` only once [\\#9847](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9847)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:156
msgid ""
"`inherit (x) a b ...` now evaluates the expression `x` only once for all "
"inherited attributes rather than once for each inherited attribute. This "
"does not usually have a measurable impact, but side-effects (such as "
"`builtins.trace`) would be duplicated and expensive expressions (such as "
"derivations) could cause a measurable slowdown."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:159
msgid ""
"Store paths are allowed to start with `.` [\\#912](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/912) [\\#9091](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9091) [\\#9095]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9095) [\\#9120](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9120) [\\#9121](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9121) [\\#9122]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9122) [\\#9130](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9130) [\\#9219](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9219) [\\#9224]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9224) [\\#9867](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9867)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:161
msgid ""
"Leading periods were allowed by accident in Nix 2.4. The Nix team has "
"considered this to be a bug, but this behavior has since been relied on by "
"users, leading to unnecessary difficulties. From now on, leading periods are "
"supported. The names `.` and `..` are disallowed, as well as those starting "
"with `.-` or `..-`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:164
msgid ""
"Nix versions that denied leading periods are documented [in the issue]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/912#issuecomment-1919583286)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:166
msgid ""
"`nix repl` pretty-prints values [\\#9931](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"9931)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:168
msgid "`nix repl` will now pretty-print values:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:188
msgid ""
"Introduction of `--regex` and `--all` in `nix profile remove` and `nix "
"profile upgrade` [\\#10166](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10166)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:190
msgid ""
"Previously the command-line arguments for `nix profile remove` and `nix "
"profile upgrade` matched the package entries using regular expression. For "
"instance:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:197
msgid "This would remove all packages that contain `vim` in their name."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:199
msgid ""
"In most cases, only singular package names were used to remove and upgrade "
"packages. Mixing this with regular expressions sometimes lead to unintended "
"behavior. For instance, `python3.1` could match `python311`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:201
msgid ""
"To avoid unintended behavior, the arguments are now only matching exact "
"names."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:203
msgid ""
"Matching using regular expressions is still possible by using the new `--"
"regex` flag:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:209
msgid ""
"One of the most useful cases for using regular expressions was to upgrade "
"all packages. This was previously accomplished by:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:215
msgid ""
"With the introduction of the `--all` flag, this now becomes more "
"straightforward:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:221
msgid ""
"Visual clutter in `--debugger` is reduced [\\#9919](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9919)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:256
msgid ""
"Cycle detection in `nix repl` is simpler and more reliable [\\#8672](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/8672) [\\#9926](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/9926)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:258
msgid ""
"The cycle detection in `nix repl`, `nix eval`, `builtins.trace`, and "
"everywhere else values are printed is now simpler and matches the cycle "
"detection in `nix-instantiate --eval` output."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:275
msgid ""
"In the debugger, `while evaluating the attribute` errors now include "
"position information [\\#9915](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9915)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:296
msgid ""
"Stack size is increased on macOS [\\#9860](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"9860)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.21.md:298
msgid ""
"Previously, Nix would set the stack size to 64MiB on Linux, but would leave "
"the stack size set to the default (approximately 8KiB) on macOS. Now, the "
"stack size is correctly set to 64MiB on macOS as well, which should reduce "
"stack overflow segfaults in deeply-recursive Nix expressions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.22.md:1
msgid "Release 2.22.0 (2024-04-23)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.22.md:3
msgid "Significant changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.22.md:5
msgid ""
"Remove experimental repl-flake [\\#10103](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/10103) [\\#10299](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10299)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.22.md:7
msgid ""
"The `repl-flake` experimental feature has been removed. The `nix repl` "
"command now works like the rest of the new CLI in that `nix repl {path}` now "
"tries to load a flake at `{path}` (or fails if the `flakes` experimental "
"feature isn't enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.22.md:9
msgid "Other changes"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.22.md:11
msgid ""
"`nix eval` prints derivations as `.drv` paths [\\#10200](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/10200)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.22.md:13
msgid ""
"`nix eval` will now print derivations as their `.drv` paths, rather than as "
"attribute sets. This makes commands like `nix eval nixpkgs#bash` terminate "
"instead of infinitely looping into recursive self-referential attributes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:1
msgid "Release 2.23.0 (2024-06-03)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:3
msgid ""
"New builtin: `builtins.warn` [\\#306026](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/"
"306026) [\\#10592](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10592)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:5
msgid ""
"`builtins.warn` behaves like `builtins.trace \"warning: ${msg}\"`, has an "
"accurate log level, and is controlled by the options [`debugger-on-trace`]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-debugger-on-trace), [`debugger-on-warn`]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-debugger-on-warn) and [`abort-on-warn`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-abort-on-warn)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:10
msgid "Make `nix build --keep-going` consistent with `nix-build --keep-going`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:12
msgid ""
"This means that if e.g. multiple fixed-output derivations fail to build, all "
"hash mismatches are displayed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:15
msgid ""
"Modify `nix derivation {add,show}` JSON format [\\#9866](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/9866) [\\#10722](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10722)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:17
msgid ""
"The JSON format for derivations has been slightly revised to better conform "
"to our [data modeling guidelines](../development/data-modeling.md). In "
"particular, the hash algorithm and content addressing method of content-"
"addressed derivation outputs are now separated into two fields `hashAlgo` "
"and `method`, rather than one field with an arcane `:`\\-separated format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:21
msgid ""
"This JSON format is only used by the experimental `nix derivation` family of "
"commands, at this time. Future revisions are expected as the JSON format is "
"still not entirely in compliance even after these changes."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:24
msgid ""
"Warn on unknown settings anywhere in the command line [\\#10701](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10701)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:26
msgid ""
"All `nix` commands will now properly warn when an unknown option is "
"specified anywhere in the command line."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:50
msgid ""
"`nix env shell` is the new `nix shell`, and `nix shell` remains an accepted "
"alias [\\#10504](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/10504) [\\#10807]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10807)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:52
msgid ""
"This is part of an effort to bring more structure to the CLI subcommands."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:54
msgid ""
"`nix env` will be about the process environment. Future commands may include "
"`nix env run` and `nix env print-env`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:57
msgid ""
"It is also somewhat analogous to the [planned](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/10504) `nix dev shell` (currently `nix develop`), which is less about "
"environment variables, and more about running a development shell, which is "
"a more powerful command, but also requires more setup."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:59
msgid ""
"Flake operations that expect derivations now print the failing value and its "
"type [\\#10778](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10778)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:61
msgid ""
"In errors like `flake output attribute 'nixosConfigurations.yuki.config' is "
"not a derivation or path`, the message now includes the failing value and "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:75
msgid ""
"`fetchTree` now fetches Git repositories shallowly by default [\\#10028]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10028)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:77
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchTree` now clones Git repositories shallowly by default, which "
"reduces network traffic and disk usage significantly in many cases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:79
msgid ""
"Previously, the default behavior was to clone the full history of a specific "
"tag or branch (e.g. `ref`) and only afterwards extract the files of one "
"specific revision."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:81
msgid ""
"From now on, the `ref` and `allRefs` arguments will be ignored, except if "
"shallow cloning is disabled by setting `shallow = false`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:83
msgid ""
"The defaults for `builtins.fetchGit` remain unchanged. Here, shallow cloning "
"has to be enabled manually by passing `shallow = true`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:85
msgid ""
"Store object info JSON format now uses `null` rather than omitting fields "
"[\\#9995](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9995)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:87
msgid ""
"The [store object info JSON format](../protocols/json/store-object-info.md), "
"used for e.g. `nix path-info`, no longer omits fields to indicate absent "
"information, but instead includes the fields with a `null` value. For "
"example, `\"ca\": null` is used to indicate a store object that isn't "
"content-addressed rather than omitting the `ca` field entirely. This makes "
"records of this sort more self-describing, and easier to consume "
"programmatically."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:91
msgid ""
"We will follow this design principle going forward; the [data modeling "
"guidelines](../development/data-modeling.md) in the contributing section "
"have been updated accordingly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:94
msgid "Large path warnings [\\#10661](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10661)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.23.md:96
msgid ""
"Nix can now warn when evaluation of a Nix expression causes a large path to "
"be copied to the Nix store. The threshold for this warning can be configured "
"using [the `warn-large-path-threshold` setting](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-warn-large-path-threshold), e.g. `--warn-large-path-threshold "
"100M` will warn about paths larger than 100 MiB."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:1
msgid "Release 2.24.0 (2024-07-31)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:5
msgid "Harden user sandboxing"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:7
msgid ""
"The build directory has been hardened against interference with the outside "
"world by nesting it inside another directory owned by (and only readable by) "
"the daemon user."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:9
msgid ""
"This is a low severity security fix, [CVE-2024-38531](https://www.cve.org/"
"CVERecord?id=CVE-2024-38531)."
