#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:74
msgid ""
"We'd like to acknowledge [Yingchi Long (@inclyc)](https://github.com/inclyc) "
"for proposing a proof of concept for this functionality in [\\#9054](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9054), as well as [@sternenseemann](https://"
"github.com/sternenseemann) and [Johannes Kirschbauer (@hsjobeki)](https://"
"github.com/hsjobeki) for their contributions, proposals, and their work on "
"[RFC 145](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/pull/145)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:82
msgid ""
"Solve `cached failure of attribute X` [\\#9165](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/9165) [\\#10513](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/10513) [\\#10564]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10564)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:84
msgid ""
"This eliminates all \"cached failure of attribute X\" messages by forcing "
"evaluation of the original value when needed to show the exception to the "
"user. This enhancement improves error reporting by providing the underlying "
"message and stack trace."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:86 source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:92
#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:100 source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:262
msgid "Author: [**Eelco Dolstra (@edolstra)**](https://github.com/edolstra)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:88
msgid ""
"Run the flake regressions test suite [\\#10603](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/10603)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:90
msgid ""
"This update introduces a GitHub action to run a subset of the [flake "
"regressions test suite](https://github.com/NixOS/flake-regressions), which "
"includes 259 flakes with their expected evaluation results. Currently, the "
"action runs the first 25 flakes due to the full test suite's extensive "
"runtime. A manually triggered action may be implemented later to run the "
"entire test suite."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:94
msgid ""
"Support unit prefixes in configuration settings [\\#10668](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10668)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:96
msgid ""
"Configuration settings in Nix now support unit prefixes, allowing for more "
"intuitive and readable configurations. For example, you can now specify [`--"
"min-free 1G`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-min-free) to set the minimum "
"free space to 1 gigabyte."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:98
msgid ""
"This enhancement was extracted from [\\#7851](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/7851) and is also useful for PR [\\#10661](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/10661)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:102
msgid ""
"`nix build`: show all FOD errors with `--keep-going` [\\#10734](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10734)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:104
msgid ""
"The [`nix build`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-build.md) command has been "
"updated to improve the behavior of the \\[`--keep-going`\\] flag. Now, when "
"`--keep-going` is used, all hash-mismatch errors of failing fixed-output "
"derivations (FODs) are displayed, similar to the behavior for other build "
"failures. This enhancement ensures that all relevant build errors are shown, "
"making it easier for users to update multiple derivations at once or to "
"diagnose and fix issues."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:106
msgid ""
"Author: [**Jörg Thalheim (@Mic92)**](https://github.com/Mic92), "
"[**Maximilian Bosch (@Ma27)**](https://github.com/Ma27)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:108
msgid "[`--keep-going`](../command-ref/opt-common.md#opt-keep-going)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:110
msgid ""
"Build with Meson [\\#2503](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/2503) "
"[\\#10378](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10378) [\\#10855](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10855) [\\#10904](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/10904) [\\#10908](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10908) [\\#10914]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10914) [\\#10933](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/10933) [\\#10936](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10936) "
"[\\#10954](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10954) [\\#10955](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10955) [\\#10963](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/10963) [\\#10967](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10967) [\\#10973]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/10973) [\\#11034](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/11034) [\\#11054](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11054) "
"[\\#11055](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11055) [\\#11060](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11060) [\\#11064](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/11064) [\\#11155](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11155)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:112
msgid ""
"These changes aim to replace the use of autotools and `make` with Meson for "
"building various components of Nix. Additionally, each library is built in "
"its own derivation, leveraging Meson's \"subprojects\" feature to allow a "
"single development shell for building all libraries while also supporting "
"separate builds. This approach aims to improve productivity and build "
"modularity, compared to both make and a monolithic Meson-based derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:114
msgid ""
"Special thanks to everyone who has contributed to the Meson port, "
"particularly [**@p01arst0rm**](https://github.com/p01arst0rm) and "
"[**@Qyriad**](https://github.com/Qyriad)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:116
msgid ""
"Authors: [**John Ericson (@Ericson2314)**](https://github.com/Ericson2314), "
"[**Tom Bereknyei**](https://github.com/tomberek), [**Théophane Hufschmitt "
"(@thufschmitt)**](https://github.com/thufschmitt), [**Valentin Gagarin "
"(@fricklerhandwerk)**](https://github.com/fricklerhandwerk), [**Robert "
"Hensing (@roberth)**](https://github.com/roberth) Co-authors: "
"[**@p01arst0rm**](https://github.com/p01arst0rm), [**@Qyriad**](https://"
"github.com/Qyriad)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:119
msgid ""
"Evaluation cache: fix cache regressions [\\#10570](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/10570) [\\#11086](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11086)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:121
msgid "This update addresses two bugs in the evaluation cache system:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:123
msgid ""
"Regression in #10570: The evaluation cache was not being persisted in `nix "
"develop`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:124
msgid ""
"Nix could sometimes try to commit the evaluation cache SQLite transaction "
"without there being an active transaction, resulting in non-error errors "
"being printed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:126
msgid "Author: [**Lexi Mattick (@kognise)**](https://github.com/kognise)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:128
msgid ""
"Introduce `libnixflake` [\\#9063](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9063)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:130
msgid ""
"A new library, `libnixflake`, has been introduced to better separate the "
"Flakes layer within Nix. This change refactors the codebase to encapsulate "
"Flakes-specific functionality within its own library."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:132
msgid ""
"See the commits in the pull request for detailed changes, with the only "
"significant code modifications happening in the initial commit."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:134
msgid ""
"This change was alluded to in [RFC 134](https://github.com/nixos/rfcs/blob/"
"master/rfcs/0134-nix-store-layer.md) and is a step towards a more modular "
"and maintainable codebase."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:136
msgid ""
"Author: [**John Ericson (@Ericson2314)**](https://github.com/Ericson2314)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:138
msgid ""
"CLI options `--arg-from-file` and `--arg-from-stdin` [\\#9913](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9913)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:161
msgid "Stop vendoring `toml11`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:163
msgid ""
"We don't apply any patches to it, and vendoring it locks users into bugs (it "
"hasn't been updated since its introduction in late 2021)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:166
msgid "Author: [**Winter (@winterqt)**](https://github.com/winterqt)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:168
msgid ""
"Rename hash format `base32` to `nix32` [\\#8678](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/8678)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:170
msgid ""
"Hash format `base32` was renamed to `nix32` since it used a special nix-"
"specific character set for [Base32](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base32)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:173
msgid "**Deprecation**: Use `nix32` instead of `base32` as `toHashFormat`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:175
msgid ""
"For the builtin `convertHash`, the `toHashFormat` parameter now accepts the "
"same hash formats as the `--to`/`--from` parameters of the `nix hash "
"convert` command: `\"base16\"`, `\"nix32\"`, `\"base64\"`, and `\"sri\"`. "
"The former `\"base32\"` value remains as a deprecated alias for `\"nix32\"`. "
"Please convert your code from:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:179
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.convertHash { inherit hash hashAlgo; toHashFormat = \"base32\";}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:183
msgid "to"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:185
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"builtins.convertHash { inherit hash hashAlgo; toHashFormat = \"nix32\";}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:189
msgid ""
"Add `pipe-operators` experimental feature [\\#11131](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/11131)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:191
msgid ""
"This is a draft implementation of [RFC 0148](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/"
"pull/148)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:193
msgid ""
"The `pipe-operators` experimental feature adds [`<|` and `|>` operators](../"
"language/operators.md#pipe-operators) to the Nix language. _a_ `|>` _b_ is "
"equivalent to the function application _b_ _a_, and _a_ `<|` _b_ is "
"equivalent to the function application _a_ _b_."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:207
msgid ""
"`<|` and `|>` are right and left associative, respectively, and have lower "
"precedence than any other operator. These properties may change in future "
"releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:210
msgid ""
"See [the RFC](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/pull/148) for more examples and "
"rationale."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:214
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` shebang uses relative path [\\#4232](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/4232) [\\#5088](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/5088) [\\#11058]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11058)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:217
msgid ""
"Relative [path](../language/types.md#type-path) literals in `nix-shell` "
"shebang scripts' options are now resolved relative to the [script's location]"
"(../glossary.md?highlight=base%20directory#gloss-base-directory). Previously "
"they were resolved relative to the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:220
msgid "For example, consider the following script in `~/myproject/say-hi`:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:230
msgid ""
"Older versions of `nix-shell` would resolve `shell.nix` relative to the "
"current working directory, such as the user's home directory in this example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:243
msgid ""
"Since this release, `nix-shell` resolves `shell.nix` relative to the "
"script's location, and `~/myproject/shell.nix` is used."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:250
msgid "**Opt-out**"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:252
msgid ""
"This is technically a breaking change, so we have added an option so you can "
"adapt independently of your Nix update. The old behavior can be opted into "
"by setting the option [`nix-shell-shebang-arguments-relative-to-script`](../"
"command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-nix-shell-shebang-arguments-relative-to-"
"script) to `false`. This option will be removed in a future release."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:258
msgid ""
"Improve handling of tarballs that don't consist of a single top-level "
"directory [\\#11195](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/11195)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:260
msgid ""
"In previous Nix releases, the tarball fetcher (used by "
"`builtins.fetchTarball`) erroneously merged top-level directories into a "
"single directory, and silently discarded top-level files that are not "
"directories. This is no longer the case. The new behaviour is that _only_ if "
"the tarball consists of a single directory, the top-level path component of "
"the files in the tarball is removed (similar to `tar`'s `--strip-"
"components=1`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:264
msgid ""
"Setting to warn about large paths [\\#10778](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/10778)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.24.md:266
msgid ""
"Nix can now warn when evaluation of a Nix expression causes a large path to "
"be copied to the Nix store. The threshold for this warning can be configured "
"using the `warn-large-path-threshold` setting, e.g. `--warn-large-path-"
"threshold 100M`."
msgstr ""

