#: source/release-notes/rl-2.5.md:1
msgid "Release 2.5 (2021-12-13)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.5.md:3
msgid ""
"The garbage collector no longer blocks new builds, so the message `waiting "
"for the big garbage collector lock...` is a thing of the past."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.5.md:7
msgid "Binary cache stores now have a setting `compression-level`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.5.md:9
msgid "`nix develop` now has a flag `--unpack` to run `unpackPhase`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.5.md:11
msgid "Lists can now be compared lexicographically using the `<` operator."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.5.md:13
msgid ""
"New built-in function: `builtins.groupBy`, with the same functionality as "
"Nixpkgs' `lib.groupBy`, but faster."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.5.md:16
msgid "`nix repl` now has a `:log` command."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:1
msgid "Release 2.6 (2022-01-24)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:3
msgid ""
"The Nix CLI now searches for a `flake.nix` up until the root of the current "
"Git repository or a filesystem boundary rather than just in the current "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:6
msgid ""
"The TOML parser used by `builtins.fromTOML` has been replaced by [a more "
"compliant one](https://github.com/ToruNiina/toml11)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:8
msgid ""
"Added `:st`/`:show-trace` commands to `nix repl`, which are used to set or "
"toggle display of error traces."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:10
msgid ""
"New builtin function `builtins.zipAttrsWith` with the same functionality as "
"`lib.zipAttrsWith` from Nixpkgs, but much more efficient."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:13
msgid ""
"New command `nix store copy-log` to copy build logs from one store to "
"another."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:15
msgid ""
"The `commit-lockfile-summary` option can be set to a non-empty string to "
"override the commit summary used when committing an updated lockfile.  This "
"may be used in conjunction with the `nixConfig` attribute in `flake.nix` to "
"better conform to repository conventions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.6.md:20
msgid ""
"`docker run -ti nixos/nix:master` will place you in the Docker container "
"with the latest version of Nix from the `master` branch."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:1
msgid "Release 2.7 (2022-03-07)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:3
msgid ""
"Nix will now make some helpful suggestions when you mistype something on the "
"command line. For instance, if you type `nix build nixpkgs#thunderbrd`, it "
"will suggest `thunderbird`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:7
msgid ""
"A number of \"default\" flake output attributes have been renamed. These are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:10
msgid "`defaultPackage.<system>` → `packages.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:11
msgid "`defaultApps.<system>` → `apps.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:13
msgid "`defaultBundler.<system>` → `bundlers.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:15
msgid "`devShell.<system>` → `devShells.<system>.default`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:17
msgid ""
"The old flake output attributes still work, but `nix flake check` will warn "
"about them."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:20
msgid ""
"Breaking API change: `nix bundle` now supports bundlers of the form `bundler."
"<system>.<name>= derivation: another-derivation;`. This supports additional "
"functionality to inspect evaluation information during bundling. A new "
"[repository](https://github.com/NixOS/bundlers) has various bundlers "
"implemented."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:27
msgid "`nix store ping` now reports the version of the remote Nix daemon."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:29
msgid ""
"`nix flake {init,new}` now display information about which files have been "
"created."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.7.md:32
msgid ""
"Templates can now define a `welcomeText` attribute, which is printed out by "
"`nix flake {init,new} --template <template>`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:1
msgid "Release 2.8 (2022-04-19)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:3
msgid ""
"New experimental command: `nix fmt`, which applies a formatter defined by "
"the `formatter.<system>` flake output to the Nix expressions in a flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:7
msgid ""
"Various Nix commands can now read expressions from standard input using `--"
"file -`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:10
msgid ""
"New experimental builtin function `builtins.fetchClosure` that copies a "
"closure from a binary cache at evaluation time and rewrites it to content-"
"addressed form (if it isn't already). Like `builtins.storePath`, this allows "
"importing pre-built store paths; the difference is that it doesn't require "
"the user to configure binary caches and trusted public keys."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:17
msgid ""
"This function is only available if you enable the experimental feature "
"`fetch-closure`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:20
msgid ""
"New experimental feature: _impure derivations_. These are derivations that "
"can produce a different result every time they're built. Here is an example:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:24
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"stdenv.mkDerivation {\n"
"  name = \"impure\";\n"
"  __impure = true; # marks this derivation as impure\n"
"  buildCommand = \"date > $out\";\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:32
msgid ""
"Running `nix build` twice on this expression will build the derivation "
"twice, producing two different content-addressed store paths. Like fixed-"
"output derivations, impure derivations have access to the network. Only "
"fixed-output derivations and impure derivations can depend on an impure "
"derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:38
msgid ""
"`nix store make-content-addressable` has been renamed to `nix store make-"
"content-addressed`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:41
msgid ""
"The `nixosModule` flake output attribute has been renamed consistent with "
"the `.default` renames in Nix 2.7."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:46
msgid ""
"As before, the old output will continue to work, but `nix flake check` will "
"issue a warning about it."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.8.md:49
msgid ""
"`nix run` is now stricter in what it accepts: members of the `apps` flake "
"output are now required to be apps (as defined in [the manual](https://"
"nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-run.html#apps)), and "
"members of `packages` or `legacyPackages` must be derivations (not apps)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:1
msgid "Release 2.9 (2022-05-30)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:3
msgid ""
"Running Nix with the new `--debugger` flag will cause it to start a repl "
"session if an exception is thrown during evaluation, or if `builtins.break` "
"is called.  From there you can inspect the values of variables and evaluate "
"Nix expressions.  In debug mode, the following new repl commands are "
"available:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:18
msgid "Read more about the debugger [here](https://www.zknotes.com/note/5970)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:21
msgid ""
"Nix now provides better integration with zsh's `run-help` feature. It is now "
"included in the Nix installation in the form of an autoloadable shell "
"function, `run-help-nix`. It picks up Nix subcommands from the currently "
"typed in command and directs the user to the associated man pages."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:27
msgid ""
"`nix repl` has a new build-and-link (`:bl`) command that builds a derivation "
"while creating GC root symlinks."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:30
msgid ""
"The path produced by `builtins.toFile` is now allowed to be imported or read "
"even with restricted evaluation. Note that this will not work with a read-"
"only store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:34
msgid ""
"`nix build` has a new `--print-out-paths` flag to print the resulting output "
"paths.  This matches the default behaviour of `nix-build`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:38
msgid ""
"You can now specify which outputs of a derivation `nix` should operate on "
"using the syntax `installable^outputs`, e.g. `nixpkgs#glibc^dev,static` or "
"`nixpkgs#glibc^*`. By default, `nix` will use the outputs specified by the "
"derivation's `meta.outputsToInstall` attribute if it exists, or all outputs "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.9.md:45
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchTree` (and flake inputs) can now be used to fetch plain files "
"over the `http(s)` and `file` protocols in addition to directory tarballs."
msgstr ""

